or housekeeping gap; the parking branch remains open indefinitely. No governance invariant broken.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a 5th bullet: 'feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking can be deleted once 024B-core + 024B-extras both merge (audit trail intact in git history + r8-archive preserved).'\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-R1-nit-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE specifies an absolute path normalisation test for --restore mode; no such test is present in the test file.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE §scope restore tests: 'absolute path normalisation.' All run_restore_case invocations in test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh use relative path 'pre-state.json'; no case passes an absolute path argument.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Minor coverage fidelity gap vs. DISPATCH-NOTE spec. No functional defect expected (bash/python handle relative and absolute paths uniformly for cat/open).\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add one restore test case passing an absolute path via `$(pwd)/pre-state.json` and asserting exit 0 to satisfy the DISPATCH-NOTE spec literally.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-R1-nit-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Step-7 placeholder file lacks an evidence template; the operator must cross-reference the DISPATCH-NOTE to know what to commit.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md contains only: 'This file is reserved for the operator-interactive step-7 restore round-trip evidence.' No template for: test repo name, before-state JSON, restore-mode invocation log, after-state JSON, byte-for-byte match assertion result.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Minor operator-ergonomics gap; no governance invariant broken. The DISPATCH-NOTE is co-located and describes the required evidence, but the operator must look in two places.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Expand the placeholder with section headers matching the required evidence format: test-repo, pre-state-capture, restore-invocation-command, after-state-GET, match-assertion-result, operator-timestamp.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"63ff13ee-81f1-4f0b-918f-ac552c57e154\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.1542960500000001,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":13,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":118115,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":892626,\"output_tokens\":29439,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":118115,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":16618,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":122151,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3345,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":3345},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1823,\"outputTokens\":26,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0019529999999999999,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":13,\"outputTokens\":29439,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":892626,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":118115,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.1523430499999998,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"af8b816c-15e1-4921-9f84-500815c4c806\"}\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-correctness.json:1:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":655432,\"duration_api_ms\":656075,\"num_turns\":18,\"result\":\"I now have all the information needed to produce the correctness review. Let me compile the findings.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"reviewer_id\\\": \\\"R1-correctness\\\",\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n  \\\"slice\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-extras\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"FAIL\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Seven findings: 1 CRIT, 3 MAJ, 3 MIN. CRIT: the paths-ignore bootstrap guard is incomplete — the 024B-extras PR changes STATUS.md, which matches the workflow paths filter and is NOT excluded by paths-ignore (which only covers 024[AB]*/**). The workflow fires, resolves the 024B-extras DISPATCH-NOTE (cascade-status: not applicable), and exits 2 because --allow-not-applicable is absent from the workflow invocation. This is the exact self-blocking defect R7 claimed to address, persisting because STATUS.md was not considered. Three MAJ defects follow: (1) check_forward_mode_safety applies a client-side jq head_branch == default_branch filter that achieves the same exclusion as the &branch= parameter the dispatch note explicitly prohibited — PR-triggered runs are silently dropped, causing false rejections for cold-start adopters; (2) ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 states '--expected-wrapper-sha is REQUIRED when prior restore evidence exists; omitting it rejects with exit 2' but the guard is gated on the flag being present — the Gate 3 requirement is silently bypassable; (3) three restore+forward-mode mutex test cases are absent (--restore+--plan, --restore+--no-enforce-admins, --restore+--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate). All other major areas check out: GET→PUT transform correct, APPLY_FAIL pattern correct, required_signatures POST/DELETE correct, prior-entry detection guard correct (R8-CORR-002 closed), cascade-status regex clean (R8-CORR-001 closed), --expected-wrapper-sha tag validation correct, ADOPT-001 §12.8 three-gate structure correct.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"CRIT\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Bootstrap defect persists: workflow self-blocks 024B-extras PR via STATUS.md trigger path.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.yml paths filter includes 'STATUS.md'; paths-ignore is 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**'. DISPATCH-NOTE scope lists STATUS.md as an explicit deliverable (aa5be78 commit message confirms). When the PR changes STATUS.md, GitHub evaluates the trigger as: STATUS.md matches paths AND does NOT match paths-ignore → workflow fires. The 'Resolve dispatch note path' step then runs git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD -- 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024*/DISPATCH-NOTE.md' | head -n1, which finds docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md (also changed). DISPATCH-NOTE line 9 declares cascade-status: not applicable. The 'Check invocation log entry' step invokes check-invocation-log-entry.sh without --allow-not-applicable, so the script exits 2 with 'ERROR: cascade-status: not applicable found, but --allow-not-applicable was not passed.' CI fails.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"024B-extras cannot achieve the CI-green acceptance criterion through its own gate. The introducing PR self-blocks — the same class as R7 bootstrap defect, now via the STATUS.md path rather than the DISPATCH-NOTE path.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Either (a) in the 'Check invocation log entry' step, detect cascade-status: not applicable in the resolved dispatch note and exit 0 (tooling-slice short-circuit), or (b) restrict the dispatch note glob in the resolution step to '024[C-Z]*/DISPATCH-NOTE.md' so tooling DISPATCH-NOTEs are never found, and exit 0 when the glob returns empty. Option (b) is narrower and avoids adding --allow-not-applicable to the workflow (which would permit cohort slices to bypass by embedding a tooling DISPATCH-NOTE).\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"check_forward_mode_safety client-side jq filter reinstates the excluded &branch= parameter, silently dropping PR-triggered runs from the safety check count.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Line 464: gh api '...runs?workflow_id=${workflow_id}&status=success&created>=${created_since}' — correct, no &branch=. Line 465: jq '.workflow_runs | map(select(.head_branch == $default_branch)) | length'. For a PR-triggered run, head_branch is the source branch (e.g. feature/pim-adopt), not main. select(.head_branch == $default_branch) excludes all such runs. This is arithmetically equivalent to ?&branch=main. DISPATCH-NOTE explicitly states: 'NO &branch= filter on workflow-runs API (PR-triggered runs have head-branch = feature branch, not default; branch filter defeats gate).' The implementation defeats the gate via the client-side path. Fake-gh fixtures all use head_branch:'main', so the test suite does not expose this.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Forward-mode invocation against a newly onboarded adopter whose only recent successful runs are PR-triggered (typical cold-start) fails with 'no successful workflow runs found' even though the wrapper is demonstrably functional. The --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci bypass is needed every time, defeating the gate's safety purpose.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Remove the select(.head_branch == ...) jq filter entirely: run_count=$(... | jq '.workflow_runs | length'). The window is already bounded by ?status=success&created>=${created_since}, so counting all successful runs regardless of head_branch satisfies the DISPATCH-NOTE spec. Add a test fixture with head_branch:'feature/pim-adopt' to expose the bug in regression.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Gate 3 enforcement gap: --expected-wrapper-sha is not required when prior restore evidence exists, contradicting ADOPT-001 §12.8's stated contract.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3: 'If the flag is omitted, re-enable is rejected with exit 2.' Implementation (lines 472-483): the prior_restore_evidence_present() check only executes inside if [ -n \\\\\\\"$EXPECTED_WRAPPER_SHA\\\\\\\" ]. If the operator runs forward-mode without --expected-wrapper-sha after completing Gate 1, the outer guard short-circuits to noop — no error, no exit 2. Gate 3 is thus advisory (documentation-enforced only) rather than code-enforced. No test case exercises the path where restore evidence IS present and --expected-wrapper-sha IS absent.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator who completes Gate 1 (restore) and then mistakenly re-enables via plain forward-mode (without --expected-wrapper-sha) bypasses Gate 3 entirely. The re-enable may run against a wrapper still pinned to the defective SCP SHA, re-arming the broken gate. The audit log does not record a Gate-3 bypass because no mechanism fires.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Before the existing --expected-wrapper-sha guard, unconditionally check prior_restore_evidence_present. If evidence is found AND --expected-wrapper-sha is absent, emit an error and exit 2. This enforces the contract stated in ADOPT-001 §12.8 in code rather than only in documentation.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-004\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Three --restore + forward-mode flag mutex test cases are absent from the test suite despite being explicitly required by the DISPATCH-NOTE acceptance criteria.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"DISPATCH-NOTE AC: 'Tests: --restore + forward-mode-flag incompatibility (--no-enforce-admins, --plan, --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate, --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci).' The enable-sha-mutex test (line 2078) covers the --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci pair. No test case invokes run_restore_case with --plan (guards at line 224), --no-enforce-admins (guard at line 228), or --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate (guard at line 232). The implementation logic for these guards is present and appears correct, but the guards have no test coverage.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A regression removing any of the three guards would not be caught by the test suite. The guards are the only enforcement against operators accidentally combining restore-mode with contradictory forward-mode flags.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add three run_restore_case test cases: (a) --plan → expected exit 2, stderr contains 'cannot be combined with --plan'; (b) --no-enforce-admins → expected exit 2, stderr contains 'cannot be combined with --no-enforce-admins'; (c) --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate → expected exit 2, stderr contains 'cannot be combined with --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate'.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-005\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"D-047 rationale omits explicit naming of the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification escape hatch flag, violating R8-SAFE-001 mitigation requirement.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"R8-SAFE-001 mitigation (DISPATCH-NOTE §Carry-forward): 'WARNING + CAUTION callouts in ADOPT-001 §12.8 + log-block CAUTION line + D-047 rationale acknowledging escape hatch.' DECISIONS.md D-047 row (line 93) names ADOPT-001 §12.8, restore mode, and CI wiring but never names the --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification flag by string in the decision rationale. ADOPT-001 §12.8 WARNING/CAUTION callouts are present and correct; the code emits the CAUTION log line (line 475-476); but D-047 itself is the governance anchor for the escape hatch and should document it explicitly.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Future review of D-047 will not surface the escape hatch's existence or its trust-model implications without cross-referencing ADOPT-001 §12.8 separately. The R8-SAFE-001 closure is technically incomplete at the decision-record level.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add one sentence to D-047 rationale naming --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification as the emergency Gate-2 bypass and stating that its use is logged in the audit trail per R8-SAFE-001.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-006\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags fetches only 100 tags without Link-header pagination, silently missing tags beyond the first 100.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Line 423: gh api 'repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags?per_page=100'. GitHub paginates at per_page=100; if >100 tags exist, subsequent pages are never fetched. The jq pipeline on line 431 processes only the single-page response. The SCP repo currently has far fewer than 100 release tags, so this does not fail today.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Once the SCP repo accumulates more than 100 release tags, validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags may report 'SHA not found in release-tag cache' for valid tags beyond page 1, blocking Gate 3 re-enable with a false negative.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Replace the single API call with a paginated loop using the gh --paginate flag or --header 'Link' parsing, or limit validation to recent tags only (e.g. refs starting with 'v' sorted by creation date, last 100). Nit-level urgency today but worth filing as a tracked-forward item before the estate reaches 100 releases.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-007\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"No test exercises the working-tree-only restore evidence path in prior_restore_evidence_present (R8-SAFE-002 mitigation).\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"R8-SAFE-002 mitigation: 'also check working-tree diff via git diff HEAD branch-protection-log.md.' The enable-expected-sha test (line 1945) has restore evidence in both HEAD (committed at line 2007) AND the working tree (appended via printf at lines 2008-2022). There is no test where restore evidence is ONLY in the working tree (not yet committed). The git diff HEAD path in prior_restore_evidence_present (line 409) would catch this case in production, but it is never the sole path exercised by any test.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A regression that breaks the working-tree diff component of prior_restore_evidence_present (e.g. a path quoting bug) would not be caught. The committed-log path would still pass all existing tests.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a test case for enable-expected-sha-wt-only: commit the log WITHOUT restore evidence, then append restore evidence to the working tree (printf >> log), run run_enable_case with --expected-wrapper-sha <valid-sha>, expect exit 0. This isolates the git diff HEAD path.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"0eb1f737-21a1-4304-994a-ff982e77e5ad\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.4023415999999997,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":11,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":148740,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":842552,\"output_tokens\":39326,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":148740,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":21645,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":154213,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1908,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1908},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1753,\"outputTokens\":25,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.001878,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":11,\"outputTokens\":39326,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":842552,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":148740,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.4004636000000001,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"487e026e-dd7e-449b-ac98-0aadfdf1e36e\"}\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/r1-safety_bypass.json:1:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":725242,\"duration_api_ms\":725718,\"num_turns\":17,\"result\":\"I now have enough information to produce the structured findings report.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"review_id\\\": \\\"R1-SAFETY_BYPASS-024B-EXTRAS-2026-05-10\\\",\\n  \\\"slice\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-extras\\\",\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"SAFETY_BYPASS\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"NOT_FIXPOINT\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Four MAJ and four MIN/nit findings; no CRIT. Every defect produces some observable signal, but two MAJ findings allow API mutations to succeed despite guards being circumvented. SAFE-MAJ-001: Forward-mode jq post-filter (head_branch == default_branch) is functionally identical to the prohibited API ?branch= filter. The canonical wrapper (pull_request trigger only, confirmed via templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl) never produces head_branch=main runs; the safety gate is permanently useless for normal adopters, training routine bypass-flag usage. SAFE-MAJ-002: restore pre-state JSON with enforce_admins: {enabled: 0} bypasses the ACK guard (jq // treats integer 0 as non-null/non-false; bash '0' != 'false') while Python bool(0)=False silently applies enforce_admins=false via PUT; verification failure fires after the mutation. SAFE-MAJ-003: prior_restore_evidence_present's second return-0 block (grep 'Restoring TO:') is target-agnostic; a Gate-1 entry for adopter A satisfies Gate-3's Gate-1 prerequisite for any other target, collapsing per-adopter gate integrity. SAFE-MAJ-004: CI bootstrap defect incompletely closed: paths-ignore covers 024[AB]*/** but STATUS.md is an unconditional paths trigger; a tooling slice modifying STATUS.md triggers the workflow against the tooling DISPATCH-NOTE (cascade-status: not applicable), FAIL-CLOSED exit 2 blocks the introducing PR. SAFE-MIN-001: no ACK for required_pull_request_reviews=null on restore. SAFE-MIN-002: tag validation capped at per_page=100, causing false-negative for repos with >100 release tags. SAFE-MIN-003: forward-mode required_signatures POST lacks the 404-suppression present in restore mode. SAFE-NIT-001: hardcoded SCP repo name in tag validation.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MAJ-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Forward-mode jq post-filter select(.head_branch == $default_branch) is functionally identical to the ?branch= API filter the DISPATCH-NOTE explicitly prohibits, making the prior-green-CI safety gate permanently useless for PR-only wrapper adopters.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:465 applies jq 'map(select(.head_branch == $default_branch))' after the API call. Canonical wrapper (templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl:5-7) only has pull_request trigger; PR-triggered runs have head_branch = source branch, never default branch. run_count is always 0 for normal adopters. Fake_gh guard (test:262-265) correctly rejects ?branch= in API endpoint but does not catch the equivalent jq post-filter exclusion.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Every adopter with a PR-only wrapper appears as 'no prior green CI'; operators must routinely pass --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci as the default, defeating the gate entirely. D-047 claim that forward-mode safety check uses 'no branch filter' is misleading; the post-filter achieves identical exclusion of PR-triggered runs.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Remove the jq head_branch filter or replace with '.workflow_runs | length' (count all successful runs without branch filtering). The existing fake_gh API guard is correct and sufficient for the no-API-branch-filter requirement.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MAJ-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"restore pre-state JSON with enforce_admins: {enabled: 0} (integer zero) bypasses the posture-degradation ACK guard while Python bool(0)=False causes the PUT to apply enforce_admins=false without --i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:624: jq '.enforce_admins.enabled // false' with integer 0 returns '0' (jq // only substitutes for null/boolean-false; 0 is neither). Bash '0' == 'false' is false → ACK not required. Python transform line 358: bool(0)=False → PUT body has enforce_admins: false. Verification then compares 'false' vs '0', sets FAIL=1 and exits 1, but the API state is already mutated.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator crafting or receiving a pre-state JSON with enabled: 0 instead of false disables admin enforcement without the required ACK. Script exits 1 (verification failure) but branch protection is already degraded. D-047 trust-model claim of posture-degradation completeness is inaccurate pending this fix.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Use RESTORE_PAYLOAD (transformed, already bool-coerced) for degradation checks instead of raw RESTORE_TARGET_JSON. Or extend bash check: jq '(.enforce_admins.enabled // false) | not' to correctly handle integers, nulls, and booleans uniformly.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MAJ-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"prior_restore_evidence_present's second return-0 condition (grep 'Restoring TO:') is target-agnostic; a Gate-1 log entry for any adopter satisfies the Gate-3 Gate-1 prerequisite for any other target repo.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:413-417 — second if-block: 'printf committed+diff | grep -Fq \\\\\\\"Restoring TO:\\\\\\\"' with no $target guard. If branch-protection-log.md contains any prior restore entry ('Restoring TO:') for adopter A, running Gate 3 for adopter B passes the prerequisite check without a B-specific Gate 1. Test (line 1945) only exercises same-target path; no cross-target negative test exists.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Operator who completed Gate 1 for adopter A can execute Gate 3 for adopter B without a Gate-1 for B, bypassing sequential 3-gate playbook integrity. Manually committing a line containing 'Restoring TO:' also fakes Gate-1 evidence for all future targets.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Require both target string and 'Restoring TO:' to co-occur in the same log entry. Replace the second return-0 block with a compound check that requires both $target AND 'Restoring TO:' in close proximity, or merge the two conditions into one.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MAJ-004\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"CI bootstrap defect incompletely fixed: paths-ignore 024[AB]*/** excludes tooling DISPATCH-NOTE paths but STATUS.md is an unconditional paths trigger, so a tooling slice modifying STATUS.md triggers the workflow against the tooling DISPATCH-NOTE and FAIL-CLOSED blocks the introducing PR.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\".github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:17-21 — paths includes 'STATUS.md' with no corresponding paths-ignore entry. STATUS.md update is a listed 024B-extras deliverable. When triggered, the dispatch-note resolution step finds the 024B-extras DISPATCH-NOTE (cascade-status: not applicable); check-invocation-log-entry.sh exits 2 without --allow-not-applicable.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"The 024B-extras PR is blocked by the workflow it introduces whenever STATUS.md is committed. D-047 trust-model claim of 'bootstrap path-filter closes introducing slice bootstrap defect' is inaccurate. Same issue applies to any future tooling slice (024G) modifying STATUS.md or branch-protection-log.md.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add STATUS.md and docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md to paths-ignore for 024[AB] slices, OR add an early-exit in the workflow when the resolved DISPATCH-NOTE has slice-type: tooling, OR pass --allow-not-applicable --tooling-slice-id derived from the DISPATCH-NOTE path.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"No posture-degradation ACK is required when restore pre-state has required_pull_request_reviews: null, potentially silently removing PR review requirements added by the adopter after the initial enable-required-check.sh invocation.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:624-633 — posture-degradation guards cover only enforce_admins.enabled=false and empty required_status_checks.contexts. required_pull_request_reviews: null in before-JSON passes the type check (line 339, dict|None allowed) and is included verbatim in the PUT body without any ACK flag.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Hardening gap: an adopter who added PR review requirements post-onboarding loses them silently during a break-glass restore. DISPATCH-NOTE acceptance criteria only names two ACK flags; this is within spec but represents an uncovered posture-degradation path.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Compare RESTORE_TARGET_JSON.required_pull_request_reviews vs BEFORE_JSON.required_pull_request_reviews at restore time; if target is null and current state is non-null, emit a WARNING and optionally require a third ACK flag.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MIN-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags fetches only the first 100 tags (per_page=100); valid release-tag SHAs beyond page 1 report as 'not found in release-tag SHA cache', false-blocking Gate 3.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:423 — 'gh api repos/.../git/refs/tags?per_page=100' with no pagination loop. If the SCP repo accumulates >100 release tags, a valid SHA on a later page causes exit 2 on --expected-wrapper-sha, forcing --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"False-negative gate failure (stricter, not weaker). Operator cannot use Gate 3 for a valid tag without the emergency escape hatch, undermining the rollback SLO. Becomes practically relevant as the tag count grows past 100.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add pagination loop (follow Link header) or document the 100-tag ceiling as a hard constraint in usage text. Alternatively, limit the search to the N most-recent tags with a documented cutoff.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-MIN-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Forward-mode required_signatures POST is missing the 404-suppression handling present in restore mode, causing spurious APPLY_FAIL=1 and exit 1 when signatures are already enabled on the target repo.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:687 — forward mode: 'gh api -X POST .../required_signatures >/dev/null || APPLY_FAIL=1' with no 404 handling. Restore mode (lines 647-656) captures stderr and suppresses 404 with 'already in desired state' log. Test restore-post-404 (line 1896) covers restore path; no equivalent forward-mode test exists.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An adopter with required_signatures pre-enabled sees APPLY_FAIL=1 and exit 1 despite branch protection being correctly set. Creates a confusing false-failure; operator may incorrectly conclude the apply failed and retry, polluting the audit log.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Apply the same 404-suppression pattern as restore mode: capture gh POST stderr to a temp file, grep for '404', suppress with log message. Reuse the pattern from lines 647-656 verbatim.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SAFE-NIT-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags hardcodes 'jrnb2024/standards-control-plane' as the SCP repo path; breaks if the SCP repo is forked, renamed, or operated under a different owner.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh:423,426 — literal 'repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/' in both git/refs/tags listing and per-tag ref resolution calls. No env var override or git remote derivation.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If SCP is forked or operated under a different org, all --expected-wrapper-sha invocations fail with tag-not-found errors. Zero test coverage for non-canonical repo paths.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Replace literal with SCP_REPO=${SCP_REPO:-jrnb2024/standards-control-plane} resolved once at script top. Preserves current behavior while allowing fork deployments to override.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"c243b213-20ab-4743-9378-ce261044a917\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.3160887000000001,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":11,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":121712,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":553989,\"output_tokens\":46108,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":121712,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":8107,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":128613,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":480,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":480},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":1669,\"outputTokens\":30,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0018189999999999999,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":11,\"outputTokens\":46108,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":553989,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":121712,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.3142697,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"4d2d9a12-7c20-4bce-8b85-3b0aec15d683\"}\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:1:# WP-SCP-024 024B-extras — CI wiring for the invocation-log gate.\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:2:#\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:3:# D-047 ratifies the break-glass restore flow and this workflow wiring.\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:4:# Plan-doc invariant 2 still governs the enforcement script itself;\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:5:# this workflow just feeds it the correct slice-local arguments.\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:6:#\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:7:# Critical bootstrap guard: paths-ignore excludes 024A / 024B-*\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:8:# tooling slices so the workflow does not self-trigger on the slice\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:9:# that introduced it.\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:10:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:11:name: check-invocation-log-entry\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:12:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:13:\"on\":\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:14:  pull_request:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:15:    branches: [main]\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:16:    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened]\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:17:    paths:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:18:      - \"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**\"\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:19:      - \"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md\"\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:20:      - \"STATUS.md\"\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:21:    paths-ignore: [\"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**\"]\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:22:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:23:permissions:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:24:  contents: read\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:25:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:26:jobs:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:27:  check-invocation-log-entry:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:28:    runs-on: ubuntu-24.04\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:29:    steps:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:30:      - name: Checkout repository\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:31:        uses: actions/checkout@de0fac2e4500dabe0009e67214ff5f5447ce83dd # v6.0.2\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:32:        with:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:33:          fetch-depth: 0\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:34:          persist-credentials: false\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:35:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:36:      - name: Resolve dispatch note path\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:37:        shell: bash\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:38:        run: |\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:39:          set -euo pipefail\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:40:          dispatch_note=\"$(git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD -- 'docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024*/DISPATCH-NOTE.md' | head -n1)\"\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:41:          if [ -z \"$dispatch_note\" ]; then\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:42:            echo \"error: could not resolve a dispatch note path from the PR diff\" >&2\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:43:            exit 1\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:44:          fi\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:45:          printf 'dispatch_note=%s\\n' \"$dispatch_note\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:46:\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:47:      - name: Check invocation log entry\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:48:        shell: bash\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:49:        run: |\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:50:          set -euo pipefail\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:51:          scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh \\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:52:            --diff-base origin/main \\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:53:            --dispatch-note \"$dispatch_note\" \\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:54:            --status-md STATUS.md \\\n.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml:55:            --branch-protection-log docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:1:# DISPATCH-NOTE — WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-extras\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:2:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:3:**Date:** 2026-05-10\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:4:**Branch:** `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras` (off main, after 024B-core merges)\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:5:**Predecessor:** WP-SCP-024 024B-core (merged at 249aa9f). Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking`. Split per `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-core/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2026-05-09.md`.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:6:**Successor target:** WP-SCP-024 024C PIM canary cascade.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:7:**Decision filed:** D-047.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:8:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:9:`cascade-status: not applicable` — this slice ships rollback + break-glass + CI wiring; not a cohort cascade slice.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:10:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:11:## Backstory\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:12:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:13:024B-core merged at 249aa9f shipped scaffolder + adopter wrapper template + cascade-status CI enforcement script (CLI) + tests. This slice (024B-extras) ships the deferred deliverables.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:14:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:15:Carry-forward findings from extras-parking R8-archive (preserved in `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking`):\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:16:- **R8-CORR-001** (extras-parking): cascade-status regex first-match captures trailing inline prose. **CLOSED in 024B-core** via single-pass regex with full-value capture + closed-set validation.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:17:- **R8-CORR-002** (extras-parking): prior-entry detection runs outside restore-mode guard, emitting spurious contradiction message. **APPLIES TO 024B-EXTRAS** — ensure restore-mode guard scoping is tight.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:18:- **R8-CORR-003** (extras-parking): TF-ticket match pattern parameterises over canonicalised slug instead of plan-doc §2 invariant 2 literal regex. **CLOSED in 024B-core** (slug canonicalisation now spec-compliant).\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:19:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:20:## Why\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:21:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:22:024B-core delivered the WHAT (scaffolder + template + CI script + tests). This slice delivers the HOW (rollback + break-glass + CI integration):\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:23:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:24:1. **`enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode** proves invariant 7's <30-min rollback SLO is real, not aspirational. Operator-interactive demo at step 7 is merge-blocking AC and is recorded through the placeholder evidence path until the operator completes the real-repo round-trip.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:25:2. **ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure** documents the 3-gate playbook for federation-primitive failure recovery.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:26:3. **`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`** wires the CLI script (shipped in 024B-core) into GitHub Actions so cohort cascade slices 024C–F have automated CI enforcement.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:27:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:28:Without 024B-extras, 024C cannot open. Plan-doc §6 cohort dispatcher precondition: 024C entry gates on BOTH 024B-core + 024B-extras merging + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closure.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:29:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:30:## Scope (in)\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:31:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:32:| Deliverable | Path | Notes |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:33:|---|---|---|\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:34:| `enable-required-check.sh --restore` mode | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (modify) | New `--restore <pre-state.json>` flag reverses prior branch-protection mutation per plan-doc invariant 7. Existing forward-mode unchanged. **Key behaviours per extras-parking lessons:** (a) GET-shape JSON transformed to PUT-shape via Python helper (strips `_links`, `url`, `checks`, `required_signatures`); (b) `required_signatures` reset via dedicated DELETE/POST sub-resource calls; (c) APPLY_FAIL=0 wrap pattern (failed PUT continues to log emission); (d) posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement` + `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks` required when before-state has `enforce_admins.enabled=false` or empty `required_status_checks.contexts`; (e) restore log block captures actual pre-restore state via `gh api -X GET` BEFORE PUT (not just the target good-state). |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:35:| Forward-mode safety check | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (modify) | Refuses forward-mode invocation against repo with no successful `policy-check` workflow run on default branch in last 60 days. **Critical (R8 + R9 lessons):** workflow lookup by `path == \".github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml\"` (NOT by display name); query workflow-runs API WITHOUT `&branch=` filter (PR-triggered runs have head-branch = feature branch, not default; branch filter defeats gate). `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag for cold-start. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:36:| `--expected-wrapper-sha` flag | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (modify) | Validates supplied SHA against actual git tags via `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/ref/tags/<tag>` (NOT just 40-char shape match). Used by Gate 3 of break-glass. **Mutex with `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci`** (R7 SAFE-MAJ-001 closure). |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:37:| ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure | `docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md` (modify) | New §12.8 (between §12.7.15 and §13). 3-gate playbook: Gate 1 (DISABLE via `--restore` capturing pre-break SHA); Gate 2 (FIX via SHA-pin to last known-good release tag — concrete `gh api .../tags/<tag>` resolution; NOT illustrative); Gate 3 (RE-ENABLE via Renovate-bumped fix release + `--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha>` REQUIRED — not optional/advisory). SLO <30 min from operator decision to merge-restored state. WARNING + CAUTION callouts for `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` escape hatch. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:38:| `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` | NEW file | CI workflow wiring for the CLI script (shipped in 024B-core). Triggers on `pull_request: [opened, synchronize, reopened]` against main with path filter targeting `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` + `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` + `STATUS.md`. **paths-ignore: `['docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**']`** to exclude tooling slices (024A plan-doc, 024B-core, 024B-extras themselves) — closes the bootstrap defect from extras-parking R7. SHA-pinned actions (per D-038 supply-chain hardening). Single job invokes `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh --diff-base origin/main --dispatch-note <found> --status-md STATUS.md --branch-protection-log docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`. Required-status-check eligible. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:39:| `--restore` mode tests | `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` (modify) | Add `run_restore_case` + `make_restore_fake_gh` helpers (mirrors extras-parking patterns). Tests: GET→PUT shape transform; APPLY_FAIL pattern (failed PUT still emits log); posture-degradation flag enforcement; `required_signatures` POST + DELETE sub-resource handling; absolute path normalisation; --expected-wrapper-sha tag-validation (release-tag SHA → exit 0; arbitrary SHA → exit 2); --restore + forward-mode-flag incompatibility (--no-enforce-admins, --plan, --i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate, --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci). |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:40:| D-047 row | `docs/DECISIONS.md` | New decision ratifying --restore mode operational contract + ADOPT-001 §12.8 break-glass procedure + CI workflow wiring. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:41:| STATUS.md update | `STATUS.md` | \"Today's chain (2026-05-10 — slice 024B-extras)\" entry. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:42:| **Step 7 operator-interactive demo evidence** | `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md` | **MERGE-BLOCKING.** Operator-interactive after R-fixpoint reached. Real-repo round-trip on throw-away test repo: create test repo → invoke `enable-required-check.sh` forward-mode → capture pre-state → invoke `--restore` mode → verify branch-protection API response matches captured before-state byte-for-byte → commit evidence. NOT a dry-run mock. The placeholder path is the handoff target until the operator completes the demo. Closes plan-doc invariant 7 SLO + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:43:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:44:## Scope (out)\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:45:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:46:- 024C PIM cascade kickoff. Unblocked when this slice merges + FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closes.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:47:- TF-023E-002 closure. Carry-forward.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:48:- D-021 May-31 atomic-workday filing. Independent track.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:49:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:50:## Carry-forward known findings (from extras-parking r8-archive)\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:51:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:52:These were surfaced in extras-parking R8 but not closed at parking time. Address proactively in this slice:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:53:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:54:1. **R8-SAFE-001** (extras-parking): `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` is a backdoor; D-044 trust-model claim 'Gate 2 wrapper-SHA pin is explicit operator consent' becomes inaccurate when bypassed. Mitigation: WARNING + CAUTION callouts in ADOPT-001 §12.8 + log-block CAUTION line + D-047 rationale acknowledging escape hatch.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:55:2. **R8-SAFE-002** (extras-parking): Gate 3 forward-mode prior-en