orkflow wiring + tests + D-047 + STATUS | Codex T3 | ~45 min |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:90:| 2 | Manual scope check + verify-commands | Opus | ~5 min |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:91:| 3 | 3× sequential Sonnet R1 review (64k cap) | Sonnet | ~30 min |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:92:| 4 | Fix-rounds (expected 1-2 given carry-forward findings pre-addressed) | Codex + Sonnet | variable |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:93:| 5 | **Operator-interactive `--restore` real-repo round-trip demo** | Operator interactive (gh PAT, throw-away test repo) | ~15 min |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:94:| 6 | Final R-fixpoint + self-merge | Opus | ~10 min |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:95:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:96:Target: 024B-extras merged within ~3-4 hours wall-clock + operator demo gating window.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:97:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:98:## Reservation guard\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:99:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:100:D-047 reserved for this slice. Codex must NOT assign D-047 to anything else.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:101:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:102:---\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:103:\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:104:**Status:** ACTIVE (post-024B-core merge). Awaiting operator-interactive step-7 evidence completion and R-fixpoint review.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:1:# SCP Federation Primitive — Versioning Contract\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:2:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:3:**Status:** active as of slice 020H.1 (2026-05-01).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:4:**Closes:** WP-SCP-020 §4 020H.1 sub-criteria (i) + (ii).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:5:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:6:---\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:7:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:8:## Scope\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:9:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:10:This document defines the semver contract that the SCP federation\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:11:primitive guarantees to adopters who pin a `# tag: v<X>.<Y>.<Z>`\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:12:wrapper at `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml`. It covers three\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:13:public surfaces:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:14:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:15:1. **Reusable workflow inputs** — `workflow_call.inputs` declared on\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:16:   `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml`.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:17:2. **Schema contracts** — JSON Schema at\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:18:   `schemas/policy-check-summary.schema.json` (the structured\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:19:   summary artefact every adopter consumes for nightly + release-gate\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:20:   reconciliation), `schemas/rule-config.schema.json`, and\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:21:   `schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` (the opt-in cross-repo\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:22:   scorecard emit per WP-SCP-023 023B / D-041 — added at v1.2.0;\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:23:   MAJOR-pinned per WP-SCP-023 plan-doc §10 Q1).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:24:3. **Rule IDs** — the `SCP-R-NNN` identifiers under `policies/`.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:25:4. **Opt-in workflow inputs** — `scorecard-emit: bool` (added at\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:26:   v1.2.0 per WP-SCP-023 023B; default false). Opt-in inputs follow\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:27:   the same MINOR/MAJOR semver category as core inputs.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:28:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:29:It does NOT cover internal-only surfaces: `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh`,\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:30:`scripts/scp-policy-check.lock`, helper scripts in `scripts/`, the\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:31:Renovate preset internal shape, the OPA Rego `scp_common.rego`\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:32:helpers, or the SCP-self cross-repo aggregator pipeline\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:33:(`.github/workflows/scorecard-aggregator.yml`,\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:34:`schemas/scorecard-opt-in-registry.schema.json`,\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:35:`schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`,\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:36:`docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml`,\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:37:`output/scorecards/index.json` — added in slice 023C / D-042; mirrors\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:38:`.github/workflows/conflict-gate.yml` posture per slice 020N).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:39:These are refactored without notice.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:40:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:41:---\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:42:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:43:## Semver guarantee\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:44:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:45:**`MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`** with strict semantic-versioning meaning:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:46:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:47:| Bump | When | Adopter action required |\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:48:|---|---|---|\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:49:| **PATCH** (`v1.0.x`) | Bug fixes, new informational annotations, performance improvements, observability records, internal refactors of helpers/lib. | None — drop in the SHA bump and merge. |\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:50:| **MINOR** (`v1.x.0`) | New `workflow_call` inputs (with safe defaults), new `SCP-R-NNN` rules added with `threshold: warn` baseline, new optional schema fields, new commit-status contexts (informational), new `disabled_rules:` reasons. | Recommended: review the release notes for new rules. None mandatory unless the adopter wants to opt into a new rule's `threshold: deny`. |\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:51:| **MAJOR** (`vX.0.0`) | Breaking changes — see \"What is breaking\" below. | **Mandatory** — read the migration guide in the release notes; an amending decision row in adopter's `DECISIONS.md` (or equivalent) before bumping the SHA pin. |\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:52:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:53:---\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:54:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:55:## What counts as a breaking change\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:56:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:57:Any of the following requires a MAJOR bump and an amending decision row:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:58:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:59:### Workflow inputs\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:60:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:61:- Removing a `workflow_call.inputs.<name>`.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:62:- Renaming a `workflow_call.inputs.<name>`.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:63:- Changing the `default:` value of an input in a way that flips an existing adopter's effective behaviour (e.g. `threshold: warn` → `threshold: deny`).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:64:- Changing the `type:` of an input.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:65:- Making a previously-optional input required.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:66:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:67:### Schema contracts\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:68:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:69:- Removing a previously-required field from `policy-check-summary.schema.json` or `rule-config.schema.json`.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:70:- Renaming any field (use add-new-then-deprecate instead).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:71:- Tightening a string `pattern:` such that previously-valid values are rejected.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:72:- Tightening a `format:` constraint (e.g. `date` → `date-time`).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:73:- Adding a new required field (covered by the deprecation ramp — see below).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:74:- Removing an `enum:` value that was previously emitted.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:75:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:76:### Rule IDs\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:77:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:78:- Removing an `SCP-R-NNN` rule.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:79:- Re-numbering an `SCP-R-NNN` rule (the ID is the durable contract; the underlying logic is internal).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:80:- Promoting a rule from `threshold: warn` to `threshold: deny` as the **default** at the SCP source. (Adopters may always override per-rule via `.scp/rule-config.yaml`; the default flip is what's breaking.)\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:81:- Tightening a rule's match scope such that previously-passing manifests now deny.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:82:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:83:### Read-back / annotation contracts\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:84:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:85:- Removing `scp/policy-check-readback` commit-status posting.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:86:- Removing a `::warning::` or `::error::` annotation surface that adopters' downstream tooling parses (e.g. an annotation parser that grouped on `title=SCP-E001`).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:87:- Renaming an `SCP-ENNN` error-code identifier.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:88:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:89:### Branch-protection helper\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:90:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:91:- Removing `--repo`, `--branch`, `--plan`, `--no-enforce-admins`, or `--i-understand-this-bypasses-the-gate` flags from `scripts/enable-required-check.sh`.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:92:- Changing the script's invocation-log markdown block schema.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:93:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:94:### Tag protection\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:95:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:96:- Changing the `v*` or `renovate/v*` Repository Ruleset shape (deletion / non-fast-forward / update behaviour).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:97:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:98:---\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:99:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:100:## What does NOT count as breaking\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:101:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:102:- Adding new `workflow_call.inputs.<name>` with a safe default.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:103:- Adding new `SCP-R-NNN` rules at `threshold: warn` baseline.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:104:- Adding new schema fields (`additionalProperties: false` is preserved — but new fields are added under existing properties, not as required new top-level fields).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:105:- Adding new `enum:` values that were not previously emitted.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:106:- Adding new `disabled_rules:` reasons.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:107:- Adding new informational `::warning::` or `::error::` titles (if existing titles preserved).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:108:- Internal helper-library refactors.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:109:- New commit-status contexts (the existing two are stable).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:110:- New OPA / Conftest / Regal binary version bumps in the lockfile (these are SHA-pinned; adopters get the new pins via Renovate auto-bump).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:111:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:112:---\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:113:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:114:## Deprecation ramp (one-release warning window)\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:115:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:116:**Closes 020H.1 sub-criterion (ii); enforced by 020H.3 release-gate.**\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:117:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:118:When the SCP source needs to remove or breaking-change one of the\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:119:public surfaces above, the change MUST proceed via a **one-release\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:120:deprecation ramp**:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:121:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:122:1. **Release N: add the new surface** (alongside the old surface), and\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:123:   in the same release add a `::warning::` annotation to the old\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:124:   surface stating: `<surface> deprecated; use <new-surface>; will be\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:125:   removed in v<X+1>.0.0`. Document in release notes. **Add an entry\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:126:   to `policies/deprecations.yaml`** with `announced_at`,\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:127:   `announced_release`, `target_release`, and `migration_pointer`\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:128:   (per `schemas/deprecations.schema.json`).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:129:2. **Release N+1 (the next MINOR or MAJOR — whichever lands first):**\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:130:   keep both surfaces live; the warning continues to fire.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:131:3. **Release N+M (the MAJOR after the next MINOR):** old surface is\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:132:   removed; the MAJOR bump is the breaking-change vehicle. An amending\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:133:   decision row in `docs/DECISIONS.md` records the removal. **Remove\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:134:   the entry from `policies/deprecations.yaml`** as part of the\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:135:   removal commit.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:136:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:137:The minimum gap between deprecation announcement (step 1) and\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:138:removal (step 3) is **one MINOR release**. Adopters who track every\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:139:MINOR release see at least one full PR cycle's worth of warnings\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:140:before the surface vanishes.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:141:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:142:**Machine enforcement** — two operating modes per `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml`:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:143:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:144:1. **Dry-run pre-flight (workflow_dispatch).** The pre-emptive\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:145:   enforcement path. The operator runs the gate BEFORE pushing the\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:146:   tag:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:147:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:148:   ```bash\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:149:   gh workflow run release-gate.yml -f dry_run_tag=v1.1.0\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:150:   # Wait for the run to start, then watch for completion + non-zero\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:151:   # exit on failure (gh run list always exits 0; gh run watch with\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:152:   # --exit-status surfaces the workflow's verdict). Closes 020H.3 R2\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:153:   # nit-SAFE-001.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:154:   sleep 5  # allow the dispatch to register\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:155:   RUN_ID=\"$(gh run list --workflow=release-gate.yml --limit 1 --json databaseId --jq '.[0].databaseId')\"\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:156:   gh run watch \"${RUN_ID}\" --exit-status\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:157:   ```\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:158:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:159:   If the dry-run exits clean, the tag is safe to push. **The\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:160:   dry-run pre-flight is mandatory before every v* tag-cut.**\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:161:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:162:2. **Post-tag observer (`push: tags: ['v*']`).** GitHub Actions\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:163:   cannot block a `push: tags` event — by the time the workflow\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:164:   fires, the tag already exists on the remote. This trigger\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:165:   therefore acts as a last-line-of-defense observer: it annotates\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:166:   the bad tag with `SCP-EREL-001` AND opens a\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:167:   `release-gate-violation` GitHub issue auto-assigned to `@jrnb2024`\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:168:   for triage (per slice 020H.3.1 closure of TF-020H3rg-003 —\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:169:   `permissions: { issues: write }` on the workflow + de-dup by tag,\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:170:   matching the canary-replay.yml pattern). The bad tag itself is\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:171:   immutable per D-030 (the `scp-tag-protection-v` Repository\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:172:   Ruleset blocks deletion + force-push + non-fast-forward, including\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:173:   for admins).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:174:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:175:Both modes evaluate the same TWO invariants:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:176:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:177:- any `policies/deprecations.yaml` entry has `target_release` matching\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:178:  the candidate tag AND `announced_release` is not at least one MINOR\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:179:  behind the candidate, OR\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:180:- any `.scp/rule-config.yaml` entry on the SCP repo itself has\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:181:  `disable: true` AND `expires_at < <UTC date>` (the SCP-self\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:182:  half of TF-005 — adopter-side rule-config expiry is enforced at\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:183:  PR time via SCP-E007, not here).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:184:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:185:The release-gate also emits **warning** annotations\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:186:(`SCP-EREL-001-warn`) on suspicious deprecation patterns\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:187:(announced_release more than one major behind candidate) without\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:188:blocking — operators triage manually.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:189:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:190:### Tag-cut procedure (operator)\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:191:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:192:Mandatory pre-flight + apply pattern. ALWAYS:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:193:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:194:1. **Author the release-prep PR.** Bump `version-manifest.json`;\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:195:   add or remove entries in `policies/deprecations.yaml` per the\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:196:   ramp; write release notes; merge to `main`.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:197:2. **Dry-run the gate.** `gh workflow run release-gate.yml -f dry_run_tag=<tag>` and wait for exit 0.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:198:3. **Push the tag.** Only after dry-run is clean. The post-tag\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:199:   observer fires automatically as a final check.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:200:4. **Publish the GitHub release** + Renovate bump cascade per the\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:201:   normal 020H part 2 procedure.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:202:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:203:### Bad-tag recovery procedure\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:204:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:205:If a tag is pushed that fails the post-tag observer:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:206:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:207:- **Do NOT attempt to delete or force-push the tag.** The D-030 +\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:208:  D-034 tag-protection rulesets block deletion and force-push,\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:209:  including for admins. The bad tag is immutable.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:210:- **Cut a corrected `v<X>.<Y+1>.0`** (next MINOR) that satisfies\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:211:  the ramp. The bad tag remains in the tag list but is superseded\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:212:  by the corrected one.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:213:- **Add a release note on the bad tag's GitHub release page**\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:214:  documenting the violation + pointing adopters to the corrected\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:215:  tag. Detection latency depends on the adopter's bump path:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:216:  - **Renovate-using adopters** (the §12.7.2 recommended path) see\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:217:    the automated bump PR to `v<X>.<Y+1>.0` within hours of\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:218:    publication; the bump PR is the primary signal.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:219:  - **Manually SHA-pinning adopters** see no immediate signal at\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:220:    all. The `SCP-FRESH-001` freshness warning (ADOPT-001 §12.7.11)\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:221:    fires only when the wrapper is more than `freshness_warning_threshold_minor` (default 2) MINOR releases behind main HEAD —\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:222:    so an adopter pinned to the bad v<X>.<Y>.<Z> sees the warning\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:223:    only after `v<X>.<Y+3>.0` has been cut. Manual quarterly review\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:224:    of the SCP releases page (per the §12.7.11 manual fallback) is\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:225:    the supplementary signal for this cohort.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:226:- **In an emergency only** (e.g. the bad tag introduced a security\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:227:  vulnerability that publishing a corrected tag does not\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:228:  immediately mitigate), the temporary-ruleset-disable path is:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:229:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:230:  ```bash\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:231:  # 1. Discover the ruleset id.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:232:  gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/rulesets \\\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:233:    --jq '.[] | {id, name}'\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:234:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:235:  # 2. Delete the ruleset (requires administration:write PAT).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:236:  gh api -X DELETE repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/rulesets/<id>\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:237:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:238:  # 3. Delete the bad tag.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:239:  git push --delete origin v<X>.<Y>.<Z>\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:240:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:241:  # 4. Restore the ruleset (idempotent; reproduces the D-030 state).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:242:  bash scripts/configure-020j-protections.sh\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:243:  ```\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:244:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:245:  This bypasses the bus-factor-1 protection and MUST be paired with\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:246:  an amending decision row in `docs/DECISIONS.md` (closes 020H.3\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:247:  R2 COR-nit-002).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:248:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:249:Rule deprecation specifically: when an `SCP-R-NNN` rule is\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:250:deprecated:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:251:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:252:- The rule's deny continues to fire at its current `threshold:` value\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:253:  during the deprecation window.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:254:- **The rule's own Rego implementation** emits a per-PR\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:255:  `::warning::SCP-R-NNN deprecated; will be removed in v<X+1>.0.0; <migration-pointer>`\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:256:  annotation. There is no centralized emitter — each rule self-announces.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:257:  This is the `SCP-DEP-001` annotation class (registered in ADOPT-001\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:258:  §12.7.7); the deprecation-PR adds the warning emission alongside\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:259:  the existing rule logic and adds the matching entry to\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:260:  `policies/deprecations.yaml`.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:261:- The release-cut at v<X+1>.0.0 removes the rule from `policies/`\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:262:  AND removes the entry from `policies/deprecations.yaml`. The\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:263:  release-gate enforces this contract (refuses to cut the tag if\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:264:  the entry is still present and the ramp window hasn't elapsed).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:265:- A migration pointer (link to a rule-proposal-style amending document\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:266:  or a §M.N section of an ADR) MUST be in the warning annotation.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:267:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:268:Non-rule surfaces (workflow inputs, schema fields, annotation titles,\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:269:branch-protection helper flags, tag-protection patterns) follow the\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:270:same ramp pattern with surface-specific emission paths — the\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:271:`policies/deprecations.yaml` entry has `surface_kind` covering each\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:272:category. The emission responsibility belongs to the surface\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:273:maintainer (e.g. a workflow-input deprecation announces via a\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:274:deprecation log line in the workflow itself).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:275:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:276:---\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:277:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:278:## What \"stable\" means for v1.x\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:279:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:280:`v1.0.0` (cut 2026-04-30) is the first stable release. Until v2.0.0 is\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:281:cut:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:282:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:283:- The three rules `SCP-R-001`, `SCP-R-002`, `SCP-R-003` keep their IDs\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:284:  and (subject to the deprecation ramp) their behaviour shape.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:285:- The `workflow_call` inputs declared on `policy-check.yml` at v1.0.0\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:286:  remain stable.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:287:- The `schemas/policy-check-summary.schema.json` shape at v1.0.0\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:288:  remains stable.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:289:- The required-check context name `policy-check / scp/policy-check`\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:290:  (per D-033) remains stable.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:291:- The Renovate preset `extends:` shorthand\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:292:  `github>jrnb2024/standards-control-plane//renovate/default` remains\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:293:  stable.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:294:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:295:When v2.0.0 is contemplated, the proposal lands as an ADR via the\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:296:rule-RFC process at `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/` (see that\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:297:directory's `README.md`).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:298:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:299:---\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:300:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:301:## What adopters SHOULD do on each bump type\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:302:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:303:- **PATCH (auto-bumped by Renovate):** review the diff in the bump PR\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:304:  for unexpected behavioural changes, then merge. Most patches require\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:305:  no other action.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:306:- **MINOR:** read release notes; if any new rule lands at\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:307:  `threshold: warn` baseline, decide whether to opt into `threshold: deny`\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:308:  via `.scp/rule-config.yaml` or wait for the rule to be promoted in a\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:309:  future release.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:310:- **MAJOR:** read the migration guide in the release notes; file an\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:311:  amending decision row in your repo's `DECISIONS.md` (or equivalent)\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:312:  before bumping the SHA pin; if your repo is part of an estate\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:313:  cascade (WP-SCP-024), coordinate the bump with the estate owner.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:314:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:315:---\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:316:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:317:## How to file an amending decision\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:318:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:319:When an adopter accepts a MAJOR bump or breaking change, the\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:320:amending decision row should follow the pattern in\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:321:`docs/DECISIONS.md`:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:322:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:323:```\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:324:| D-NNN | <date> | Adopt SCP federation primitive v<X>.0.0 — breaking changes <enumerate>. <Migration steps taken>. | ACCEPTED | <rationale> |\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:325:```\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:326:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:327:This creates a durable audit trail of the version-bump decision\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:328:chain. Symmetric with how SCP self files D-022 (initial adoption)\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:329:and would file an amending row for any future SCP-self v2.0.0 jump.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:330:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:331:---\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:332:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:333:## References\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:334:\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:335:- WP-SCP-020 plan §4 020H.1 — slice acceptance for this document.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:336:- ADOPT-001 §12.7 — adopter integration appendix.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:337:- `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-022 — initial federation primitive adoption.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:338:- `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-036 — VERSIONING.md + rule-RFC process ratification.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:339:- `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/README.md` — rule-RFC process for rule additions and proposed breaking changes.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:340:- `policies/deprecations.yaml` — live deprecation register (the data the release-gate workflow reads).\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:341:- `schemas/deprecations.schema.json` — schema for the register.\npolicies/VERSIONING.md:342:- `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` — the machine-enforced ramp + expired-config refusal at tag-cut.\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:1:# Standards Control Plane — Decision Log\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:2:\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:3:**Last Updated:** 2026-05-10 (D-047 filed for WP-SCP-024 024B-extras; restore/break-glass/workflow wiring)\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:4:\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:5:> **D-021 reservation note (2026-04-28):** D-021 is reserved for the\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:6:> 2026-05-31 atomic workday filing per WP-SCP-019 hygiene response (PR\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:7:> #30, 2026-04-21). Codex executors running WP-SCP-022 implementation\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:8:> slices must NOT assign D-021 to any decision filed during the\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:9:> autonomous run. The WP-SCP-022 §4.7 gate-enforcement helper\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:10:> (`scripts/wp_scp_022_gate_check.sh --check-d021`) detects collisions.\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:11:\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:12:> **D-041 / D-042 / D-043 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 023A):**\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:13:> D-041 is reserved for WP-SCP-023 slice 023B (cross-repo scorecard data\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:14:> shape + opt-in adopter participation model). D-042 is reserved for\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:15:> slice 023C (aggregator pipeline trust model — GitHub Actions Artifact\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:16:> Attestation for adopter emits + SCP-side Ed25519 key registry).\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:17:> **Mandatory trust constraint on D-042 (closes 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001,\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:18:> per WP-SCP-023 §5 step 3):** the 023C aggregator MUST verify the\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:19:> `job_workflow_ref` OIDC claim in each artifact attestation against the\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:20:> SCP reusable workflow path AND SHA pin via `gh attestation verify\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:21:> --signer-workflow <owner>/<repo>/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<sha>`;\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:22:> OIDC JWKS signature verification alone is not sufficient.\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:23:> D-043 is reserved for slice 023D (MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:24:> shape + read-only contract). Codex executors dispatched for any\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:25:> WP-SCP-023 implementation slice must NOT assign D-041, D-042, or D-043\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:26:> to any other decision filed during that slice. The reservation pattern\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:27:> mirrors the D-021 guard above.\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:28:\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:29:> **D-044 / D-045 / D-046 reservation note (2026-05-03, plan-doc 024A):**\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:30:> D-044 was reserved for WP-SCP-024 slice 024B (`scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:31:> = `SCP-073-scaffolder` operational contract + adopter-template versioning\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:32:> + invocation-log convention extension). It is now filed as ACCEPTED in\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:33:> 024B-core; the deferred 024B-extras surface carries the `--restore`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:34:> rollback mode and workflow wiring. D-045 is reserved for slice 024C (estate\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:35:> cascade ordering canary-first per WP-SCP-024 §5.1, per-adopter\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:36:> onboarding contract per §5.2, post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:37:> week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle per invariant 8, cascade-slice rollback\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:38:> procedure per invariant 7). D-046 is reserved for slice 024G\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:39:> (estate-cascade Threshold A criteria + post-Threshold-A maintenance\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:40:> posture: recurring drift remediation, version-ramp coordination,\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:41:> departing-adopter procedure; decision on whether `scp.consult_estate_status`\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:42:> ships standalone or rolls into existing `consult_scorecard`). Codex\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:43:> executors dispatched for any WP-SCP-024 implementation slice must NOT\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:44:> assign D-044, D-045, or D-046 to any other decision filed during that\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:45:> slice. The reservation pattern mirrors the D-021 / D-041–043 guards\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:46:> above.\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:47:\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:48:| ID | Date | Decision | Status | Rationale |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:49:|----|------|----------|--------|-----------|\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:50:| D-001 | 2026-04-11 | Use Python for the phase 1 CLI-first implementation | ACCEPTED | Fast path to explicit schemas, local tooling, JSON validation, and deterministic file-based execution |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:51:| D-002 | 2026-04-11 | Keep the project as a standalone app rather than extending docs-agent or Control Tower directly | ACCEPTED | Keeps evaluator runtime independent while still allowing later integration with both systems |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:52:| D-003 | 2026-04-11 | Limit the first governed implementation slice to standards registry loading, minimal findings loading, and consult retrieval | ACCEPTED | Keeps the first end-to-end work package narrow enough to review rigorously while still allowing real consult output |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:53:| D-004 | 2026-04-11 | Introduce an explicit project-area intermediate representation before evaluator implementation | ACCEPTED | Keeps evaluator inputs deterministic, testable, and independent from raw repo sprawl |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:54:| D-005 | 2026-04-11 | Wire governance evaluation through the audit CLI before attempting architecture evaluation | ACCEPTED | Establishes one real evaluator path end to end before widening the audit surface |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:55:| D-006 | 2026-04-11 | Extend audit and project-area contracts before WP-SCP-003 implementation | ACCEPTED | Governance review evidence and unsupported-domain coverage must be first-class structured data, not implied by prose or raw path scanning |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:56:| D-007 | 2026-04-11 | Use an explicit unattended-delivery protocol for the remaining programme | ACCEPTED | The remaining work should continue without waiting for user answers, using documented default decisions, bounded review loops, and backlog carry-forward for non-blocking residuals |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:57:| D-008 | 2026-04-12 | Use explicit file-content signal heuristics for phase-1 architecture evaluation | ACCEPTED | The architecture slice needs deterministic, test-backed checks against repo-local evidence rather than broad semantic inference or prompt-only judgement |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:58:| D-009 | 2026-04-12 | Add a second repo-backed fixture corpus for architecture signal coverage | ACCEPTED | `ARCH-003` and `ARCH-004` need concrete repo-backed sample files instead of synthetic payload-only tests if the slice is going to prove its own honesty |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:59:| D-010 | 2026-04-12 | Reconcile findings by deterministic finding ID and area-scoped audit coverage | ACCEPTED | Findings persistence must refresh and resolve records only inside the audited area and evaluated domains so unrelated history is not disturbed |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:60:| D-011 | 2026-04-12 | Guard findings persistence with scope-collision checks and per-file atomic replacement plus rollback | ACCEPTED | Persisted lifecycle state must fail on `finding_id` scope collisions and should avoid half-written files without pretending phase 1 has a crash-safe multi-file transaction |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:61:| D-012 | 2026-04-12 | Bind generated report and area-summary timestamps to the current audit timestamp | ACCEPTED | Report outputs need byte-stable reruns and freshness checks, so they should reuse `audit_result.generated_at` rather than inventing wall-clock timestamps |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:62:| D-013 | 2026-04-12 | Reuse the current write-flow guarantees for report artifacts and carry true bundled transactions to backlog | ACCEPTED | The reporting slice should stay downstream of the existing persistence guarantees instead of pretending to offer a crash-safe cross-artifact commit in phase 1 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:63:| D-014 | 2026-04-12 | Guard `report` freshness with embedded findings-state signatures as well as audit timestamp | ACCEPTED | A date-bound audit timestamp alone is too weak to detect same-day content drift, so the report needs a stronger freshness check against persisted findings state |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:64:| D-015 | 2026-04-12 | Apply waivers as an audit-time overlay rather than embedding waiver rules inside evaluators | ACCEPTED | Evaluators should keep emitting deterministic raw findings so the same checks can be reused with or without waivers, while audit assembly owns exception handling |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:65:| D-016 | 2026-04-12 | Centralise score calculation in a shared module and count only active unwaived findings against score | ACCEPTED | Score semantics must be documented, deterministic, and consistent across evaluators and audit assembly, and waived issues should not drag active score down |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:66:| D-017 | 2026-04-12 | Use one embedded fenced JSON review-evidence block as the shared contract for governance validation and historical review retrieval | ACCEPTED | One small structured block inside markdown keeps review evidence inspectable in git while avoiding two drifting review-data formats |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:67:| D-018 | 2026-04-12 | Keep historical review retrieval as explicit consult output rather than hiding it inside generic guidance text | ACCEPTED | Review history should be visible, bounded, and machine-readable so later consumers can use it without reparsing prose |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:68:| D-019 | 2026-04-18 | SVC-003 is declare-a-contract with a closed four-mode set (`mode.user_oidc`, `mode.service_rs256`, `mode.api_key`, `mode.bearer_legacy`); commit `66ba8a4` codifies `mode.user_oidc` with no rework; WP-SCP-018 `--auth-token` classifies as `mode.bearer_legacy` with deprecation close date 2026-06-30 | ACCEPTED | Estate reality has three live token types plus a cookie session flow; a single fixed mechanism breaks machine callers; a closed mode set prevents drift; codifying the existing CT OIDC layer keeps the in-repo auth story consistent without forcing a rework |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:69:| D-020 | 2026-04-18 | `_normalise_scope` accepts `request.scope.area_id` as the normaliser hint when `_infer_area_id` raises `AreaIdInferenceError`; mismatched-inference still raises the same way as before | ACCEPTED | Adopters auditing scopes that lack an ENH-style marker (e.g. a root-level `services.yml` dogfood) would otherwise have to plant placeholder enhancement docs to satisfy area-id inference; the narrow relaxation preserves the auditor discipline of catching inferred-vs-claimed mismatches while closing the genuine uninferrable-scope ergonomic gap |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:70:| D-022 | 2026-04-21 | Adopt reusable GitHub Actions workflow + OPA/Conftest + Renovate shared preset + required status check with `enforce_admins=true` as the estate's policy federation primitive. Alternatives rejected: `palantir/policy-bot` (GitHub App per org, HCL-not-Rego, no Renovate cascade, no native waiver-overlay); custom control-plane service (build cost, duplicates GH Actions + branch protection primitives) | ACCEPTED | Industry-standard shape; no custom control-plane service required; cheapest path converting SCP from advisory auditor to pre-merge gate; Renovate preset cascade gives \"change one rule → enforce across 10 repos in 24h\"; supports waiver-aware evaluation and structured annotation payloads. Full rationale body in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §10 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:71:| D-023 | 2026-04-21 | Reject multi-agent free-form chat-forum pattern as the agent-coordination venue; adopt structured proposal queue (`docs/reviews/proposals/PROP-NNN.md` + MCP `propose()` tool — initial stub in WP-SCP-021 slice 021E; full adjudication workflow in `WP-SCP-022-proposal-queue`, separately tracked per `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §12). Agents never free-form chat with each other; they read SCP's decision records and call SCP's MCP tools | ACCEPTED | Du et al. (ICML 2024, `arxiv 2305.14325`) show multi-agent debate converges to consensus fast including when the consensus is wrong; Anthropic's multi-agent research post reports ~15× token cost with compounding coordination errors; human-on-the-loop literature converges on moderator-as-bottleneck past a few decisions/hour. Proposal-queue pattern scales because the human is on the loop, not in it. Full rationale body in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §10 (decision originator) and `docs/plans/WP-SCP-021-scp-as-mcp-server.md` §10 (`propose()` stub design). Note 2026-04-28: original D-023 forward-referenced \"WP-SCP-022 plan when that WP opens\"; WP-SCP-022 v0.2 is the implementation programme plan, not the proposal-queue WP — the rationale-body expansion lives in the parent plans named here, and the adjudication WP is renamed `WP-SCP-022-proposal-queue` |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:72:| D-024 | 2026-04-21 | Adopt Anthropic's Model Context Protocol (MCP) as the estate's agent-to-SCP tool protocol. Transports: stdio (primary, local, trust-the-process) + streamable HTTP (opt-in, bearer-token via `SCP_MCP_TOKEN` with 30-day rotation overlap). Ed25519 asymmetric signing for consult receipts — SCP holds private key; adopters verify with public key published at `scp://security/signing-keys` + committed `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` (90-day rotation overlap). Python `mcp` SDK pinned by version + sdist SHA256; distributed via PyPI as `standards-control-plane[mcp]` extra. OAuth deferred to SCP-075-oauth | ACCEPTED | MCP is the dominant vertical agent-to-tool protocol post Linux Foundation Agentic AI Foundation launch (Dec 2025); Anthropic is protocol origin; Claude Code/Desktop + ACC speak MCP natively. Asymmetric signing prevents adopter-held-key forgery (HMAC symmetric rejected in adversarial review round 1). Alternatives rejected: raw REST (no client ecosystem); custom JSON-RPC (reinvents MCP); gRPC (no agent client support); HMAC symmetric (forgeable by any key-holding adopter). Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-021-scp-as-mcp-server.md` §10 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:73:| D-025 | 2026-04-21 | Scoped pre-code consult requirement with Ed25519-signed receipts. Downstream `CLAUDE.md` mandates `scp.consult_rules` before code authoring in governed domains; Claude Code `PreCommit` hook refuses commit without valid receipt. Scope rule: hook consults `scp://rules/domain-map` via `resolve_domain(changed_files)`; non-empty result → receipt required; default-skip globs for docs-only changes. Receipt envelope binds `{schema_version, key_id, repo, head_sha, base_sha, changed_files_hash, domains_covered, issued_at, expires_at ≤ 2h}`; hook validates every field. Break-glass `SCP_MCP_ALLOW_OFFLINE=true` requires committed `docs/overrides/OVERRIDE-NNN.md` with schema-validated expiry ≤ 14d; emits tracked finding SCP-MCP-E010 | ACCEPTED | Client-side enforcement pairs with server-side gate (WP-SCP-020) as belt + braces; scoped + TTL + PR-bound receipts prevent replay/forgery/scope-bypass. Break-glass requires sibling OVERRIDE artefact so fail-closed posture is maintained. Rego gate is authoritative — MCP consult never bypasses. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-021-scp-as-mcp-server.md` §10 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:74:| D-026 | 2026-04-28 | Autonomous-dispatch protocol for SCP implementation slices. Each WP-SCP-020 and WP-SCP-021 implementation slice flows through four-tier dispatch: Opus orchestrator (current agent) prepares dispatch package conforming to `~/Projects/acc/schemas/codex_work_package.schema.json`; Codex executor tier runs the slice via `codex_dispatch.py`; 3× parallel Sonnet R1 reviewers apply correctness / safety_bypass / completeness_governance lenses via `claude_dispatch.py` with 500 ms stagger; Opus consolidates verdicts and orchestrates fix rounds. Recurse to fixpoint per `feedback_recursive_adversarial_review.md`. Fix-round budget 5; on budget exhaustion, slice escalates to user review. Evidence persists at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-022/dispatches/<slice-id>/`. No slice merges without 3× APPROVED verdict | ACCEPTED | Estate four-tier dispatch standard since 2026-04-22 (per `feedback_four_tier_dispatch.md`); applies to non-trivial work. SCP implementation slices are non-trivial — they touch CI, branch protection, signing keys, and PyPI. Adversarial review pattern proven on WP-SCP-019 (5 rounds), WP-SCP-020 (5 rounds), WP-SCP-021 (3 rounds, fixpoint). Persisting evidence in-repo gives a permanent audit trail and lets future agents recover from session-bounded amnesia. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:75:| D-027 | 2026-04-28 | Parallel-track execution for WP-SCP-020 (federation primitive) and WP-SCP-021 (MCP server) implementation, Scope Y per user 2026-04-28 selection. Both tracks run concurrently from dispatch-zero to user-gate. Track 1 (020): 020B → 020B.1 → 020B.2 → 020C → 020C.1 → 020J → 020K → 020D1 → 020H part 1 → 020E.a → [USER-GATE-A0 release sign-off] → 020H part 2 → 020D2 → [USER-GATE-A] (12 implementation slices + 1 mid-chain human-input gate + 1 terminal gate, matching WP-SCP-020 §3 canonical sequence verbatim). Track 2 (021): 021B → 021C → 021D → 021E → [USER-GATE-C] (4 implementation slices + 1 terminal gate). Concurrent-dispatch limit: 4 active Codex sessions across both tracks. `pyproject.toml` partition: Track 1 owns `[tool.scp.federation]` and adds `scp-policy-check` to `[project.scripts]`; Track 2 owns `[project.optional-dependencies.mcp]` and adds `scp-mcp-server` to `[project.scripts]`. `docs/STATUS.md` excluded from all slice scope_boundary globs | ACCEPTED | WP-SCP-021 §scope statement declares the tracks independent; serial execution would defer MCP availability for ~2× wall-clock without quality gain. Concurrent dispatch within rate-limit envelope per `four-tier-dispatch-field-report-2026-04-22.md`. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.4. Track 1 sequence corrected in v0.2 (R1 fix-round) to match WP-SCP-020 §3 canonical ordering — earlier draft omitted 020K and inverted 020D2 placement |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:76:| D-028 | 2026-04-28 | SCP adopts D-048 / ADR-016 Design Parity Build Method (DPBM) as a contract input for any SCP slice that produces designed visual output. Layered amendment to four-tier dispatch — prototype + flows + design principles enter the contract layer the build is bound to. Enforcement-injection mechanism per `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.6: visual-output slices' dispatch packages MUST include a \"DPBM contract\" subsection naming prototype path, flow diagram, and design-principles reference; orchestrator verifies subsection presence before launching the review pass; absence is treated as a CRIT finding. Within WP-SCP-022 itself no slices match the DPBM \"applies\" criteria (workflow / Rego / MCP-server / CI work, no visual output); D-028 is forward-looking. WP-SCP-024 estate cascade inherits D-028; FLA, ACC, RI canary-onboarding instructions reference the DPBM contract layer. D-028 lands operationally once CT PR #202 + ACC PR #106 have merged | ACCEPTED | DPBM closes a structural gap that pure-code lenses can't see — a frontend built under standard four-tier dispatch can satisfy every test and still drift from the design. Without an SCP-side adoption decision, agents working through SCP's MCP consult won't be told that the contract for visual-output work includes design artefacts. CT PR #202 + ACC PR #106 (both 2026-04-28) introduce the upstream doctrine; SCP adopts at the policy layer. Full rationale + injection-mechanism specification in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-022-implementation-programme-plan.md` §4.6 |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:77:| D-029 | 2026-04-29 | `policy-check.yml` reusable workflow `permissions:` block expands to `contents: read, statuses: write` to support WP-SCP-022 020C.1(vi) read-back commit-status posting on the sibling context `scp/policy-check-readback`. Original 020B(iii) baseline was `contents: read` only. The `statuses: write` privilege uses the caller's `${{ github.token }}` and posts only to `repos/<caller>/statuses/${{ pull_request.head.sha }}`; no other write surface is unlocked. Disabling the read-back would require accepting a regression on 020C.1(vi); keeping `contents: read` only would prevent the read-back from being posted | ACCEPTED | The read-back surface is the only place a PR reviewer sees waiver/disabled-rule posture without reading JSON artefacts; WP-SCP-020 §4.3 fixpoint criteria for 020C.1(vi) require it. The privilege footprint is narrowest possible — `statuses: write` does not allow content modification, branch operations, issue/PR comments, or token impersonation. The workflow checkout uses `persist-credentials: false` so the elevated privilege is bounded to the policy-check job. Plan amendment: `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §4 020B(iii) updated with cross-reference to D-029. Identified by WP-SCP-022 R1 completeness review (MAJ-005) |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:78:| D-030 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020J on the SCP repository: (a) tag-protection rule on `v*` (legacy tag-protection API and/or Repository Ruleset) preventing force-push or deletion of release tags; (b) `required-signed-commits` on `main` so every commit reaching `main` carries a verified signature. Both are preconditions for slice 020D1 (self-dogfood wrapper pinned at the v1.0.0-rc.1 commit-SHA) and 020D2 (required-status-check + v1.0.0 cut). Configured via `scripts/configure-020j-protections.sh` (idempotent API caller). Documented in `docs/security/branch-protection.md`. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: a single GitHub admin (@jrnb2024) can disable these via repo Settings; quarterly review cadence per WP-SCP-020 §14 U-sec-2 closure | ACCEPTED | Path (a) selected at WP-SCP-020 plan merge per §14 U-sec-2 — Personal GitHub Pro tier supports both protections natively, no signed-release-manifest substitute needed. Tag-protection prevents tag mutation post-cut (the supply-chain anchor for adopters pinning by SHA + comment-tag); required-signed-commits prevents un-attested code from reaching the gate's source of truth. Future direct commits to main without a verified signature are blocked, which is the intent (forces all changes through PRs whose squash-merges are auto-signed by GitHub's bot key). The unsigned commit `bcfc706` (USER-GATE-C signoff, 2026-04-29, unsigned) predates this enablement and is grandfathered. Identified as gate-readiness work in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §4 020J + §3 sequence + §8 risks (\"Bootstrap trust\") + §9.1 sequencing |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:79:| D-031 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020K on the SCP repository in the personal-account / single-operator mode resolved at §14 U-k closure: (a) NO `scp-break-glass` GitHub team is created — GitHub teams are not available on user namespaces and `jrnb2024` is a personal user account; (b) `CODEOWNERS` extends to cover the additional governance-sensitive paths named in §4 020K (canonical-minimum), then broadened/extended via 020K R1+R2+R3 safety reviews to close 7 MAJ + 4 MIN + 6 nit findings — see CODEOWNERS file header + `FIX-ROUND-{1,2,3}.md` for the full audit trail of which paths were broadened (subsuming a narrower canonical rule) vs added net-new; (c) at slice 020D2, branch-protection on `main` is configured with `required_approving_review_count = 1`, `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`, and `require_review_from_non_author = false` (solo operator; self-approval is the only option) — **NOTE (D-033 amendment, 2026-04-30 evening):** the anticipated `required_approving_review_count = 1` was corrected to `count = 0` by D-033 when the first PR through enforced mode revealed that GitHub forbids PR self-review; count=1 + sole CODEOWNER = operator locked out of repo. See D-033 for the live state, the operational test path (USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64), and the second-maintainer escalation path; (d) §8 bus-factor-1 risk row remains LIVE with quarterly escalation review at 2026-07-21 named in `STATUS.md` \"Open scheduled follow-ups\" and in auto-memory `project_scheduled_followups.md`. **Escalation path when a second maintainer onboards:** add them to `CODEOWNERS`, flip `require_review_from_non_author = true`, amend §8 risk row to CLOSED. **020D1 → 020D2 dependency:** 020K completes before 020D2 opens (the branch-protection wiring at 020D2 reads from CODEOWNERS established here). Identified at WP-SCP-020 plan §3 sequence + §4 020K + §14 U-k closure | ACCEPTED | Personal-account path is the only viable shape for v1.0.0 on a personal user namespace. The CODEOWNERS expansion forces every future change to `renovate/**` (Renovate preset that cascades pin-bumps across adopters), `docs/DECISIONS.md` (the decision-record canonical home), and `output/findings/waivers.json` (the safety-valve store) through reviewer attention rather than allowing direct push. Bus-factor-1 is acknowledged as live operational exposure rather than papered over: `require_review_from_non_author = false` reflects reality (a solo operator cannot self-approve under non-author review), and the 2026-07-21 quarterly review is the named re-evaluation moment. Path (b) extension of `CODEOWNERS` is forward-looking on `renovate/**` (the directory does not yet exist in the working tree; it lands in slice 020F); CODEOWNERS rules on non-existent paths are no-ops, so adding the rule pre-emptively is harmless and removes a future drift risk where 020F could land without simultaneously adding the matching CODEOWNERS row. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §4 020K + §8 (bus factor risk row, line 188) + §14 U-k closure |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:80:| D-032 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020D2 on the SCP repository post-USER-GATE-A0: enable `scp/policy-check` as a required status check on `main` with `strict: true` (PR must be up-to-date with base before evaluation); set `enforce_admins: true` (no admin bypass); set `required_pull_request_reviews` with `required_approving_review_count: 1`, `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`, `require_code_owner_reviews: true`; explicitly leave `require_review_from_non_author: false` per 020K personal-account closure (single-operator self-approval is the only viable path). Configured via `scripts/configure-020d2-required-check.sh` (idempotent). After 020D2, every PR to `main` must pass the federation primitive's gate AND have at least one approving review AND have a verified signature on every commit AND cannot be bypassed by the admin role. The 020E.a pre-protection canary (workflow-run-id 25172373569) demonstrated the deny path on a real PR with a real violation pre-flip; 020E.b will demonstrate that the now-required check actually blocks merge. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: a single GitHub admin (@jrnb2024) is the operator; quarterly review at 2026-07-21 (per 020K + D-031) reconciles documented-vs-live state. **Note (D-033 forward-reference, 2026-04-30 evening):** the live state of three D-032 parameters was amended