action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\nSTATUS.md:120:\nSTATUS.md:121:## Today's chain (2026-05-09 — D-035-rules retired + WP-SCP-025 parked)\nSTATUS.md:122:\nSTATUS.md:123:**Operator decision (locked 2026-05-09):** the 6 D-035-aligned rules previously framed as gating CT Wave 1 entry on 2026-05-15 are **RETIRED under that deadline** — re-scoped under WP-SCP-025 (parked, post-WP-SCP-024 Threshold A). The retirement is conditional on a strategic reframe: SCP's near-term credibility depends on shipping 2-3 high-value domain rules that catch things review misses + measurable adopter consumption (≥3 cohort adopters running ≥2 SCP-R-005+ rules with ≥80% pass rate over ≥4-week observation window), not on forcing the 6 SDK-discipline rules through under deadline pressure when (a) CT D-035 Phase 5 already shipped 2026-05-07 without these rules as preconditions; (b) WP-SCP-024 cascade is operator-decided FLA-independent per 2026-05-03 §2 invariants row 4; (c) none of the 6 had been drafted with 6 days remaining; (d) parallel work on slice 024B (the actual cascade gate per plan-doc §6) would have been diluted.\nSTATUS.md:124:\nSTATUS.md:125:**The 6 retired rule names** (preserved here for traceability — re-evaluate at WP-SCP-025 kickoff against the §4 candidate list in the parked plan-doc):\nSTATUS.md:126:1. `sdk_version_pin` (was Wave 1 gate)\nSTATUS.md:127:2. `ct_sdk_conformance` (was Wave 1 gate)\nSTATUS.md:128:3. `sdk_migration_waiver` (was Wave 1 gate)\nSTATUS.md:129:4. `sdk_adoption_schedule` (was Wave 1 mid)\nSTATUS.md:130:5. `bff_refresh_hardening` (was Wave 2 gate)\nSTATUS.md:131:6. `ct_auth_provider_memoization` (was Wave 3 gate)\nSTATUS.md:132:\nSTATUS.md:133:**Cross-project reconciliation:** SCP filed `SCP-D035-RULES-RETIRED-2026-05-09.md` to CT governance notifications log requesting CT amendments to (a) `docs/briefings/recommender-shopify-j1-rbac-response-2026-05-09.md` Q6+Q8 to drop the 6-rules / 2026-05-15-deadline framing before the response ships, (b) `docs/plans/PL