d:202:- ~~**TF-020H1-001**: `enforce_release_gate` workflow~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.3** (this PR's branch); `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` reads `policies/deprecations.yaml` (validated against `schemas/deprecations.schema.json`) and refuses a tag-cut on `push: tags: ['v*']` when any entry's `target_release` matches the candidate AND `announced_release` is not at least one MINOR behind. `workflow_dispatch:` with `dry_run_tag` input lets the operator test before pushing. Annotation: `SCP-EREL-001`.\nSTATUS.md:203:- **TF-020H1-002**: `canary-replay.yml` paging rotation — at v1.0.0 the auto-opened `rule-regression` issue assigns `@jrnb2024` only (single-operator per D-031). For estate cascade (WP-SCP-024) a paging rotation would replace the assignee-only signal. Closure path: revisit at WP-SCP-024 planning OR at the 2026-07-21 quarterly bus-factor review when a second maintainer onboards. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.1 R1 completeness COMP-MAJ-002 closure.\nSTATUS.md:204:- **TF-020H1-003**: `auto-defer` GitHub Action for stale rule-proposals — currently a manual close + `defer` label step (per `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/README.md` §Process step 2). For estate scale (post-WP-SCP-024 cascade) when proposal volume warrants automation, a scheduled GH Action would close PRs with no approvals after the 48h window. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.1 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-004 closure.\nSTATUS.md:205:- ~~**TF-020H1-004**: rule-config disable canary missing~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.4** (this PR's branch). New `canary/rule-config-disabled` branch (PR #81 DO-NOT-MERGE; SHA `841d350`) carries the deliberate SCP-R-001 violation + a `.scp/rule-config.yaml` disable entry; workflow run `25211284467` verified PASS (deny suppressed by rule-config code path; findings=0; waivers=0; disabled_rules=2). `scripts/replay-canary.sh` registry extended with `rule-config-disabled|canary/rule-config-disabled|SUCCESS|0|0`. `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/canary-evidence.md` extended with Canary 4 baseline section. Suppression-path coverage triad complete: deny / waiver-suppressed / rule-config-suppressed.\nSTATUS.md:206:- ~~**TF-020H1-005**~~ ✅ primary deliverable closed in 020H.1 fix-round-1 (SAFE-nit-008): `RULE-TEMPLATE.md` §10 `[BLOCKING]` / `[deferrable]` question-marking guidance + no-quorum-with-unresolved-`[BLOCKING]` invariant landed. This TF remains nominally open only for any subsequent §10 enhancement (e.g. an auto-detect linter that flags unresolved `[BLOCKING]` markers in a proposal PR). No deadline (cosmetic).\nSTATUS.md:207:\nSTATUS.md:208:## Tracked-forward items from 020H.3 (release-gate)\nSTATUS.md:209:\nSTATUS.md:210:- **TF-020H3rg-001**: PR-time deprecation-announcement linter — currently a rule-deprecation PR adds an entry to `policies/deprecations.yaml` per the rule-RFC process; no automated check that the entry is added when a `deprecated` annotation is introduced. Closure path: a future linter step in `policy-check.yml` (or a separate workflow) that greps for new `deprecated` warning emissions in a PR diff and refuses the PR if no corresponding `policies/deprecations.yaml` entry was added in the same PR. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.3 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-002 closure.\nSTATUS.md:211:- ~~**TF-020H3rg-002**: `pip install --require-hashes` for `policy-check.yml` + `release-gate.yml` pyyaml/jsonschema installs.~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020M** (this PR's branch). `requirements/policy-check.in` (top-level pins) + `requirements/policy-check.txt` (generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes`, full transitive closure with all-platform wheel SHA256s) added. All 5 install sites (4× `policy-check.yml` + 1× `release-gate.yml`) switched to `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/policy-check.txt`. Top-level pins unchanged from v1.0.0 (`pyyaml==6.0.2` + `jsonschema==4.23.0`); only the install mechanism is hardened. PATCH bump v1.0.0 → v1.0.1 per VERSIONING.md \"internal refactors\". D-038 filed.\nSTATUS.md:212:- ~~**TF-020H3rg-003**: Auto-open `release-gate-violation` issue on push:tags failure~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020H.3.1** (this PR's branch). `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` split into two jobs: `release-gate` (evaluation; `contents: read`) + `release-gate-violation-issue` (`needs: release-gate`; `if: needs.release-gate.result == 'failure' && github.event_name == 'push'`; `permissions: { contents: read, issues: write }`; pre-creates labels via `gh label create --force`; de-dups by tag substring; uses Python templating in both new-issue and comment branches). Ratified by **D-037** (issues:write job-level scope). Forward-compat assignee env: `SCP_RELEASE_GATE_ASSIGNEES` (defaults to `jrnb2024`).\nSTATUS.md:213:- **TF-020H3rg-004**: Issue auto-close on corrective tag-cut — when the operator cuts the corrected `v<X>.<Y+1>.0`, the open `release-gate-violation` issue isn't auto-closed. Operator closes manually after the triage checklist completes. Closure path: a future workflow step that detects the corrected tag-cut and `gh issue close`s any open release-gate-violation issue for the bad tag-series. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.3.1 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-001 closure.\nSTATUS.md:214:\nSTATUS.md:215:## Tracked-forward items from 020M (supply-chain hash-pinning)\nSTATUS.md:216:\nSTATUS.md:217:- ~~**TF-020M-001**: `conflict-gate.yml` retains `pip install pyyaml>=6.0` (line ~42) without hash-pinning.~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020N** (this PR's branch). `requirements/conflict-gate.in` (top-level pins matching `pyproject.toml` `[project.dependencies]` + `[project.optional-dependencies.dev]`) + `requirements/conflict-gate.txt` (generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes` under Python 3.12, full transitive closure with all-platform wheel SHA256s) added. `.github/workflows/conflict-gate.yml` \"Install Python dependencies\" step restructured to: (i) hash-pinned `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/conflict-gate.txt`; (ii) local vendored `ct-auth` wheel installed `--no-deps`; (iii) editable local SCP package installed `--no-deps`; (iv) post-install version-pin assertion (mirrors 020M SAFE-MAJ-002 pattern). No semver bump (conflict-gate is internal-only per VERSIONING.md §\"Scope\"). D-039 filed.\nSTATUS.md:218:- ~~**TF-020M-002**: ADOPT-001 §12.7.13 lockfile regeneration procedure does not warn that the hardcoded version-pin assertion strings must be updated in lockstep when bumping the lockfile.~~ ✅ **already inline-closed in slice 020M fix-round-2** (commit `37bbf5e`). The REGENERATION INVARIANT callout added to ADOPT-001 §12.7.13 explicitly names the four hardcoded `assert yaml.__version__ ==` / `assert jsonschema.__version__ ==` sites that must be updated in lockstep. The TF entry filed by the R2 safety reviewer was redundant with the inline closure; pruned in slice 020N STATUS.md update.\nSTATUS.md:219:\nSTATUS.md:220:## Tracked-forward items from 020N (conflict-gate hash-pinning)\nSTATUS.md:221:\nSTATUS.md:222:- **TF-020N-001**: `conflict-gate.yml` `permissions: id-token: write` is workflow-default scoped (line ~23) and applies across all steps including the new pip-install step (slice 020N). The `id-token: write` was originally added for `gh attestation verify` of OPA/Conftest binaries (a pre-020N step). With slice 020N's hash-pinned pip install above the attestation step, the `id-token: write` exposure surface during the pip-install network call is now broader than necessary — pip itself does not need OIDC. Closure path: narrow the privilege to job-level or step-level scoping so the new pip-install step runs with `contents: read` only. Forward-compat; symmetric posture with D-037's `release-gate-violation-issue` job-level scoping (slice 020H.3.1). Filed at 020N R1 safety SAFE-MIN-003 closure.\nSTATUS.md:223:\nSTATUS.md:224:## Tracked-forward items from 020L (first rule-RFC dogfood)\nSTATUS.md:225:\nSTATUS.md:226:- **TF-020L-001**: Unicode-whitespace regex divergence between Python `re` (Unicode-aware `\\S`) and OPA RE2 (ASCII-only `\\s`). For the §6.2 ASCII fixture corpus the divergence is irrelevant; a future fixture with Unicode whitespace in a URL-like string may surface conflict-gate flap. Closure path: Phase-2 implementation monitors SCP self-dogfood gate for `SCP-E005` flap on Unicode-whitespace input; if observed, anchor the regex pattern to ASCII-only printable range (e.g. `https?://[\\x21-\\x7e]+`) in both engines and add a fixture. Close as no-op if no divergence surfaces during the warn-baseline observation window. **Status at v1.1.0 cut (2026-05-02): no flap observed across slice 020P CI, release-gate dry-run, and post-tag observer; continue monitoring across estate adopters until ~30-90d post-v1.1.0.** Forward-compat; no deadline. Filed at 020L R1 correctness COR-NIT-001 closure.\nSTATUS.md:227:- ~~**TF-020L-002**: RULE-TEMPLATE.md §5 lacks residual-bypass guidance for rules enforcing syntactic-only patterns.~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020P** (PR #91, commit `d83ce52`); RULE-TEMPLATE.md §5 amended with \"Residual known bypass (for syntactic-pattern rules)\" guidance pointing at RULE-001 §5 case 5 as worked example.\nSTATUS.md:228:- ~~**TF-020L-003**: README.md §3 Merge says \"An entry in `docs/DECISIONS.md` if the rule introduces a new domain...\" but does NOT define \"new domain\".~~ ✅ **closed in slice 020P** (PR #91, commit `d83ce52`); README.md §3 amended with \"new domain\" definition (new top-level input schema OR no existing SCP-R-NNN counterpart; same-input-schema additions are same-domain).\nSTATUS.md:229:\nSTATUS.md:230:## Tracked-forward items from 020P (RULE-001 Phase 2)\nSTATUS.md:231:\nSTATUS.md:232:- **TF-020P-001**: data-driven `policies/rule-baselines.yaml` + `schemas/rule-baselines.schema.json` to replace the hardcoded `WARN_BASELINE_RULES = {\"SCP-R-004\"}` set in `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml`. Closure path: file when a 2nd warn-baseline rule lands (likely during the next rule-RFC slice). Hardcoded set is sufficient at v1.1.0 (single warn-baseline rule). Forward-compat; no deadline. Filed in DISPATCH-NOTE risk surface + release notes + workflow inline comment.\nSTATUS.md:233:- **TF-020P-002**: conflict-gate fixture corpus has 2 fixtures (1 allow + 1 deny) vs RULE-001 §6.2's spec'd ~12 (matches established SCP-R-001/002 minimal-smoke-test pattern; Conftest tests cover full corpus exhaustively). Closure path: EITHER expand conflict-gate fixture corpus to match RULE-001 §6.2 verbatim (10 more fixture pairs) OR amend RULE-TEMPLATE.md §6.2 framing to canonise the minimal-smoke-test pattern. Lightweight; foldable into next RFC slice or process-doc maintenance slice. Forward-compat; no deadline. Filed at 020P R1 completeness COMP-MIN-001 closure.\nSTATUS.md:234:- ~~**TF-020P-003**~~ ✅ **closed 2026-05-02 PM-4 in TF-020P-005 slice (this PR)** — absorbed by `scripts/scp-pre-push-verify.sh`'s Regal lint gate (parity with CI \"Lint policies with Regal\" step, same disable list).\nSTATUS.md:235:- ~~**TF-020P-004**~~ ✅ **closed 2026-05-02 PM-4 in TF-020P-005 slice (this PR)** — absorbed by `scripts/scp-pre-push-verify.sh`'s per-rule `opa test --coverage --threshold 90 --fail-on-empty -v` gate (parity with CI \"Enforce per-rule OPA coverage\" step).\nSTATUS.md:236:- ~~**TF-020P-005**~~ ✅ **closed 2026-05-02 PM-4 (this PR)** — `scripts/scp-pre-push-verify.sh` lands; ~150 lines bash, mirrors all three CI rule-author gates (Regal lint + `opa fmt --fail` + per-rule `opa test --coverage --threshold 90 --fail-on-empty -v`); aggregate failure collection; non-fatal `.tool-versions` parity warning; CODEOWNERS already covers via `scripts/** @jrnb2024`. ADOPT-001 §12.7.9.1 references the wrapper as recommended-not-required for rule authors.\nSTATUS.md:237:- **TF-020P-005b**: ADOPT-001 §12.7.9.1 audience-placement reorganisation. The wrapper section sits as a sub-section of §12.7.9 (adopter pre-commit hook section) but its audience is SCP-repo rule authors. Acceptable for v1.1.0 with the explicit \"Audience: SCP-repo rule authors only\" clarifier added in slice TF-020P-005 (this PR). Closure path: opportunistic next ADOPT-001 structural pass — move §12.7.9.1 to a dedicated §12.x SCP-self tooling section. Forward-compat; no deadline. Filed at TF-020P-005 R1 completeness COMP-MIN-001.\nSTATUS.md:238:- **TF-020P-005c**: optional `SCP_PRE_PUSH_VERSION_STRICT=1` env var to make `scripts/scp-pre-push-verify.sh`'s `.tool-versions` parity check fatal — for CI-in-CI or strict local-dev workflows where version drift should hard-fail. Default behaviour stays non-fatal warning per slice 020P-005 design (DISPATCH-NOTE Risk #1). Closure path: opportunistic; file when a second requestor surfaces the need. Forward-compat; no deadline. Filed at TF-020P-005 R1 completeness COMP-NIT-003.\nSTATUS.md:239:\nSTATUS.md:240:## Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-023 023A (plan-doc) + 023B (emitter) + 023C (aggregator)\nSTATUS.md:241:\nSTATUS.md:242:- **TF-023A-001** (low priority): R-023-01 k-anonymity mitigation framing clarification when WP-SCP-024 cascade slice begins. The plan-doc R-023-01 risk row references \"slice 024 introduces aggregator-side k-anonymity\"; tighten when WP-SCP-024 plan-doc lands. Forward-compat; opportunistic.\nSTATUS.md:243:- **TF-023A-002** (medium priority): Cross-repo notification (v1.2.0 release announcement to ACC / CT / mapp-estate-regression) — **re-deferred to slice 023E** (was 023D; 023D ships exposure surface but Threshold A onboarding is where adopters first participate). Until adopters can opt in with the exposure surface live, the notification is a \"pre-Threshold-A FYI\" only. Filed at WP-SCP-023 023A; re-deferred at 023D R1 completeness CMP-MIN-001.\nSTATUS.md:244:- **TF-023B-001** (low priority): Workflow-selftest harness `fixture-pass-with-scorecard-emit` — extend `tests/workflow/fixture-pass/` to cover the new opt-in `scorecard-emit: true` input on the SCP self-dogfood wrapper. Target slice 023C (when SCP self-dogfood wrapper is extended with `scorecard-emit: true` to feed the aggregator's first run). Forward-compat. Filed at 023B R1 completeness CG-MIN-005.\nSTATUS.md:245:- **TF-023B-002** (low priority): FLA-pilot canary scorecard fixture — capture FLA's first successful scorecard emit at slice 023E as a permanent fixture. Target slice 023E. Filed at 023B R1 completeness CG-nit-003.\nSTATUS.md:246:- **TF-023B-003** (low priority): Promote `WARN_BASELINE_RULES` to data-driven manifest per TF-020P-001's scope. Filed at 023B R3 R3-MIN-SAFE-002.\nSTATUS.md:247:- **TF-023C-001** (medium priority): SCP self-dogfood — opt the SCP repo's own `policy-check-wrapper.yml` self-test into `scorecard-emit: true` so the aggregator has a 1-adopter test corpus before real adopters arrive. Target slice 023E (or earlier).\nSTATUS.md:248:- **TF-023C-002** (low priority): cron-health monitor — alert when `scorecard-aggregator.yml` hasn't produced a fresh index in >2 weeks. Target slice 023E or post-Threshold-A maintenance.\nSTATUS.md:249:- **TF-023C-003** (low priority): rate-limit handling for large estate. Filed at 023C R1 completeness CG-nit-002.\nSTATUS.md:250:- **TF-023C-004** (low priority): aggregator job `timeout-minutes` constraint. Filed at 023C R1 safety nit-SAFE-004.\nSTATUS.md:251:- **TF-023C-005** (forward-compat): SCP repo rename/transfer — update the regex anchor in `schemas/scorecard-opt-in-registry.schema.json` + `SCP_WORKFLOW_REF_PREFIX` constant. Filed at 023C R1 safety MAJ-SAFE-001 closure.\nSTATUS.md:252:- **TF-023C-006** (low priority): Minimum `scp_version` check on verified emits. An adopter pinning a very old SCP version remains 'verified' since the aggregator is informational-not-authoritative (invariant 1); revisit if estate-wide drift becomes material. Filed at 023C R1 safety MIN-SAFE-002.\nSTATUS.md:253:- **TF-023C-007** (low priority): Adopter wrapper filename constraint (must be `policy-check.yml`) — document at slice 023D ADOPT-001 §13 onboarding. Filed at 023C R1 completeness CG-MIN-006.\nSTATUS.md:254:- **TF-023D-001** (low priority): `scp.audit_scorecard_changed` MCP method (write-side). Plan-doc §1 names this as forward-looking; 023D ships only the read-only `consult_scorecard`. Out of scope per invariant 5 (read-only); revisit only if a write surface emerges as necessary. Filed at 023D DISPATCH-NOTE forward-looking.\nSTATUS.md:255:- **TF-023D-002** (low priority): markdown report retention policy — keep last 90 days; compact older. Defer until ~Q3 2026 (~13 weekly reports accumulated). Filed at 023D DISPATCH-NOTE forward-looking.\nSTATUS.md:256:- **TF-023D-003** (medium priority): `_log_tool_invocation` carries `key_id=\"pending_021J\"` for every MCP tool — pre-existing audit-trail gap. consult_scorecard exposes the gap because it's the first MCP method exposing aggregated estate-wide data. Closure path: replace with active key_id from `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` before slice 023E / Threshold A sign-off. Filed at 023D R1 safety MAJ-SAFE-001.\nSTATUS.md:257:- **TF-023D-004** (medium priority): drift section in markdown report — plan-doc §5 + DISPATCH-NOTE AC (i) named it. Deferred at 023D because real adopter data is needed to compute drift (until 023E onboards adopters, no drift to surface). Closure path: at slice 023E or first weekly run with ≥2 verified adopters, implement either prior-markdown-comparison or prior-index-comparison. Filed at 023D R1 completeness CMP-MAJ-001.\nSTATUS.md:258:- **TF-023D-005** (low priority): MCP server redeploy — `scp.consult_scorecard` MCP method registration is a code change; the deployed MCP server at acc.brokapps.ai requires a redeploy to make the method callable by agents. Closure path: bundle with next ACC deployment cycle. Filed at 023D R1 completeness CMP-MIN-003.\nSTATUS.md:259:- **TF-023E-001** (medium priority): SCP-self scorecard-emit opt-in is **deferred** until `standards-control-plane-` becomes public OR transfers to an org. GitHub blocks `actions/attest-build-provenance` on user-owned private repos with \"Feature not available for user-owned private repositories\" — D-042's trust model requires every emit to carry an OIDC attestation, and a self-exemption would weaken it. Surface impact: TF-023C-001 (1-adopter test corpus via SCP-self) cannot close at slice 023E; first real adopter must be public/org-owned (likely FLA, mapp-doc-agent, or an org-owned ACC/CT subrepo). Closure path: (a) make the SCP repo public, OR (b) transfer to an org, OR (c) accept SCP-self perpetually as `verification_failure` in the index (rejected at 023E fix-round-3 — degrades trust signal). Surfaced at 023E CI fix-round-3 (the first PR to set `scorecard-emit: true` on the wrapper failed at the attestation step with the GitHub error message). Cross-references USER-GATE-D criterion (i) carve-out.\nSTATUS.md:260:- **TF-023E-002** (medium priority): SCP-self wrapper SHA pin is **stuck at v1.0.0 (@41a5299)** — bumping to any post-WP-SCP-023 SHA produces `startup_failure` because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation) against the caller's ceiling. The `attest-scorecard` job in `policy-check.yml@5ff2acd` declares `attestations: write` + `id-token: write`, which exceeds the wrapper's `contents:read + statuses:write` ceiling, even when `scorecard-emit: false` would skip the job at runtime. Closure path: (a) restructure `policy-check.yml` so `attest-scorecard` lives in a separate top-level workflow file (called workflows can't have job-scoped perms above caller ceiling regardless of `if:`), OR (b) once TF-023E-001 unblocks (repo public/org-owned), grant `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` universally at the wrapper level. (a) preserves least-privilege for opt-out adopters and is the recommended path. Surfaced at 023E fix-round-3 (the bumped wrapper failed startup_failure even after reverting `scorecard-emit: true` because the SHA bump alone trips the validation). Real adopters that opt in MUST follow the (b) path because they will universally grant the two permissions per ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 step 2.\nSTATUS.md:261:\nSTATUS.md:262:## Tracked-forward items from 020H.4 (rule-config canary)\nSTATUS.md:263:\nSTATUS.md:264:- **TF-020H4-001**: Extend `scripts/replay-canary.sh` registry tuple to include `expected_disabled_rules_count` field. Current tuple (verdict, findings, waivers) catches the primary regression class (suppress stops working → deny fires → conclusion=FAILURE + findings>=1) but misses a \"suppress-still-works-but-observability-record-dropped\" regression class. Closure path: extend the registry tuple to a 6th field, add a parse + verify branch in the script, update existing entries with the baseline disabled_rules counts. No deadline (forward-compat). Filed at 020H.4 R1 safety SAFE-MIN-003 + completeness COMP-MIN-001 closure.\nSTATUS.md:265:- **TF-020H4-002**: Repository Ruleset matching `canary/*` blocking merge to `main` from any `canary/` branch. Currently the suppression-canary PRs (Canary 3 PR + Canary 4 PR #81) are CI-green (the gate suppresses) and the only merge barrier is the DO-NOT-MERGE label + operator discipline. Bus-factor-1 risk: a single accidental click would merge a canary into main. Closure path: when a second maintainer onboards (D-031 escalation, 2026-07-21 review), add a `scp-canary-no-merge-to-main` ruleset. Forward-compat — single-operator mode at v1.0.0 mitigates this risk via the same operator running both halves. Filed at 020H.4 R1 safety SAFE-MAJ-001 closure (architectural framing) + SAFE-nit-002 (canary branch protection).\nSTATUS.md:266:- **TF-020H4-003**: `scripts/replay-canary.sh` error-handling hardening — (a) the `-1` sentinel for failed `gh run download` produces ambiguous output (REGRESSION rows could be either real drift or download failure); explicit ERROR rows would disambiguate; (b) `--measure-cold-start` mode dispatches a workflow run + sleeps 5 + reads \"latest\" with no race-protection — under concurrent invocations the wrong run could be read. Both pre-exist 020H.4 (landed in 020E.c) but surfaced by this slice's R1 safety review. Closure path: a hardening pass on replay-canary.sh in a future canary-touch slice. No deadline. Filed at 020H.4 R1 safety SAFE-MIN-001 + SAFE-MIN-002.\nSTATUS.md:267:\nSTATUS.md:268:## Recent decisions\nSTATUS.md:269:\nSTATUS.md:270:- **D-029 (2026-04-29)** — `policy-check.yml` permissions block adds `statuses: write` for the read-back commit-status.\nSTATUS.md:271:- **D-030 (2026-04-30)** — apply 020J protections (tag-protection v* + required-signed-commits on main); idempotent applier at `scripts/configure-020j-protections.sh`.\nSTATUS.md:272:- **D-031 (2026-04-30)** — adopt 020K personal-account / single-operator CODEOWNERS path.\nSTATUS.md:273:- **D-032 (2026-04-30)** — apply 020D2 required-status-check + enforce_admins=true branch protection.\nSTATUS.md:274:- **D-033 (2026-04-30)** — 020D2.1 reconciliation: required-check context renamed to `policy-check / scp/policy-check` (the rendered Actions check-run name); single-operator review shape corrected to `count=0` + `codeowner=false` (GitHub forbids PR self-review, locking out the operator under count=1).\nSTATUS.md:275:- **D-034 (2026-04-30)** — 020F renovate-tag-protection: parallel ruleset on `refs/tags/renovate/v*` (deletion / non_fast_forward / update blocked, `enforcement: active`, `bypass_actors: []`). Closes 020F R1 safety review CRIT-SAFE-001.\nSTATUS.md:276:- **D-035 (2026-04-30)** — 020G adopter-helper invocation procedure as estate doctrine: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` two-call PUT + POST shape, refuses CI, preserves `required_pull_request_reviews`, mandatory invocation-log commit at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`.\nSTATUS.md:277:- **D-036 (2026-05-01)** — `policies/VERSIONING.md` MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH semver contract with one-release deprecation ramp AND `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/` RFC-lite process (quorum=1, 48h wall-clock window, auto-defer on zero approvals, **non-waivable window for bypass-introducing proposals** per 020H.1 R1 SAFE-MAJ-001 closure) adopted as estate doctrine. Closes WP-SCP-020 §4 020H.1 (i)+(ii)+(iii) and BS-5.\nSTATUS.md:278:- **D-037 (2026-05-01)** — Grant `issues: write` (job-level scope) to the `release-gate-violation-issue` job in `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` per slice 020H.3.1. The release-gate evaluation job remains `contents: read` only; the new job fires solely on `needs.release-gate.result == 'failure' && github.event_name == 'push'`. Symmetric with D-029 (020C.1 `statuses: write` for readback). Closes WP-SCP-022 020H.3.1 R1 SAFE-MIN-003 + SAFE-MAJ-001.\nSTATUS.md:279:- **D-038 (2026-05-02)** — Adopt hash-pinned Python supply-chain installs across the SCP federation primitive's two YAML/JSON-validating workflows per slice 020M (`requirements/policy-check.{in,txt}`; `pip install --require-hashes`). PATCH bump v1.0.0 → v1.0.1. Closes TF-020H3rg-002.\nSTATUS.md:280:- **D-039 (2026-05-02)** — Extend the slice 020M hash-pinned Python supply-chain install pattern to the SCP-self conflict-gate workflow per slice 020N (`requirements/conflict-gate.{in,txt}`; `pip install --require-hashes` + `--no-deps` ct-auth + `--no-deps -e .`). No semver bump (conflict-gate.yml is internal-only per VERSIONING.md §\"Scope\"). Closes TF-020M-001.\nSTATUS.md:281:- **D-040 (2026-05-02)** — Amend rule-RFC process so 48h is a CEILING (auto-defer trigger) not a FLOOR (minimum wait time) **in single-operator mode** (D-031 default at v1.0.0). Operator may merge as soon as adversarial-review fixpoint reached AND PR is open with `scp-rule-proposal` label. The non-waivable 48h MINIMUM for bypass-introducing proposals (020H.1 R1 SAFE-MAJ-001) is preserved. When 2nd maintainer onboards (D-031 escalation), 48h becomes mandatory MINIMUM. Surfaced by 020L dogfood when operator review of merge-readiness identified the wall-clock pause as theatre rather than safety in single-operator mode (no second pair of eyes for the pause to enable). Symmetric with D-033's \"operational reality must amend the spec\" pattern.\nSTATUS.md:282:- **D-041 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard data shape (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` v0.1) + opt-in adopter participation model per WP-SCP-023 023B. MAJOR-pinned schema; default-false `scorecard-emit: bool` workflow_call input; OIDC artifact attestation via `actions/attest-build-provenance@v4.1.0`; aggregator verifies at slice 023C via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`. NEVER carries waiver content (invariant 2 enforced by schema's `additionalProperties: false`). v1.1.0 → v1.2.0 (MINOR per VERSIONING.md additive-opt-in). Closes plan-doc §9 D-041 reservation.\nSTATUS.md:283:- **D-042 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard aggregator pipeline trust model per WP-SCP-023 023C. Per-emit verification via `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow <expected_workflow_ref>` (mandatory `job_workflow_ref` constraint pre-committed at 023A R2 MAJ-SAFE-R2-001 closure); index trust rooted in git's required-signed-commits + CODEOWNERS + branch protection (NOT a separate Ed25519 layer; Sigstore/Fulcio uses Ed25519 under the hood, managed by GitHub). Two-job permission split (aggregate read-only + commit write-scoped) mirrors 023B's `attest-scorecard` job pattern. Internal-only; no semver bump. Closes plan-doc §9 D-042 reservation.\nSTATUS.md:284:- **D-043 (2026-05-03)** — Adopt the cross-repo scorecard exposure surface — markdown report + MCP method `scp.consult_scorecard` — per WP-SCP-023 023D. Markdown generator at `scripts/generate-scorecard-report.py` (deterministic golden-file-tested). MCP method has read-only contract per plan-doc invariant 5 (request: `repo_filter?` + `since_emitted_at?`; response: aggregated counts only, never waiver content per invariant 2; Pydantic-enforced field whitelist). ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 documents the adopter onboarding workflow. Closes plan-doc §9 D-043 reservation.\nSTATUS.md:285:\nSTATUS.md:286:## Post-Threshold-A backlog\nSTATUS.md:287:\nSTATUS.md:288:> **Naming note (per 020H.3 + 020H.3.1 disambiguation):** \"020H **part** 3\" (no dot, with the word \"part\") is the pre-Threshold-A v1.0.0-cut sequence slice that landed at PR #75 / commit `347fde2` (ADOPT-001 §12 federation appendix). \"020H**.**3\" (with dot) is the post-Threshold-A dot-N follow-up that landed at PR #79 / commit `42f49db` (release-gate workflow). \"020H**.**3.1\" (with two dots) is the reconciliation follow-up at this PR (release-gate auto-issue). The dot-N convention extends infinitely (020H.4, 020H.5, ...); the `part N` series is closed at part 3 (Threshold A).\nSTATUS.md:289:\nSTATUS.md:290:- ~~**020E.b**: post-protection canary evidence~~ ✅ landed 2026-04-30 (PR #66, commit `8248732`).\nSTATUS.md:291:- ~~**020E.c**: waiver-suppression canary + `scripts/replay-canary.sh`~~ ✅ landed 2026-04-30 (PR #70, commit `4962bc9`); needed 2-PR fixpoint dance for warn-msg conftest bug.\nSTATUS.md:292:- ~~**020F**: Renovate shared preset~~ ✅ landed 2026-04-30 (PR #71, commit `2743d4a`); 4-round R1 fixpoint surfaced CRIT-SAFE-001 (renovate/v* unprotected) → D-034 + new ruleset live; preset published at `renovate/v1.0.0`.\nSTATUS.md:293:- ~~**020G**: branch-protection automation script for adopter onboarding~~ ✅ landed 2026-04-30 (PR #74, commit `373bcd2`); fix-round-1 closed 11 R1 findings + R2 + R3 + R4 fixpoint.\nSTATUS.md:294:- ~~**020H part 3**: ADOPT-001 §12 federation-integration appendix (closes TF-D1-001..003)~~ ✅ landed 2026-04-30 (PR #75, commit `347fde2`); 6-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R3 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on all 3 lenses), 11 MAJ + 31 MIN + 11 nit closed. Opened TF-020H3-001..005.\nSTATUS.md:295:- ~~**020H.1**: VERSIONING.md + rule-RFC process + rollback detection + version-manifest.json + freshness-warning emit~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #78, commit `06c2b61`); 2-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on all 3 lenses), 6 MAJ + 17 MIN + 11 nit closed. Filed D-036 + opened TF-020H1-001..005. Closed SCP-073.sec (SECURITY.md published).\nSTATUS.md:296:- ~~**020H.2**: Regal binary SHA256 verification — closes TF-020H3-001~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #77, commit `bac1427`); 3-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ), 3 MAJ + 5 MIN + 13 nit closed; closed 13 days ahead of the 2026-05-14 deadline.\nSTATUS.md:297:- ~~**020H.3**: release-gate workflow (closes TF-005 + TF-020H1-001)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #79, commit `42f49db`); 2-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on all 3 lenses), 1 CRIT + 7 MAJ + 10 MIN + 10 nit closed across 2 fix-rounds. Architectural framing: workflow is observer/annotator (post-tag), not pre-emptive gate; pre-emptive enforcement is the operator's mandatory dry-run pre-flight discipline. Opened TF-020H3rg-001..003.\nSTATUS.md:298:- ~~**020H.3.1**: release-gate auto-issue (closes TF-020H3rg-003)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #80, commit `d3e3c73`); 2-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 with R2 safety clean APPROVED (0 findings), 1 MAJ + 8 MIN + 6 nit + 1 fix-round-1 self-correction closed. Two-job split: release-gate (contents:read) + release-gate-violation-issue (issues:write at job level per D-037). Filed TF-020H3rg-004.\nSTATUS.md:299:- ~~**020H.4**: rule-config disable canary (closes TF-020H1-004)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #82, commit `c67a91a`); 2-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on all 3 lenses), 1 MAJ + 6 MIN + 8 nit closed. New `canary/rule-config-disabled` branch (PR #81 DO-NOT-MERGE; SHA `841d350`) verified PASS at workflow run `25211284467`; `scripts/replay-canary.sh` registry extended; `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/canary-evidence.md` Canary 4 baseline section added. Suppression-path coverage triad complete (deny / waiver / rule-config). Opened TF-020H4-001..003.\nSTATUS.md:300:- ~~**SCP-073.sec**: `SECURITY.md` publication (security disclosure path for policy-bypass reports)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 in 020H.1 fix-round-1 (commit `3817384`); `SECURITY.md` at repo root with GitHub Security Advisory + `jimbrooke@me.com` channels, 3-business-day SLA, 30-day coordinated-disclosure target; ADOPT-001 §12.7.8 + `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/rule-regression.md` updated to reference it directly. Closes WP-SCP-020 §4.1 SCP-073.sec forward-looking flag.\nSTATUS.md:301:- ~~**TF-020H3rg-002**: pip install --require-hashes for both YAML/JSON-validating workflows~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-02 in slice 020M (PR #84, commit `0e24cc6`); cut v1.0.1 PATCH.\nSTATUS.md:302:- ~~**WP-SCP-022 proposal-queue**: structured proposal queue for new rules.~~ ✅ Phase 1 closed 2026-05-02 in slice **020L** (PR #89, commit `25db685`) — RFC-001 / SCP-R-004 (waiver `reason` must cite issue/PR URL) authored, R1+R2 fixpoint, merged via operator-discretion early-merge per D-040. ✅ **Phase 2** closed 2026-05-02 in slice **020P** (PR #91, commit `d83ce52`) — `policies/SCP-R-004.rego` + 21 Conftest tests + conflict-gate fixtures + workflow warn-baseline rendering + ADOPT-001 §12.7.14 + RULE-TEMPLATE.md §5 + README.md §3 amendments + **v1.1.0 tag cut** (`https://github.com/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/releases/tag/v1.1.0`). Closes TF-020L-002 + TF-020L-003. Filed TF-020P-001/002/003/004/005.\nSTATUS.md:303:- **WP-SCP-023**: cross-repo scorecards.\nSTATUS.md:304:- **WP-SCP-024**: estate cascade (FLA pilot → PIM/recommender/etc.).\nSTATUS.md:305:\nSTATUS.md:306:## Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras\nSTATUS.md:307:\nSTATUS.md:308:- **FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001** (open): per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC. install_acc_hook.sh currently hardcodes ROOT_DIR via BASH_SOURCE so each adopter repo would need its own install ceremony. 024C MUST NOT open until closed. ACC-side work item; SCP-side awaits closure. Owner: @jrnb2024.\nSTATUS.md:309:- **FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001** (open): 024B-extras workflow wiring will hardcode `--tooling-slice-id` per workflow file and omit `--allow-not-applicable` from cohort workflows, closing the residual operator-supplied `not applicable` bypass surface. 024B-core keeps the CLI guard + documentation only; the workflow-side hardcoding is the canonical closure path.\nSTATUS.md:310:- **TF-024B-SCAFFOLDER-023E002-UPDATE** (open): when TF-023E-002 closes, remove the post-v1.2.0 warning block from `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` and delete the cutover ancestry guard that keeps the v1.0.0 fallback recommendation alive. The scaffolder should stop warning only after the separate `attest-scorecard` workflow restructuring lands. Owner: @jrnb2024.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1:# ADOPT-001 — Standards Control Plane Project Onboarding\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:2:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:3:**Version:** 0.1\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:4:**Status:** Active\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:5:**Date:** 2026-04-12\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:6:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:7:## 1. Purpose\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:8:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:9:This is the single onboarding brief for any repo that wants to adopt the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:10:Standards Control Plane.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:11:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:12:If a team asks, \"What do we need to change to use SCP in our repo, wire it into\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:13:CI, and update our governance docs?\", point them here.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:14:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:15:The goal is not to redesign the adopter repo. The goal is to plug SCP into the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:16:repo's existing delivery process in a way that is:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:17:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:18:- structured\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:19:- reviewable\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:20:- advisory first\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:21:- easy to run locally and in CI\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:22:- compatible with stronger existing repo governance\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:23:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:24:Repos that host an HTTP service audited by SCP also take on the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:25:service-lifecycle adoption obligation: `services.yml` must declare an\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:26:`auth_contract` block conforming to SVC-003 (see §11).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:27:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:28:## 2. What Adopting Teams Get\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:29:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:30:After onboarding, a project should be able to:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:31:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:32:1. ask for targeted standards guidance before coding\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:33:2. run changed-file audit in PR workflows\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:34:3. run full or subsystem audit on a schedule\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:35:4. keep findings, waivers, and reports in a consistent shape\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:36:5. layer repo-specific standards on top of the shared registry\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:37:6. publish CI-facing and Control Tower-facing outputs without a second audit path\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:38:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:39:## 3. Estate Best-Practice Position\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:40:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:41:Adopt SCP using the same broad discipline already proven across Control Tower,\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:42:Documentation Intelligence, and the estate conformance work:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:43:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:44:- use a shared standard, not copy-pasted local folklore\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:45:- extract and reuse proven patterns rather than inventing a second mechanism\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:46:- keep the integration layer thin; do not refactor core business logic just to\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:47:  \"make SCP fit\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:48:- keep audit local to the repo that owns the code\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:49:- keep findings structured and durable; markdown is a projection, not the source\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:50:  of truth\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:51:- keep the rollout advisory first; do not introduce hard CI blocking at\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:52:  adoption time\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:53:- keep project overlays explicit instead of weakening the shared standard into\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:54:  vague prose\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:55:- keep the existing repo governance protocol if it is stronger; SCP supplements\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:56:  governance, it does not replace it\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:57:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:58:## 4. Governance Rules Teams Must Preserve\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:59:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:60:The minimum expected governance posture for adopters is:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:61:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:62:1. do not silently descope\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:63:2. do not skip the repo's existing review process\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:64:3. every SCP finding is resolved, waived, accepted, marked false positive, or\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:65:   explicitly deferred by the repo's normal governance path\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:66:4. docs and control records are updated in the same session as code changes\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:67:5. git stays clean: branch, PR, merge, and artifact ownership remain explicit\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:68:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:69:If a repo already follows the stronger Control Tower delivery protocol with\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:70:parallel adversarial review, keep using it.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:71:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:72:## 5. Recommended Deployment Model\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:73:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:74:Use this deployment model unless there is a strong repo-specific reason not to:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:75:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:76:### 5.1 Package and CLI first\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:77:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:78:Install SCP as a Python tool dependency in the adopter repo and call it through\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:79:CLI commands in local workflows and CI.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:80:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:81:This is the default and recommended mode.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:82:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:83:### 5.2 Repo-local audit\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:84:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:85:Run `audit-changed` and `audit` inside the target repo, not in a central shared\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:86:service. The repo that owns the code should own extraction, normalisation, and\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:87:artifact generation.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:88:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:89:### 5.3 Optional shared consult service\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:90:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:91:If teams want a shared consult endpoint, run `serve` against a Control Tower\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:92:OIDC audience and use it for consult and registry access. Do not move the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:93:canonical audit runtime there yet. Raw `--auth-token` bearer auth is\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:94:deprecated — machine callers should use Control Tower agent keys\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:95:(`mode.api_key`). See §11.6 for the mode-selection guide and §11.7 for\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:96:the bearer deprecation window.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:97:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:98:### 5.4 Control Tower consumes artifacts\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:99:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:100:Control Tower should read the emitted artifacts. It should not invoke evaluator\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:101:runtime directly.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:102:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:103:### 5.5 Docs-agent remains optional\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:104:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:105:Docs-agent is a future enrichment layer for broader retrieval and historical\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:106:evidence. It is not required for base onboarding.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:107:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:108:## 6. Pre-Onboarding Decisions\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:109:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:110:Before implementation begins, each adopting repo must decide the following:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:111:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:112:| Decision | Why it matters |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:113:|----------|----------------|\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:114:| **Repo owner** | Owns the adoption and follow-up fixes |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:115:| **Governance owner** | Owns waivers, accepted debt, and process wording |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:116:| **Overlay owner** | Owns repo-specific standards and overlay drift |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:117:| **Pilot subsystem** | Gives consult and audit a bounded first target |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:118:| **Primary domains** | Start with `governance,architecture` unless there is a specific reason not to |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:119:| **CI owner** | Wires PR and scheduled audit jobs |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:120:| **Agent instruction file** | Defines where consult-before-coding will be added (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, or equivalent) |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:121:| **Service mode decision** | Decide whether local CLI is enough or whether the repo wants the optional HTTP service |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:122:| **Service auth modes (SVC-003)** | If the repo hosts an HTTP service audited by SCP, decide which of the four approved `auth_contract` modes it accepts (see §11). `mode.user_oidc` for browsers, `mode.api_key` for machine callers, `mode.service_rs256` for S2S, `mode.bearer_legacy` only with a time-bound migration waiver |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:123:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:124:## 7. Required Repo Changes\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:125:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:126:Every adopter should make the following changes.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:127:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:128:### 7.1 Install SCP as a pinned tool dependency\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:129:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:130:Until SCP is published to an internal package index, the simplest path is to pin\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:131:the GitHub repo:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:132:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:133:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:134:pip install \"git+https://github.com/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane.git@main\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:135:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:136:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:137:Best practice:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:138:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:139:- pin the Git reference or released version explicitly\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:140:- do not install from a floating local copy in CI\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:141:- keep SCP version changes visible in dependency review\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:142:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:143:Installing SCP pulls in a small transitive closure at runtime. The\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:144:load-bearing runtime dependencies are:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:145:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:146:- `fastapi`, `uvicorn`, `httpx` — the HTTP surface\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:147:- `jsonschema>=4.25.0` — schema validation\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:148:- `pyyaml>=6.0` — `services.yml` parsing (required once SVC-001/002/003\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:149:  are in use; see §11)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:150:- `pydantic>=2.12.0`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:151:- the vendored `ct_auth-0.8.0` wheel — Control Tower OIDC + BFF helpers\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:152:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:153:No action is required beyond `pip install` — but teams with locked\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:154:dependency sets should know these are on the list before SCP lands.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:155:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:156:### 7.2 Add a repo-local overlay\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:157:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:158:Create a repo-local overlay directory so project-specific rules and patterns can\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:159:sharpen the shared registry without editing SCP core.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:160:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:161:Recommended location:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:162:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:163:```text\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:164:governance/standards-control-plane/\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:165:  standards-index.json\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:166:  architecture/\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:167:    index.json\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:168:    rules/\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:169:    patterns/\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:170:  governance/\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:171:    index.json\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:172:    rules/\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:173:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:174:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:175:Use overlays for:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:176:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:177:- repo-specific boundary rules\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:178:- stricter severity for already-shared rules\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:179:- approved local patterns\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:180:- project terminology or subsystem tags\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:181:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:182:Do not use overlays for:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:183:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:184:- broad restatement of the shared registry\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:185:- undocumented local preferences with no owner\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:186:- hiding or weakening shared standards that should remain estate-wide\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:187:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:188:### 7.3 Add thin wrapper scripts\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:189:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:190:Do not scatter raw long CLI invocations across prompts, READMEs, and CI files.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:191:Create repo-local wrapper scripts with the repo's fixed defaults.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:192:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:193:Recommended wrappers:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:194:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:195:```text\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:196:scripts/scp-consult\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:197:scripts/scp-audit-pr\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:198:scripts/scp-audit-full\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:199:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:200:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:201:Those wrappers should own:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:202:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:203:- subsystem default\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:204:- overlay path\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:205:- standards version\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:206:- any repo-specific request-file path\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:207:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:208:### 7.4 Add findings and waiver ownership\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:209:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:210:The repo must own these artifacts:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:211:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:212:- `output/findings/waivers.json`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:213:- `output/findings/open-findings.json`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:214:- `output/findings/findings-history.json`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:215:- `output/findings/area-summaries/*.json`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:216:- `output/reports/latest-review.md`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:217:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:218:Best practice:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:219:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:220:- commit waivers and long-lived findings/history artifacts through normal PR flow\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:221:- treat PR-scoped CI summaries as build artifacts, not as mandatory committed files\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:222:- keep waiver approvals explicit and time-bound\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:223:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:224:### 7.5 Update governance docs\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:225:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:226:Every adopter should update:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:227:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:228:- `CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, or equivalent agent instruction file\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:229:- repo governance protocol or delivery guide\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:230:- PR template or delivery checklist if one exists\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:231:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:232:## 8. Governance Doc Wording to Add\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:233:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:234:At minimum, the adopting repo should add a section equivalent to this:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:235:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:236:```text\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:237:## Standards Control Plane Usage\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:238:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:239:Before implementation:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:240:1. Identify impacted subsystem, area, and files.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:241:2. Run SCP consult for the relevant domains.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:242:3. Read applicable rules, approved patterns, and open findings.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:243:4. Summarise the implementation plan against those constraints before coding.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:244:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:245:Before PR or handoff:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:246:1. Run SCP changed-file audit.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:247:2. Review findings and fix them where required.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:248:3. Record waivers or accepted debt explicitly; do not silently bypass findings.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:249:4. Keep generated findings and report artifacts aligned with the code change.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:250:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:251:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:252:If the repo already has stronger governance language, integrate SCP into that\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:253:language rather than replacing it.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:254:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:255:## 9. Agent Workflow Teams Should Adopt\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:256:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:257:This is the expected operating loop for implementation agents:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:258:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:259:1. identify impacted subsystem, area, and likely changed files\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:260:2. run `consult` (include `service-lifecycle` in `domains` when the repo\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:261:   hosts an HTTP service or when the change touches `services.yml`)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:262:3. read:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:263:   - applicable rules\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:264:   - approved patterns\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:265:   - open findings\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:266:   - relevant historical review references\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:267:4. summarise the plan against those constraints\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:268:5. implement\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:269:6. run `audit-changed`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:270:7. fix findings or explicitly record exceptions through the repo's governance path\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:271:8. only then open or update the PR\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:272:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:273:SCP should become part of the normal pre-coding and pre-PR loop. It should not\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:274:be a late afterthought.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:275:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:276:## 10. CI Integration\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:277:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:278:### 10.1 PR workflow\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:279:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:280:Each adopting repo should add a non-blocking PR job that runs changed-file audit.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:281:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:282:Recommended command shape:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:283:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:284:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:285:standards-control-plane audit-changed \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:286:  --base-ref origin/main \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:287:  --head-ref HEAD \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:288:  --domains governance,architecture \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:289:  --subsystem <subsystem> \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:290:  --standards-version <registry-version> \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:291:  --overlay governance/standards-control-plane \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:292:  --write-output\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:293:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:294:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:295:Then publish:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:296:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:297:- `output/ci/latest-ci.json`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:298:- `output/ci/latest-ci.md`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:299:- `output/reports/latest-review.md`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:300:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:301:Do not fail the build on day one. Warnings should be visible first.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:302:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:303:### 10.2 Scheduled workflow\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:304:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:305:Each adopting repo should also add a scheduled job for broader refresh:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:306:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:307:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:308:standards-control-plane audit \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:309:  --request governance/scp/audit-request.json \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:310:  --overlay governance/standards-control-plane \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:311:  --write-output\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:312:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:313:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:314:Recommended cadence:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:315:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:316:- nightly for fast-moving repos\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:317:- weekly for slower repos\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:318:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:319:### 10.3 Control Tower projection\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:320:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:321:If the repo participates in estate-level reporting, publish or expose:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:322:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:323:- `output/control-tower/surface.json`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:324:- `output/control-tower/estate-dashboard.json`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:325:- `output/control-tower/subsystems/*.json`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:326:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:327:## 11. Service Auth Contract (SVC-003)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:328:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:329:SVC-003 defines a closed four-mode auth contract every estate service\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:330:must declare in its `services.yml`. This section has two tracks:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:331:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:332:- **Consumer track (§11.2)** — adopters who only *call* SCP's HTTP\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:333:  service (or any other estate service). Read §11.1 and §11.2 and\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:334:  skip the producer subsections.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:335:- **Producer track (§11.3–§11.8)** — adopters who *host* an HTTP\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:336:  service audited by SCP. Read everything: the services.yml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:337:  declaration shape, per-mode guidance, the `--auth-token`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:338:  deprecation window, and the upgrade path from pre-SVC-003\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:339:  manifests.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:340:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:341:SCP's own `services.yml` at repo root and `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-019/\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:342:dogfood-scp.md` are the canonical producer example.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:343:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:344:> **Operative close date update — 2026-04-20.** Per SCP's Option-B\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:345:> signal (`docs/reviews/WP-SCP-019/d019-option-b-signal.md`, filed\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:346:> 2026-04-20), the estate-wide `mode.bearer_legacy` deprecation close\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:347:> date has **operationally slid from 2026-06-30 to 2026-09-30** for\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:348:> consumer-team planning and outbound comms from 2026-04-20 forward.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:349:> The formal amending decision (D-021) records on 2026-05-31 with\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:350:> observed adoption-PR evidence substituted. D-019's 2026-06-30\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:351:> citation in this section, the `deprecation_close_date` example\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:352:> snippet in §11.7, and the SCP-specific close-date statement in\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:353:> §11.7 all remain as-ratified until D-021 fires — substitute\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:354:> `2026-09-30` when authoring new `services.yml` / `waivers.json`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:355:> entries from this signal forward. Threshold for the 2026-05-31\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:356:> check (whether Option B holds or D-019 stands) was CT-confirmed\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:357:> verbatim on 2026-04-20; corner cases §2.1–§2.3 in\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:358:> `SCP-CONFIRM-D-019-THRESHOLD-2026-04-20.md` apply.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:359:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:360:### 11.1 Approved modes (closed set)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:361:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:362:Custom modes are not permitted; a new mode requires a standards\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:363:change. The static evaluator scans for the implementation-marker\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:364:patterns listed below; Node/Go services must produce source patterns\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:365:matching the same substrings to satisfy the code-pattern scan.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:366:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:367:| Mode ID | Use | Shape | Implementation markers |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:368:|---------|-----|-------|------------------------|\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:369:| `mode.user_oidc` | Browser flows | Control Tower OIDC + JWKS verification + `aud=<app-id>` claim + httpOnly cookie session | `ControlTowerAuth`, `ct_auth.`, `create_bff_routes`, `CT_JWKS_URL` |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:370:| `mode.service_rs256` | Service-to-service (target state; replaces HS256) | S2S RS256 + required `aud` claim + JWKS verification | `algorithms=[\"RS256\"]`, `algorithms=['RS256']`, `algorithm=\"RS256\"`, `algorithm='RS256'` |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:371:| `mode.api_key` | Agents, CLIs, machine callers | Control Tower-issued agent key, revocable via CT, `X-API-Key` header | `X-API-Key`, `x-api-key` |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:372:| `mode.bearer_legacy` | Deprecated. Pre-SVC-003 raw bearer token | Requires per-service migration waiver with explicit `deprecation_close_date` | `secrets.compare_digest` |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:373:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:374:The reference implementation for `mode.user_oidc` is SCP's own\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:375:service at `src/standards_control_plane/service.py` (commit\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:376:`66ba8a4`): vendored `ct_auth` wheel, `ControlTowerAuth` with\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:377:`jwks_url` + `audience`, `create_bff_routes` for the cookie session\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:378:flow.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:379:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:380:### 11.2 Consumer track: calling SCP (or any SVC-003 service)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:381:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:382:Find the target service's `services.yml` (SCP's lives at the root of\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:383:`standards-control-plane`). The `auth_contract.accepted_modes` list\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:384:tells you which headers your caller must send.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:385:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:386:- **Browser**: perform the Control Tower OIDC login flow at the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:387:  service's `/auth/login`; subsequent requests carry the httpOnly\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:388:  cookie session the BFF sets. No explicit header from your code.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:389:- **Machine caller (`mode.api_key`)**: request an agent key from\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:390:  Control Tower's agent-key admin surface and send\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:391:  `X-API-Key: <key>` on every request. Keys are revocable via CT.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:392:- **Machine caller (`mode.bearer_legacy`, deprecated)**: during the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:393:  deprecation window (close date per D-019 is 2026-06-30), send\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:394:  `Authorization: Bearer <token>` using the token the target service\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:395:  configured via `--auth-token`. Plan your migration to\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:396:  `mode.api_key` before the close date — after it, SVC-003 fires\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:397:  `bearer-legacy-close-date-passed` on the target service.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:398:- **S2S caller (`mode.service_rs256`)**: mint an RS256 JWT with\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:399:  `aud` set to the target service's `services.yml` key and send it\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:400:  in the Authorization header.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:401:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:402:The producer subsections below describe the shape a service\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:403:publishes; as a consumer, you only need the declaration's mode list\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:404:and the issuance endpoint for each mode.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:405:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:406:### 11.3 Producer track: upgrading a pre-SVC-003 services.yml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:407:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:408:If your repo already has a `services.yml` from WP-SCP-018 or earlier\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:409:and it has no `auth_contract` block, SVC-003's auto-check will fire\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:410:`missing-auth-contract` against every non-planned service. The\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:411:minimum upgrade:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:412:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:413:1. Pick the auth mode(s) your service actually accepts today. If it\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:414:   still uses `--auth-token`, that is `mode.bearer_legacy` and needs\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:415:   the waiver shape in §11.7.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:416:2. Add the `auth_contract` block under each service's\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:417:   `runtime_contract` (see §11.4–§11.7 for per-mode shape).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:418:3. Run `standards-control-plane audit --request <your-request>.json\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:419:   --domains service-lifecycle` and address any findings.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:420:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:421:Upgrading one service at a time is supported — other services fire\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:422:their own `missing-auth-contract` until they are declared, but the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:423:rule scope is per-service.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:424:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:425:### 11.4 Producer track: mode.user_oidc\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:426:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:427:Register an OAuth client with Control Tower for each environment\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:428:(e.g. `my-app`, `my-app-dev`). Control Tower registration covers the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:429:redirect URIs and CORS origins; SCP's `docs/deployment.md` §3 is a\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:430:worked example for reference.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:431:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:432:Set runtime env vars on the service process:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:433:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:434:```text\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:435:AUTH_ENABLED=true\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:436:CT_BASE_URL=https://control-tower.brokapps.ai\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:437:CT_APP_ID=my-app-dev\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:438:PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://my-app-dev.brokapps.ai\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:439:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:440:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:441:`CT_JWKS_URL` is optional — if unset, it defaults to\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:442:`<CT_BASE_URL>/api/v1/.well-known/jwks.json`. Override only if your\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:443:Control Tower deployment publishes JWKS at a non-standard path.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:444:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:445:Declare the mode in `services.yml`. The `audience` value must match\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:446:the service's `services.yml` key in the target environment. SCP\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:447:solves the \"local key vs staging key\" mismatch by using distinct\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:448:service keys per environment (e.g. `scp-dev` locally, `scp` in\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:449:staging); adopters should do the same rather than using a shared\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:450:key with divergent audiences.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:451:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:452:```yaml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:453:services:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:454:  my-app-dev:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:455:    healthcheck: /health\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:456:    local:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:457:      status: ready\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:458:      runtime_contract:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:459:        # ... SVC-001 fields ...\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:460:        auth_contract:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:461:          accepted_modes:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:462:            - mode: mode.user_oidc\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:463:              audience: my-app-dev\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:464:              jwks_url: https://control-tower.brokapps.ai/api/v1/.well-known/jwks.json\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:465:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:466:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:467:In Python services, reuse the vendored `ct_auth` wheel:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:468:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:469:```python\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:470:from ct_auth.bff import create_bff_routes\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:471:from ct_auth.fastapi import ControlTowerAuth\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:472:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:473:auth = ControlTowerAuth(jwks_url=CT_JWKS_URL, audience=CT_APP_ID)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:474:create_bff_routes(app, auth=auth, ...)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:475:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:476:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:477:Node/Go services need the equivalent OIDC + JWKS implementation.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:478:The code-pattern scan is substring-based on the markers in the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:479:§11.1 table; non-Python services must emit matching patterns or\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:480:accept impl-missing findings as waivers.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:481:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:482:### 11.5 Producer track: mode.api_key\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:483:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:484:**Status (as of 2026-04-18):** ratified and admin-surface-live but\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:485:operational-doc pending. Adopters should not plan immediate\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:486:production migration to `mode.api_key` yet.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:487:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:488:Concretely, per the CT 2026-04-18 audit\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:489:(`control-tower/governance/docs/notifications/SCP-FOLLOWUP-2026-04-18-admin-ui-audit.md`):\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:490:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:491:- CT's service-account + API-key backend (`CT-016`) is shipped.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:492:- The admin UI (create / list / revoke / rotate service-account keys,\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:493:  7-day rotation overlap window, audit logging) is live today.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:494:- The **operational doc** (`CT_AGENT_KEY_OPS.md`) covering default\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:495:  expiry, rotation cadence, revocation path, scope model, audit-log\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:496:  format, and `mode.api_key` vs `mode.service_rs256` discrimination\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:497:  is **not yet published** — CT-led authoring, target mid-to-late\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:498:  May 2026.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:499:- Until the ops doc publishes, production adoption of `mode.api_key`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:500:  has undefined operational characteristics (key rotation timing,\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:501:  expiry defaults, rate limits). Declaring the mode is fine; routing\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:502:  real traffic through it is not advised.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:503:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:504:For services currently on `mode.bearer_legacy` with a deprecation\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:505:waiver, stay on the waiver track until the ops doc publishes. The\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:506:2026-05-31 D-019 checkpoint\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:507:(`docs/reviews/WP-SCP-019/d019-may31-checkpoint.md`) governs whether\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:508:the 2026-06-30 close date stands or is amended to 2026-09-30.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:509:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:510:When the ops doc publishes, request that Control Tower register the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:511:service (or SCP, if running a shared SCP instance) as an agent-key\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:512:issuer. SCP itself is tracked as an SCP-071 dependency.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:513:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:514:Declaration shape:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:515:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:516:```yaml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:517:auth_contract:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:518:  accepted_modes:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:519:    - mode: mode.api_key\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:520:      issuer: control-tower\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:521:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:522:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:523:Machine callers pass `X-API-Key: <key>` on every request. Agent keys\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:524:are issued and revoked via Control Tower's agent-key admin surface\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:525:(not via services.yml edits).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:526:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:527:### 11.6 Producer track: mode.service_rs256\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:528:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:529:Target state for in-estate S2S calls; replaces the HS256 tokens used\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:530:by pre-WP-SCP-019 services. The declaration shape matches\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:531:`mode.user_oidc` (audience + jwks_url):\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:532:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:533:```yaml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:534:auth_contract:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:535:  accepted_modes:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:536:    - mode: mode.service_rs256\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:537:      audience: my-app\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:538:      jwks_url: https://control-tower.brokapps.ai/api/v1/.well-known/jwks.json\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:539:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:540:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:541:Verifying services validate `aud == \"<services.yml key>\"` and the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:542:RS256 signature against the JWKS endpoint.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:543:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:544:### 11.7 Producer track: mode.bearer_legacy (deprecated)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:545:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:546:The `--auth-token <token>` flag that shipped in WP-SCP-018 is now\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:547:classified as `mode.bearer_legacy`. Services still using this path\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:548:must:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:549:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:550:1. Declare the mode in `services.yml` with both\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:551:   `deprecation_close_date` (an ISO date) and `waiver_ref` (the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:552:   `waiver_id` of a record in `output/findings/waivers.json`).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:553:2. Register the waiver in `output/findings/waivers.json` with\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:554:   `approved_by`, `created_at`, and `expires_at` at or before the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:555:   close date.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:556:3. Draft and track a migration plan to either `mode.api_key`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:557:   (Control Tower-issued agent keys, for most machine callers) or\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:558:   `mode.service_rs256` (CT-signed S2S JWT, for high-throughput or\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:559:   inter-service callers where a CT round-trip per request is a\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:560:   latency-budget problem) by the close date. `mode.bearer_legacy`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:561:   is a machine-caller path; migration target is NOT\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:562:   `mode.user_oidc` (which is a browser cookie session flow). Mode\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:563:   choice follows the throughput / latency heuristic CT carries in\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:564:   `CT_AGENT_KEY_OPS.md` §2.2 — `mode.service_rs256` is not\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:565:   operational today (CT authoring + JWKS + consumer helpers are\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:566:   scoped in SVC-003 but not shipped), so services picking that\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:567:   target declare `mode.bearer_legacy` with a waiver now and\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:568:   migrate when CT operationalises. Per-app migrations are tracked\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:569:   as separate work packages, not as WP-SCP-019 deliverables.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:570:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:571:`services.yml`:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:572:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:573:```yaml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:574:auth_contract:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:575:  accepted_modes:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:576:    - mode: mode.bearer_legacy\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:577:      deprecation_close_date: \"2026-06-30\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:578:      waiver_ref: my-app-bearer-legacy-migration\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:579:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:580:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:581:`output/findings/waivers.json`:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:582:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:583:```json\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:584:[\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:585:  {\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:586:    \"waiver_id\": \"my-app-bearer-legacy-migration\",\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:587:    \"finding_id\": \"F-SVC-003-<area>-<service>-<signal>\",\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:588:    \"reason\": \"Machine callers migrating from raw bearer to mode.api_key\",\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:589:    \"approved_by\": \"my-app-platform-owner\",\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:590:    \"created_at\": \"2026-04-18T00:00:00Z\",\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:591:    \"expires_at\": \"2026-06-30T23:59:59Z\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:592:  }\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:593:]\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:594:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:595:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:596:The `finding_id` in the waiver record is a placeholder shape —\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:597:substitute the real evaluator finding_id from a prior audit output\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:598:(format: `F-SVC-003-<area_id>-<service>-<signal_key>`).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:599:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:600:On or after the close date the SVC-003 evaluator fires\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:601:`bearer-legacy-close-date-passed-*` and the waiver must be renewed\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:602:(governance-approved) or the mode entry removed. If no waivers are\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:603:registered in `waivers.json` (file absent, empty list, or unparseable)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:604:the `bearer-legacy-waiver-not-found-*` check skips — the evaluator\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:605:treats pre-adoption state as \"not yet using the waiver system\" rather\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:606:than a hard fail.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:607:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:608:The estate-wide close date for SCP's own `--auth-token` path is\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:609:`2026-06-30` per D-019. Per-app close dates can be earlier but not\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:610:later without an amending decision row.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:611:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:612:### 11.8 Which mode to pick (producer track)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:613:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:614:- Browser users → `mode.user_oidc` (cookie session via `ct_auth` BFF)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:615:- Python / Node / CLI client hitting the HTTP API programmatically →\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:616:  `mode.api_key`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:617:- Service-to-service within the estate → `mode.service_rs256`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:618:- Only during migration off WP-SCP-018 `--auth-token` →\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:619:  `mode.bearer_legacy` with a time-bound waiver\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:620:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:621:Services may declare more than one mode. SCP itself declares\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:622:`[mode.user_oidc, mode.bearer_legacy]` during the migration window;\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:623:after the 2026-06-30 close date the latter comes out.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:624:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:625:### 11.9 Running SCP's HTTP service locally\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:626:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:627:If your team runs its own SCP instance (for team-scoped consult /\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:628:registry access), use the standard CLI form:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:629:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:630:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:631:standards-control-plane serve --host 127.0.0.1 --port 3787\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:632:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:633:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:634:With auth:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:635:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:636:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:637:AUTH_ENABLED=true CT_APP_ID=my-app-dev \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:638:  PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://my-app-dev.brokapps.ai \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:639:  standards-control-plane serve --host 127.0.0.1 --port 3787\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:640:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:641:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:642:See `docs/deployment.md` for the canonical runtime variable contract\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:643:and the Cloudflare dev-tunnel setup. Keep the canonical audit runtime\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:644:local to each repo — SCP's HTTP surface is for consult and registry\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:645:only.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:646:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:647:### 11.10 Caller-side rule override (`.scp/rule-config.yaml`)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:648:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:649:The `policy-check.yml` reusable workflow accepts a caller-side override\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:650:file at `.scp/rule-config.yaml` (configurable via the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:651:`rule-config-path:` input on `workflow_call`). Use this to disable an\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:652:SCP rule that doesn't fit your repo's context — but only with\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:653:intentional friction: the schema requires a justification + an\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:654:expiry, the disable is observable in every PR, and an expired disable\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:655:emits a workflow warning every run for one release as a deprecation\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:656:ramp.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:657:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:658:Schema: `schemas/rule-config.schema.json` (draft 2020-12,\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:659:`additionalProperties: false`).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:660:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:661:Minimum example:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:662:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:663:```yaml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:664:# .scp/rule-config.yaml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:665:rules:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:666:  SCP-R-002:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:667:    disable: true\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:668:    justification: \"Repo doesn't ship a waivers.json (no governed exceptions yet); revisit when SCP-R-002 surface broadens.\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:669:    expires_at: 2026-09-30\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:670:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:671:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:672:Required keys per rule entry:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:673:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:674:- `disable` (boolean) — when `true`, the rule's deny is suppressed.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:675:- `justification` (string, non-empty) — recorded in the audit trail\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:676:  and surfaced to PR reviewers.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:677:- `expires_at` (date or RFC 3339 date-time) — the disable's planned\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:678:  end-of-life. The schema accepts either form; the workflow normalises\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:679:  to UTC for the expiry comparison.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:680:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:681:Behaviour:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:682:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:683:- A `disable: true` entry suppresses the rule's deny *and* emits an\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:684:  observability record into `policy-check-summary.json`'s\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:685:  `disabled_rules:` list with `{rule_id, reason: \"rule-config\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:686:  override\", expires_at}`.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:687:- Each PR run also posts a sibling commit-status `scp/policy-check-readback`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:688:  with text like `\"3 rules enabled, 1 disabled: SCP-R-002 until 2026-09-30\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:689:  (rule-config override)\"` so reviewers see the bypass posture inline.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:690:- When `expires_at` is in the past, the disable still suppresses the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:691:  deny **for one release** as a deprecation ramp, but every PR run\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:692:  emits a `::warning::` annotation:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:693:  `SCP-R-NNN rule-config disable expired YYYY-MM-DD; remove or extend`.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:694:  Treat this as merge-soft-blocking — the team should either renew\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:695:  the disable with a fresh `expires_at` or remove the entry.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:696:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:697:When **not** to use rule-config:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:698:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:699:- Per-finding suppression — use a `waivers.json` waiver instead with a\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:700:  `finding_id`. Rule-config is rule-wide; waivers are per-finding.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:701:- \"Permanent\" disables — they are not. The schema requires\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:702:  `expires_at`. If your context structurally never matches a rule,\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:703:  open an issue against SCP for the rule definition itself rather\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:704:  than long-term-disabling it locally.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:705:- One-off PR exceptions — use `scp_bypass: true` on the workflow\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:706:  invocation per the **three-gate** break-glass procedure documented\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:707:  in §12.7.4 (CODEOWNERS approval + sibling D-NNN row + matching\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:708:  `waivers.json` entry — all three required simultaneously).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:709:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:710:**CODEOWNERS requirement (MUST).** CODEOWNERS protection on `.scp/rule-config.yaml` is required, not optional: a `disable: true` entry suppresses a rule's deny WITHOUT triggering the three-gate break-glass check (see §12.7.4), making `.scp/rule-config.yaml` a bypass-surface equivalent to `scp_bypass: true`. Without CODEOWNERS coverage, a single developer can silently disable any SCP rule. Minimum:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:711:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:712:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:713:.scp/rule-config.yaml @your-team-owners\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:714:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:715:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:716:## 12. Architecture Principles for Adopters\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:717:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:718:These are the key architectural principles teams should follow while adopting\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:719:SCP.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:720:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:721:### 12.1 Extract, do not reinvent\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:722:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:723:Use the shared registry, shared contracts, and shared outputs. Do not create a\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:724:repo-specific second standards engine.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:725:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:726:### 12.2 Thin integration only\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:727:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:728:Add wrapper scripts, CI jobs, overlays, and governance references. Do not\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:729:perform broad business-logic refactors just because the repo is onboarding SCP.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:730:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:731:### 12.3 One audit model\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:732:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:733:CI outputs, Control Tower outputs, and reports should all be projections from\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:734:the same audit result. Do not invent a separate CI-specific evaluator path.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:735:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:736:### 12.4 Structured artifacts first\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:737:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:738:Findings JSON, waivers JSON, audit results, and summaries are the durable\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:739:records. Markdown exists to help humans review those records.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:740:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:741:### 12.5 Explicit overlays\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:742:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:743:If the repo needs local specificity, express it through an explicit overlay with\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:744:an owner. Do not bake local assumptions into global SCP core.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:745:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:746:### 12.6 Deterministic checks before inference\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:747:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:748:Start by relying most heavily on governance and architecture signals that are\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:749:already deterministic or evidence-backed. Expand advisory use of UX, design, and\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:750:product only when the repo is comfortable with the confidence model.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:751:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:752:### 12.7 Federation primitive — adopter integration\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:753:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:754:This appendix is the canonical adopter-integration contract for the SCP\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:755:federation primitive at v1.0.0. It tells an adopter exactly what to add to\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:756:their repo, what to set on their branch protection, what to expect when\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:757:SCP cuts a new release, and how break-glass + rollback work.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:758:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:759:#### 12.7.1 Minimal caller wrapper\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:760:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:761:Add this file at `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` in your repo. Pin\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:762:the `uses:` line by 40-character commit SHA, NOT by tag name. The\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:763:`# tag: v1.0.0` comment is the human-readable annotation and the signal\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:764:the SCP Renovate preset uses to bump the SHA + comment together on every\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:765:SCP release.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:766:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:767:```yaml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:768:# .github/workflows/policy-check.yml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:769:name: policy-check\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:770:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:771:\"on\":\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:772:  pull_request:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:773:    branches: [main]\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:774:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:775:permissions:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:776:  contents: read\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:777:  statuses: write  # required for scp/policy-check-readback per D-029 / 020C.1(vi)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:778:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:779:jobs:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:780:  policy-check:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:781:    # Refuse fork PRs — same-repo only for v1.0.0 (mandatory; do not\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:782:    # remove this `if:`. Fork PRs run with the fork's read-only\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:783:    # GITHUB_TOKEN and cannot post the readback commit-status, plus\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:784:    # they can carry malicious workflow-context-injection payloads.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:785:    # Closes WP-SCP-020 020D1 R1 review TF-D1-002.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:786:    if: ${{ github.event.pull_request.head.repo.full_name == github.event.pull_request.base.repo.full_name }}\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:787:    # renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:788:    uses: jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<commit-SHA>  # tag: v1.0.0\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:789:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:790:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:791:The `if:` fork-PR refusal is **mandatory**, not optional. Closes the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:792:20D1 R1 review tracked-forward item TF-D1-002.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:793:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:794:**Before deploying:** review §12.7.13 for the v1.0.0 supply-chain posture (OPA + Conftest + Regal SHA256-verified per platform).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:795:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:796:**CODEOWNERS for the wrapper.** Multi-maintainer adopters MUST\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:797:protect this file with CODEOWNERS so a single PR cannot silently\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:798:delete the fork-PR `if:`, weaken `permissions:`, or change the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:799:pinned SHA without an owning reviewer. Symmetric with §11.10's\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:800:recommendation for `.scp/rule-config.yaml`. Minimum entry:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:801:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:802:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:803:.github/workflows/policy-check.yml @your-team-owners\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:804:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:805:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:806:#### 12.7.2 Renovate preset (`extends:` snippet)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:807:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:808:Add this single-line preset extension to your repo's `renovate.json`:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:809:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:810:```json\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:811:{\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:812:  \"$schema\": \"https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json\",\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:813:  \"extends\": [\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:814:    \"github>jrnb2024/standards-control-plane//renovate/default#renovate/v1.0.0\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:815:  ]\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:816:}\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:817:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:818:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:819:The preset is published at `renovate/v1.0.0` (independent of the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:820:federation-primitive `v*` tag series; see `docs/security/branch-protection.md`).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:821:The customManager regex matches the canonical wrapper marker and bumps both\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:822:the SHA pin and the `# tag:` comment together on every SCP release.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:823:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:824:Adopters MUST NOT add packageRules that override the preset's\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:825:`automerge: false` for the SCP federation primitive — that's how\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:826:malicious supply-chain updates would auto-promote.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:827:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:828:**Tag-series protection.** The `renovate/v*` tag series is\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:829:protected by Repository Ruleset `scp-tag-protection-renovate-v`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:830:(D-034 — deletion + force-push + non-fast-forward all blocked,\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:831:including for admins). Verify before extending:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:832:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:833:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:834:gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/rulesets \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:835:  --jq '.[] | select(.name == \"scp-tag-protection-renovate-v\") | .enforcement'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:836:# expected: active\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:837:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:838:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:839:`docs/security/branch-protection.md` carries the full SCP-side\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:840:protection state.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:841:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:842:#### 12.7.3 Branch-protection setup\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:843:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:844:Run the SCP-published helper from your local clone of the SCP repo:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:845:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:846:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:847:cd <your-local-clone-of-standards-control-plane>\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:848:./scripts/enable-required-check.sh \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:849:  --repo OWNER/NAME \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:850:  --branch main\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:851:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:852:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:853:The script (per WP-SCP-020 §4 020G + D-035):\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:854:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:855:1. Asserts `gh --version >= 2.40` + `jq` + `git` + `python3` + `shasum` on PATH.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:856:2. Refuses to run when `CI=true` or `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` (bootstrap-only).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:857:3. Validates `--repo` (regex + path-traversal guard) and `--branch` (no slashes / .. / leading dot).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:858:4. Logs a stderr WARNING about required PAT scope (`administration:write` on the single target repo).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:859:5. Captures before-state, applies the unified PUT (status-checks + admins + reviews), then a separate POST to the `required_signatures` sub-resource.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:860:6. Verifies 4 properties (strict, contexts, enforce_admins, signatures) and emits the result.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:861:7. Emits an invocation-log markdown block for paste into `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` on the SCP repo. The log commit is part of the invocation procedure.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:862:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:863:Use `--plan` first to see both the current state and the proposed payload before applying.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:864:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:865:For multi-maintainer adopters who want review enforcement: the script *preserves* any existing `required_pull_request_reviews` shape rather than nulling it (per 020G fix-round-1 SAF-002 closure). Configure your review-shape via the standard GitHub UI or API; the SCP helper won't touch it. **Multi-maintainer adopters MUST also set `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`** — see §12.7.4 for the security rationale and the helper's stderr WARNING when this is missing.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:866:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:867:**PAT scope is broader than it looks.** `administration:write` on a fine-grained PAT covers more than branch-protection settings — it also enables some webhook operations, repository-transfer initiation, and archival. (Repository **environments** — deployment secrets and protection rules — are governed by a separate `environments: write` permission and are NOT included in `administration:write`; mention here only to clarify the boundary.) Issue a single-use fine-grained PAT scoped to the one target repo, run the helper, then immediately revoke or expire the PAT. Do NOT retain an `administration:write` PAT for routine use.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:868:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:869:**Required-check context name.** The required status check MUST be configured to the **check-run** context `policy-check / scp/policy-check`, NOT to the **commit-status** context `scp/policy-check-readback`. The check-run is the authoritative gate (driven by GitHub Actions); the readback is an informational commit-status forge-able by any runner with `statuses: write`. The `enable-required-check.sh` helper defaults to the correct check-run context per D-033.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:870:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:871:**Verify the gate is live before relying on it.** Empirical verification, per D-033 (don't trust the spec — test the live state):\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:872:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:873:1. Confirm the required-check context is registered:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:874:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:875:   ```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:876:   gh api repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:877:     --jq '{strict: .strict, contexts: .contexts}'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:878:   # expected (selectively): {\"strict\": true, \"contexts\": [\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\"]}\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:879:   ```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:880:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:881:2. Confirm `enforce_admins` and `required_signatures`:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:882:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:883:   ```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:884:   gh api repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/enforce_admins --jq '.enabled'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:885:   # expected: true\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:886:   gh api repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_signatures --jq '.enabled'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:887:   # expected: true\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:888:   ```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:889:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:890:3. Open a draft PR introducing a deliberate `SCP-R-001` violation (e.g., a `services.yml` entry with an invalid `auth.mode` value). Confirm the PR's `policy-check / scp/policy-check` check shows red with an `SCP-E003` annotation AND that the merge button is disabled. Close the draft PR after verification — it is not for merge. Do NOT promote production traffic onto a gate that has not been empirically tested with a real deny.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:891:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:892:#### 12.7.4 Break-glass procedure (three-gate model)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:893:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:894:The SCP federation gate fails closed by default. To bypass on a single PR (`scp_bypass: true` on the wrapper), the PR must satisfy ALL THREE gates simultaneously:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:895:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:896:1. **Approving review** from a member listed in your repo's CODEOWNERS for the paths the bypass affects. (This is the adopter's own CODEOWNERS file, not SCP's.) **Minimum-necessary path: `output/findings/waivers.json`** — every bypass PR adds a waiver entry per Gate 3 below, so CODEOWNERS coverage on this path guarantees Gate 1 fires on every bypass PR. Extend coverage to `services.yml`, `policies/**` (if you mirror policies locally), and any other SCP-governed paths in your repo, but do NOT omit `waivers.json` — without it, a bypass PR that touches only the wrapper or only a non-listed path slips through Gate 1.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:897:2. **Sibling D-NNN row** in the SAME PR adding a new row to your equivalent of `docs/DECISIONS.md` (regex pattern `^\\|\\s*D-[0-9]{3}\\s*\\|\\s*20[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}\\s*\\|`).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:898:3. **Matching `waivers.json` entry** in the SAME PR with `expires_at > now` and `rule_id` matching the bypass-triggering SCP-R-NNN rule.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:899:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:900:`scripts/verify-bypass-pairing.sh` (in the SCP repo, called by the workflow's `bypass-gate` step) checks Gates 2 and 3. Gate 1 (CODEOWNERS approval) is enforced by GitHub branch protection — see the two-mode breakdown immediately below. Any miss → `SCP-E004` → merge-blocked.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:901:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:902:**Two operating modes — Gate 1 enforcement varies.** Per D-033, the SCP self-dogfood gate runs in single-operator mode with `required_approving_review_count = 0` because GitHub forbids PR authors from approving their own PRs (count=1 + a single CODEOWNER would lock the operator out entirely). Adopters inherit the same dichotomy:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:903:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:904:- **Multi-maintainer adopters.** Configure branch protection with `required_approving_review_count >= 1`, `require_code_owner_reviews: true`, **AND `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`**. (GitHub enforces non-self-approval at the platform level — there is no separate REST API field for that constraint; the WP-SCP-020 plan corpus uses `require_review_from_non_author: true` as shorthand for this platform behaviour, but no API field needs to be set.) Gate 1 is **machine-enforced** — a bypass PR cannot merge without a CODEOWNER review from someone other than the author. The `dismiss_stale_reviews: true` setting is non-optional in this mode: without it, an approving CODEOWNER review on an initial commit persists across subsequent commits in the same PR, so an attacker who obtains a clean review can later push commits that add `.scp/rule-config.yaml disable: true`, change `scp_bypass: true`, or weaken the wrapper's fork-PR `if:` — and merge without re-review. Dismissal fires on ANY push to the PR branch regardless of which files the new commit touches — it is not path-selective. Stale-review dismissal is the enforcement complement to `require_code_owner_reviews`. The `enable-required-check.sh` helper preserves your existing review-shape verbatim and does NOT set `dismiss_stale_reviews: true` for you; configure it explicitly via the GitHub branch-protection UI or API. (As of fix-round-5 of this slice, `enable-required-check.sh` emits a stderr WARNING when the preserved existing review config has `dismiss_stale_reviews: false` — see also the \"verify the gate is live\" block in §12.7.3.)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:905:- **Single-operator adopters** (personal account, sole maintainer). Configure `required_approving_review_count = 0` per D-033 (count >= 1 makes the repo unmergeable). Gate 1 collapses to **documentation-only** — `scripts/verify-bypass-pairing.sh` does NOT check for an approving review, and the operator can self-author a bypass PR satisfying only Gates 2 and 3. This is the accepted bus-factor-1 cost (WP-SCP-020 §8 risk row); revisit at the 2026-07-21 quarterly review when a second maintainer onboards.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:906:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:907:**SCP source — bus-factor-1 disclosure.** As of v1.0.0, the SCP reusable workflow and Renovate preset (the supply-chain source this integration depends on) are themselves operated by a single maintainer (`@jrnb2024`) per D-031 (WP-SCP-020 §8 bus-factor-1 risk row). The SCP-side quarterly bus-factor-1 review is scheduled for 2026-07-21, separate from your repo's own bus-factor review. Adopters with multi-maintainer or regulatory requirements for supply-chain diversity should note this constraint and re-evaluate at that checkpoint. Estate-cascade rollouts (FLA pilot → PIM / recommender / shopify-app / mapp-doc-agent / control-tower per WP-SCP-024) will surface the same constraint until SCP onboards a second maintainer.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:908:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:909:**Gate 2 content-check limitation.** `verify-bypass-pairing.sh` checks that a D-NNN row containing the bypassed `rule_id` was added in the same PR, using a fixed-string substring match on the row contents (line 33 of the script). It does NOT validate that the row's Decision column specifically authorizes the bypass — a row that merely mentions the rule_id in the Rationale column will satisfy the content check. Human reviewers MUST verify the D-NNN row content is a genuine bypass authorization, not a tangential reference.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:910:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:911:**Alternative bypass surface — `.scp/rule-config.yaml`.** The three-gate model above covers `scp_bypass: true` invocations only. A rule disabled via `.scp/rule-config.yaml` (`disable: true` with an `expires_at`) suppresses the deny WITHOUT triggering `verify-bypass-pairing.sh`; the only signal is the SCP-E006 observability annotation (informational; non-blocking — see §12.7.7). Treat `.scp/rule-config.yaml` as a bypass-surface equivalent to `scp_bypass: true`:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:912:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:913:- **Adopters MUST CODEOWNERS-protect `.scp/rule-config.yaml`** (per §11.10) so a single developer cannot silently disable a rule.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:914:- An expired `disable` entry (`expires_at < now`) continues to suppress the deny for **one release** while the workflow emits a per-PR `::warning::` annotation `SCP-R-NNN rule-config disable expired YYYY-MM-DD; remove or extend` (`.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` \"Emit expired-rule-config one-release warning\" step). The runtime warning IS shipped at v1.0.0; **release-tag-time refusal** of SCP-self expired rule-config entries is shipped at v1.0.0 via `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` (TF-005 closed in slice 020H.3 — the release-gate workflow refuses a tag-cut when SCP-self `.scp/rule-config.yaml` has any `disable: true` entry with `expires_at < <UTC tag-cut date>`). Adopter-side rule-config expiry is enforced separately at PR time via SCP-E007. Treat the runtime warning as merge-soft-blocking and the CODEOWNERS coverage as the hard control.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:915:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:916:#### 12.7.5 Rollback procedure\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:917:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:918:If a SCP release introduces a regression that breaks your repo's PR flow:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:919:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:920:0. **Close any open Renovate-bot PR** that is bumping the wrapper SHA pin. The discriminating label is `scp-bump` (applied by the preset's SCP-primitive packageRule); this is distinct from the root-level `scp-federation` label, which appears on every PR generated by this preset. Filter on `scp-bump` so the rollback closure scopes to exactly the SCP-primitive bump series, not all Renovate PRs in your repo. If left open, a teammate may merge the bump PR during the rollback window and silently re-pin to the bad SHA. Re-open or let Renovate recreate the PR only after the SCP-side regression is confirmed resolved.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:921:1. Revert the wrapper's `@<SHA>` pin to the previous SCP release SHA via PR.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:922:2. Update the `# tag:` comment to match.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:923:3. Renovate will re-run the bump on its next scheduled cycle (default weekly); if you need it to retry sooner, close + reopen the Renovate-bumped PR or run Renovate dispatch manually.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:924:4. Open an issue at https://github.com/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/issues using the `rule-regression` template (`.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/rule-regression.md` — shipped at 020H.1) so SCP-side detection workflows correlate.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:925:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:926:Target: 4 hours from regression report to tag-pin revert (per WP-SCP-020 §4 020H.1 iv-e).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:927:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:928:**Full de-adoption** (different from per-release rollback). If your repo is exiting the SCP federation primitive entirely:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:929:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:930:1. Open a PR that:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:931:   - Deletes `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml`.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:932:   - Removes the `extends:` entry pointing at `github>jrnb2024/standards-control-plane//renovate/default` from your `renovate.json`.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:933:   - Adds a D-NNN row in your DECISIONS log naming the de-adoption rationale.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:934:2. After merge, remove the required-check from branch protection. The `enable-required-check.sh` helper does NOT have a removal mode — invoke the GitHub API directly:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:935:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:936:   ```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:937:   # List current required-check contexts\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:938:   gh api repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks --jq '.contexts'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:939:   ```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:940:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:941:   Then PATCH the contexts list. **Important:** the PATCH replaces the contexts array entirely, it does not subtract. If `policy-check / scp/policy-check` is your only required check, pass an empty array; if you have other required checks, you MUST include them in the new array or this PATCH removes them too:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:942:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:943:   ```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:944:   # Case A — SCP federation was your only required check\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:945:   gh api -X PATCH repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:946:     --input - <<'EOF'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:947:   {\"strict\": true, \"contexts\": []}\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:948:   EOF\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:949:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:950:   # Case B — you have other required checks (substitute their context names)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:951:   gh api -X PATCH repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:952:     --input - <<'EOF'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:953:   {\"strict\": true, \"contexts\": [\"other-required-check-1\", \"other-required-check-2\"]}\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:954:   EOF\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:955:   ```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:956:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:957:3. Optionally relax `enforce_admins` if it was set ONLY for the SCP gate. Keep `required_signatures` regardless — it is independent of SCP and a baseline supply-chain hygiene control.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:958:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:959:This procedure is intentionally explicit so de-adoption is auditable; partial de-adoption (deleting the wrapper without removing the required-check) leaves the branch unmergeable.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:960:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:961:#### 12.7.6 Python evaluator vs Rego scope\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:962:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:963:- **Rego** (this gate) = PR-time fast shape-checks. Three rules in v1.0.0 (SCP-R-001/002/003).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:964:- **Python** evaluator (existing in SCP) = nightly + manual + release-gate deep audit. Different code path.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:965:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:966:The conflict-gate (CI job `rego-vs-python-conflict`) ensures both engines agree on every shared fixture. Disagreement → `SCP-E005` → merge-blocked → amending decision row in a separate PR resolves it.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:967:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:968:#### 12.7.7 Error codes\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:969:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:970:| Code | Meaning | Failure mode |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:971:|---|---|---|\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:972:| `SCP-E001` | Infrastructure fetch failure (OPA/Conftest binary unreachable, SHA256 mismatch, lockfile pin missing) | Fail-closed (workflow exits non-zero before policy evaluation) |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:973:| `SCP-E002` | Policy-bundle or invocation pre-condition failure — policy directory missing/wrong type, changed-files manifest absent, waivers/rule-config data preparation error, manifest-file checkout missing, or Conftest invocation failure (Rego compilation, missing helper, etc.) | Fail-closed |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:974:| `SCP-E003` | Policy deny — a rule fired and no waiver suppressed it | Merge-blocked; structured finding emitted |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:975:| `SCP-E004` | Break-glass bypass failed three-gate check | Merge-blocked |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:976:| `SCP-E005` | Conflict-gate disagreement (Rego ≠ Python on shared fixture) | Merge-blocked; amending D-NNN required |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:977:| `SCP-E006` | Disabled-rule observability record (informational) | Non-blocking — step exits 0 and merge proceeds. Note: GitHub renders the `::error::` annotation as a red X icon in the PR Files-Changed tab; this is observability noise, not a hard failure. |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:978:| `SCP-E007` | Rule-config schema validation failure (`.scp/rule-config.yaml` does not conform to `schemas/rule-config.schema.json` — missing required field, invalid `expires_at` format, or `additionalProperties` violation) | Fail-closed (workflow exits non-zero before policy evaluation) |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:979:| `SCP-FRESH-001` | Wrapper pin is more than `freshness_warning_threshold_minor` (default 2) minor versions behind SCP `main` HEAD's `version-manifest.json` (post-020H.1). Title is `::warning::`, not `::error::` — adopters bump via Renovate (§12.7.2) or manually. | Non-blocking — informational annotation only. |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:980:| `SCP-EREL-001` | SCP-side release-gate refusal (post-020H.3). Tag-cut blocked because `policies/deprecations.yaml` shows a deprecation whose ramp window has not elapsed (one MINOR release per VERSIONING.md (ii)) OR because `.scp/rule-config.yaml` on the SCP repo has an expired `disable` entry. Two operating modes: dry-run pre-flight via `workflow_dispatch` (operator pre-emptive check before pushing the tag); post-tag observer on `push:tags:['v*']` (last-line-of-defense annotator AND auto-opens a `release-gate-violation` GitHub issue assigned to `@jrnb2024` per 020H.3.1 closure of TF-020H3rg-003 — the bad tag is immutable per D-030, recovery is via cutting a corrected v<X>.<Y+1>.0). A non-blocking `::warning::` variant (title `SCP-EREL-001-warn`) fires when an entry's `announced_release` is more than one major behind the candidate — operator advisory for potential backdating; does not block the tag-cut. Both titles fire on the SCP source repo only; adopter annotation parsers never receive them. **Adopter-side relevance:** none directly. Adopters interact with the same invariants via SCP-E007 (rule-config schema/expiry at PR time) + the per-surface deprecation `::warning::` annotations (SCP-DEP-001) emitted during the one-MINOR ramp window. | Tag-cut blocked at SCP source (dry-run mode) OR annotated + auto-issue post-tag (push:tags mode). |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:981:| `SCP-DEP-001` (announcement class) | Per-PR deprecation `::warning::` annotation emitted while a rule (or other public surface) is in its one-MINOR ramp window before removal at the next MAJOR. Format: `SCP-R-NNN deprecated; will be removed in v<X+1>.0.0; <migration-pointer>` (or analogous text for non-rule surfaces). Emission responsibility belongs to the surface itself (e.g. the rule's Rego implementation) — there is no centralized emitter. **Adopter-side relevance:** read the migration pointer + plan to bump the wrapper SHA past the removal release. The ramp window is auditable in `policies/deprecations.yaml` on the SCP source. | Non-blocking — informational annotation only. |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:982:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:983:#### 12.7.8 SECURITY.md pointer\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:984:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:985:Adopters concerned about a policy-bypass disclosure should follow the SCP repo's `SECURITY.md` policy at https://github.com/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/blob/main/SECURITY.md. Use a private GitHub Security Advisory at https://github.com/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/security/advisories/new (preferred) or email `jimbrooke@me.com`. Initial response SLA: 3 business days. Closure of WP-SCP-020 §4.1 follow-up `SCP-073.sec` shipped at 020H.1.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:986:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:987:#### 12.7.9 Pre-commit hook (optional, recommended)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:988:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:989:Run the SCP gate locally on every commit so you catch denies before pushing:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:990:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:991:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:992:# In your repo root, install the pre-commit hook\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:993:cat > .git/hooks/pre-commit <<'EOF'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:994:#!/usr/bin/env bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:995:set -euo pipefail\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:996:exec <your-local-clone-of-standards-control-plane>/scripts/scp-policy-check\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:997:EOF\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:998:chmod +x .git/hooks/pre-commit\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:999:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1000:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1001:The local script (`scripts/scp-policy-check`) reproduces the CI invocation against staged files using the same SHA-locked OPA + Conftest binaries. SHA256 verification is performed for these two; offline support if binaries are already downloaded. (Note: the local hook does not invoke Regal — Regal lint runs CI-only against the policy bundle. The CI workflow's Regal binary IS SHA256-verified as of slice 020H.2; see §12.7.13 for the supply-chain posture.)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1002:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1003:**The local SCP clone MUST be checked out at the same commit SHA as your wrapper's `# tag:` pin.** A stale clone runs old policy rules and produces hook verdicts that diverge from CI — false-passes that the developer only discovers when CI runs (defeating the hook's stated purpose). A tampered clone can suppress denies entirely. Before relying on the hook:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1004:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1005:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1006:git -C <your-local-clone-of-standards-control-plane> fetch\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1007:git -C <your-local-clone-of-standards-control-plane> checkout <your-wrapper-pinned-SHA>\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1008:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1009:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1010:Or extend the hook to read the SHA from `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` and verify the clone matches before invoking the script. Divergence from the CI-pinned SHA invalidates the hook's verdicts.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1011:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1012:##### 12.7.9.1 Rule-author pre-push verify wrapper (post-TF-020P-005)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1013:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1014:**Audience: SCP-repo rule authors only.** This subsection is for contributors working directly inside the `standards-control-plane` repository on `policies/SCP-R-*.rego` rule files. **Adopter repos do not need this wrapper** — your pre-push verification is covered by the SCP reusable workflow you wired in §12.7.1, and the SHA-pinning warnings in the parent §12.7.9 do not apply to invocations from inside the SCP repo itself.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1015:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1016:If you are authoring or modifying SCP-R-NNN rule files (`policies/SCP-R-*.rego`), `scripts/scp-pre-push-verify.sh` mirrors the three CI rule-author gates locally so you do not have to round-trip through CI to surface them: Regal lint (with the same disable list as `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml`), `opa fmt --fail` over the entire `policies/` tree, and per-rule `opa test --coverage --threshold 90 --fail-on-empty -v`. Run it from any subdirectory of the SCP clone:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1017:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1018:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1019:scripts/scp-pre-push-verify.sh\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1020:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1021:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1022:The wrapper assumes `opa` and `regal` are installed locally (it does not bootstrap binaries — that is `scripts/scp-policy-check`'s job for the policy-bundle evaluation half). It emits a non-fatal warning if your local versions diverge from `scripts/.tool-versions`. **CI is still the authoritative gate** — the wrapper is a CI-roundtrip saver, not a federation-conformance gate. Closes WP-SCP-022 TF-020P-003 / 004 / 005.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1023:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1024:#### 12.7.10 NEVER use `secrets: inherit`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1025:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1026:The SCP reusable workflow **does not declare any `secrets:`**. Adopter wrappers MUST NOT use `secrets: inherit` on the `uses:` invocation. The caller's `GITHUB_TOKEN` is the privilege ceiling; granting any other secret to the workflow expands the blast radius beyond what the federation primitive's threat model assumes.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1027:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1028:**Forward-compatibility caveat.** Do not add `secrets: inherit` even if it appears to be a safe no-op at the current SCP version (where the reusable workflow declares no secrets). A future SCP version that introduces any named `secrets:` declaration would retroactively pass every caller secret to the workflow on adopter repos that pre-emptively added `secrets: inherit`. Bypassing this declaration is therefore both unnecessary today AND a forward-compatibility risk.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1029:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1030:#### 12.7.11 Freshness warning (post-020H.1)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1031:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1032:The SCP reusable workflow annotates `::warning::title=SCP-FRESH-001` on each PR run if your wrapper's pinned SHA is more than 2 minor versions behind the latest SCP release (e.g., your pin is `v1.0.x` but `v1.2.0` is available). The freshness check reads `version-manifest.json` from two sources at workflow-execution time:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1033:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1034:1. `${SCP_RUNTIME_ROOT}/version-manifest.json` — the manifest at the SHA your wrapper pins. If absent (wrapper pin predates 020H.1), the check skips silently.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1035:2. `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/main/version-manifest.json` — the manifest at SCP `main` HEAD. Network errors / 404s skip silently — the check is best-effort and never fails the gate.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1036:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1037:Compare the `minor` fields. The minor field is a dotted string `X.Y` (e.g. `1.0`). The check parses both as `(major, minor)` integer pairs and emits the warning when:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1038:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1039:- the majors differ (treated as far-behind — always emits), OR\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1040:- the majors match AND `(main.minor - pinned.minor) > freshness_warning_threshold_minor` (default `2`).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1041:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1042:The `freshness_warning_threshold_minor` value is read from the **PINNED** manifest (the one in `.scp-runtime/`), not from main HEAD's manifest — this prevents an attacker who compromises main HEAD's `version-manifest.json` from silencing the warning by setting the threshold to a large number (closes 020H.1 R1 SAFE-MIN-006).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1043:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1044:The annotation is informational; it does not block merge. Adopters who pin via the SCP Renovate preset (§12.7.2) will see automated bump PRs that resolve the warning; adopters whose Renovate is misconfigured can still rely on this CI-time signal.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1045:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1046:**Wrapper pins predating 020H.1** silently skip the check (no `version-manifest.json` shipped under the SHA pin). When you next bump to a 020H.1+ release the warning becomes active.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1047:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1048:#### 12.7.12 Actions-billing note\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1049:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1050:Each PR run consumes ~30 seconds of GitHub Actions runner time (warm-start; cold-start adds 10–15s for binary download + SHA verification). GitHub bills Actions in whole minutes per job, rounded up — a ~30–45s job counts as 1 billed minute. Personal-account adopters on the GitHub Free tier with the standard 2,000-minute monthly budget should therefore expect ~2,000 PR runs/month before the budget caps — comfortable headroom for typical adopter PR volumes. Organisation accounts with paid plans have effectively unlimited budget.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1051:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1052:#### 12.7.13 Supply-chain posture (post-020H.2)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1053:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1054:The reusable workflow downloads three binaries at runtime, all SHA256-verified per platform against `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock`:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1055:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1056:- **OPA** (policy evaluator) — pinned by version in `scripts/.tool-versions`; SHA256-verified.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1057:- **Conftest** (Rego harness) — pinned by version + archive SHA256 + binary SHA256 per platform.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1058:- **Regal** (Rego linter) — pinned by version in `scripts/.tool-versions` (`regal 0.40.0`); SHA256-verified per platform via the same `resolve_regal()` helper pattern as `resolve_opa()`. **TF-020H3-001 closed in slice 020H.2** (2026-05-01) ahead of the 2026-05-14 deadline.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1059:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1060:**Sigstore attestation status.** OPA `gh attestation verify` is invoked but soft-warns on every run because OPA v1.x has not yet published Sigstore attestations to GitHub's attestation database (HTTP 404). Conftest does not publish attestations either. Regal is published via OPA's pipeline and almost certainly shares the same gap; slice 020H.2 elected NOT to add a parallel `gh attestation verify` for Regal (which would just emit symmetric 404 noise). All three tools' Sigstore re-tightening is tracked as **TF-007** (now extended to cover Regal) — re-tighten to hard-fail when OPA upstream begins publishing attestations.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1061:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1062:**Lockfile + version-pin governance.** `scripts/scp-policy-check.lock` and `scripts/.tool-versions` are the cryptographic root-of-trust for every supply-chain check. Both are CODEOWNERS-protected on the SCP repo via `scripts/** @jrnb2024` (and `vendor/** @jrnb2024` for the resolve-fallback path) — so a PR mutating either file must be reviewed (in single-operator count=0 mode the rule is documentary; in multi-maintainer mode it is machine-enforced). Adopters who run their own SCP fork MUST mirror this CODEOWNERS coverage on their fork: add `scripts/** @<owner>` and `vendor/** @<owner>` to the fork's CODEOWNERS, inserted **before** any CODEOWNERS self-protection line (last-match-wins ordering — see the SCP repo's CODEOWNERS comment block for the ORDERING INVARIANT). This is analogous to but distinct from the adopter-side caller-wrapper CODEOWNERS recommendations in §12.7.1 and §12.7.4 — those protect the adopter's own `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` and `.scp/rule-config.yaml`, not the fork's lockfile.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1063:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1064:**RUNNER_TEMP TOCTOU assumption.** `verify_sha256` is called inside each `resolve_<tool>()` function on the path returned to the caller, which then `cp`s into `BIN_DIR`. There is a TOCTOU window between the verify and the cp — closed in practice on GitHub-hosted ubuntu-24.04 by the runner user being the exclusive writer (`RUNNER_TEMP` is owned by the runner user; the ephemeral single-user VM has no other local accounts that could exploit the window between operations). On self-hosted runners, ensure `RUNNER_TEMP` is not group/world-writable and that no other process running as the runner user can substitute the file mid-flight. This is the same design as `resolve_opa` and is not introduced by 020H.2.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1065:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1066:**Asset-shape pin.** The lockfile's `regal` block is bare-binary-shaped (single `sha256` field, no `archive_sha256`) because Regal v0.40.0 ships as a bare binary, not a tarball. If Regal upstream moves to tarball shipping in a future release, both the lockfile schema (add `archive_sha256`) and `resolve_regal()` (add a `.gz` extraction branch matching `resolve_conftest()`) need updating in lockstep with the version bump. The current `resolve_regal()` includes `assert_bare_binary_shape()` which reads the first two bytes of the downloaded asset via Python (already a runner dependency for other helpers — no `xxd` reliance) and emits an explicit infra-failure message if the asset begins with the gzip magic bytes (`0x1f 0x8b`). Defends against a silent shape transition.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1067:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1068:**Python dependency hash-pinning (post-020M).** As of v1.0.1 the reusable workflow + release-gate workflow install Python dependencies (`pyyaml`, `jsonschema`, and the full transitive closure: `attrs`, `jsonschema-specifications`, `referencing`, `rpds-py`) via `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements/policy-check.txt`. The lockfile `requirements/policy-check.txt` is generated by `pip-compile --generate-hashes` from the input file `requirements/policy-check.in` (which carries the top-level pins `pyyaml==6.0.2` + `jsonschema==4.23.0`). Every wheel hash for every released platform-specific build is recorded; `pip` refuses install if PyPI serves a wheel whose SHA256 is not in the lockfile. Both the lockfile and its `.in` source are CODEOWNERS-protected on the SCP repo via `requirements/** @jrnb2024` (closes 020M R1 SAFE-MAJ-001). The install step is **unconditional** — a presence-only conditional guard (`if ! python3 -c 'import yaml'; then pip install...`) was previously skipping the hash-verified install on hosted ubuntu-24.04 runners which preinstall pyyaml 6.0.1 from apt; the v1.0.1 pattern always runs `pip install --require-hashes` and follows it with a version-pin assertion (`assert yaml.__version__ == '6.0.2'`) to defend against future-PR drift (closes 020M R1 SAFE-MAJ-002). Adopters running their own SCP fork should mirror this CODEOWNERS coverage on their fork: add `requirements/** @<owner>` before the CODEOWNERS self-protection line.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1069:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1070:**Lockfile regeneration procedure.** When bumping `pyyaml` or `jsonschema`, edit `requirements/policy-check.in` (the top-level pin source), then run:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1071:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1072:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1073:python3 -m venv /tmp/scp-piptools\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1074:/tmp/scp-piptools/bin/pip install pip-tools\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1075:/tmp/scp-piptools/bin/pip-compile --generate-hashes \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1076:  --output-file requirements/policy-check.txt requirements/policy-check.in\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1077:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1078:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1079:Review the diff (transitive deps may also bump), file the version change as a PATCH or MINOR per VERSIONING.md.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1080:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1081:> **REGENERATION INVARIANT (closes 020M R2 SAFE-R2-MIN-001 + COMP-R2-MIN-002 — TF-020M-002; extended in 020N R1 SAFE-MIN-001 + COMP-MIN-001 to cover conflict-gate.yml).** When ANY lockfile's top-level pins change, the **version-pin assertion strings hardcoded in the calling workflow files MUST be updated in lockstep**. The SCP repo currently maintains TWO independent lockfiles (each with its own assertion sites):\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1082:>\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1083:> - **`requirements/policy-check.txt`** (slice 020M, v1.0.1; calling workflows: `policy-check.yml` + `release-gate.yml`). Search `.github/workflows/policy-check.yml` and `.github/workflows/release-gate.yml` for `assert yaml.__version__ ==` and `assert jsonschema.__version__ ==` and update to the new pinned versions.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1084:> - **`requirements/conflict-gate.txt`** (slice 020N; calling workflow: `conflict-gate.yml` only). Search `.github/workflows/conflict-gate.yml` for `assert yaml.__version__ ==`, `assert jsonschema.__version__ ==`, `assert fastapi.__version__ ==`, and `assert pydantic.VERSION ==` and update each to the new pinned versions.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1085:>\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1086:> The assertions are intentionally string-literal (not parsed from the lockfile) so a copy/paste regression triggers fail-closed CI on the regeneration PR rather than silently allowing a version skew. Failure mode is loud: SCP-E001 / SCP-E004 annotation listing the actual vs expected versions. **A regeneration PR that bumps `requirements/<lockfile>.in` without bumping the matching assertion strings WILL fail CI** — this is the intended pre-merge enforcement.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1087:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1088:#### 12.7.14 Adopter response to SCP-R-004 warn annotations (post-020P / v1.1.0)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1089:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1090:SCP-R-004 (added in v1.1.0 per slice 020P / RULE-001) fires at **warn baseline** on each waiver entry whose `reason` field is a non-empty string but does NOT contain at least one HTTP(S) URL. The motivation is auditability: SCP-R-002 already enforces waiver shape (every entry has a non-empty `reason`), but `reason` is free-text — `reason: \"approved by Jim\"` passes both layers without a machine-checkable link to a reviewable decision artifact (issue, PR, decision log entry).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1091:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1092:When you bump your SCP federation primitive SHA pin to v1.1.0, the next PR that touches a waivers payload will surface `::warning::` annotations on every waiver entry whose `reason` lacks a URL. **The warning is non-blocking** — your `policy-check / scp/policy-check` check stays green and merge proceeds. The annotation appears as a yellow triangle in the PR Files-Changed tab on `output/findings/waivers.json` with title `SCP-R-004` and the message format specified in RULE-001 §3.3.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1093:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1094:You have three response options. Pick the one that matches your team's posture:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1095:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1096:**Option A — Gradual amendment (lowest friction, recommended for most adopters).** On each next-touch PR that modifies a waiver entry (e.g. extending `expires_at`), amend the entry's `reason` to include a URL pointing at the artifact that justified the waiver. For new waivers, include a URL at creation time. The estate's governance pattern (per `MEMORY.md` `project_estate_structure.md`) already routes most waivers through GitHub issues / PRs / `docs/notifications/` files — those have natural URLs. Over a few months your waivers.json migrates organically.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1097:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1098:**Option B — `.scp/rule-config.yaml` disable for a transition window.** Add an entry suppressing SCP-R-004 for ~90 days while you do a planned cleanup pass. The shape is:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1099:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1100:```yaml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1101:# .scp/rule-config.yaml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1102:rules:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1103:  SCP-R-004:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1104:    disable: true\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1105:    expires_at: \"2026-08-02\"  # ~90 days from v1.1.0 adoption\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1106:    justification: \"transition window — amending legacy waivers to include URLs per RULE-001\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1107:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1108:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1109:Both `expires_at` and `justification` are required by `schemas/rule-config.schema.json` (per `SCP-E007`). After the transition window expires, the workflow emits a one-release `::warning::` annotation `SCP-R-004 rule-config disable expired YYYY-MM-DD; remove or extend` (per §12.7.7 `SCP-E006`-adjacent behaviour).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1110:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1111:**Option C — Bulk-amend cleanup PR (highest friction, most complete).** Open a single PR that walks every waiver in `output/findings/waivers.json` (or wherever your waivers payload lives) and adds a URL to each `reason`. Useful if your repo's waivers count is small (≤20) or if you want to close out the SCP-R-004 surface before any other PRs touch the file.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1112:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1113:**Promotion to deny default.** SCP-R-004 stays at warn baseline at v1.1.0. The earliest plausible promotion to deny default is v2.0.0; promotion requires its own RFC-NNN proposal per `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/README.md` §When to file. The proposal would observe the warn-baseline period's actual FP rate against legacy waivers across the estate before justifying the promotion. Adopter waivers already cleaned up under Option A or C are unaffected by promotion; adopters relying on Option B's rule-config disable should remove the disable before the promotion lands (the deny-default rule-config disable still suppresses for one release per `SCP-E006`-adjacent behaviour, but that grace window is your last chance).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1114:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1115:**Meta-waiver shape.** If you waive SCP-R-004 itself (e.g. for a single legacy waiver entry that you cannot retrofit a URL onto), the meta-waiver's OWN `reason` field MUST contain a URL — otherwise the meta-waiver is itself a raw finding for SCP-R-004. Per RULE-001 §5: `reason: \"waiving SCP-R-004 for legacy waiver W-X per https://github.com/<your-repo>/issues/NNN\"`. If you cannot supply a URL in the meta-waiver reason (e.g. governance artifact lives behind VPN with no stable URL), use Option B (rule-config disable) instead.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1116:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1117:**Reference.** RULE-001 in `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/RULE-001-waiver-reason-must-cite-issue-or-pr.md` is the canonical specification — it covers the false-positive surface (§4), the implicit-exclusion set (§5), the conflict-gate strategy (§6), the estate-cascade considerations (§7), and the Phase-2 implementation details that produced this v1.1.0 ship. The merged proposal is the durable reference for any adopter question about SCP-R-004 semantics.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1118:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1119:#### Reference\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1120:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1121:- `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-022 (federation-primitive adoption); D-029 (`statuses: write` for readback); D-030 (020J `v*` tag-protection); D-031 (020K CODEOWNERS personal-account); D-032 (020D2 SCP-self required-check); D-033 (rendered context-name `policy-check / scp/policy-check`); D-034 (020F `renovate/v*` tag-protection); D-035 (020G adopter-helper invocation); D-036 (`policies/VERSIONING.md` semver contract + rule-RFC process as estate doctrine; closes 020H.1 (i)+(ii)+(iii) and BS-5); D-040 (slice 020L: 48h is CEILING-not-FLOOR in single-operator mode for the rule-RFC process); D-041 (cross-repo scorecard data shape, opt-in adopter participation); D-042 (aggregator pipeline trust model + mandatory `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`); D-043 (MCP `scp.consult_scorecard` read-only contract).\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1122:- `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` for the full federation-primitive spec.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1123:- `docs/plans/WP-SCP-023-cross-repo-scorecards.md` for the full cross-repo scorecard plan.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1124:- `docs/reviews/rule-proposals/RULE-001-waiver-reason-must-cite-issue-or-pr.md` (post-v1.1.0) — canonical specification for SCP-R-004.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1125:- `docs/security/branch-protection.md` for the SCP-side protection state.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1126:- §11.10 of this document for the `.scp/rule-config.yaml` CODEOWNERS recommendation referenced from §12.7.4.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1127:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1128:#### 12.7.15 Cross-repo scorecard opt-in (post-WP-SCP-023 / v1.2.0)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1129:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1130:Adopters MAY opt in to cross-repo scorecard aggregation. This is **optional**; non-participating repos see no behaviour change and are NOT listed as \"non-compliant\" anywhere — invariant 4 of WP-SCP-023 plan-doc.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1131:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1132:**Privacy contract:** the emit aggregator carries **aggregated counts only** — never `reason`, `approved_by`, or `waiver_id` strings from your `output/findings/waivers.json`. Schema (`schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json`) enforces `additionalProperties: false` at every level. The aggregator NEVER reads your sibling waiver content directly; it consumes only the per-PR `scorecard-emit.json` artifact your wrapper publishes.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1133:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1134:**Three steps to opt in:**\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1135:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1136:1. **Bump your wrapper's SHA pin to v1.2.0 or later.** Renovate will prompt automatically; merge as you would any other SCP version bump.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1137:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1138:2. **Set `scorecard-emit: true`** on your wrapper's `with:` block AND grant the two extra permissions the called `attest-scorecard` job needs:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1139:   ```yaml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1140:   permissions:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1141:     contents: read\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1142:     statuses: write\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1143:     attestations: write   # required by called attest-scorecard job\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1144:     id-token: write       # required for OIDC artifact attestation\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1145:   jobs:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1146:     policy-check:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1147:       uses: jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<sha>\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1148:       with:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1149:         scorecard-emit: true   # opt-in; default false\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1150:   ```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1151:   Default-false (no `with:` block at all) means existing wrappers continue to work unchanged with the original two-permission ceiling. **You only add `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` if you opt in** — reusable workflows can never escalate above the caller's permission ceiling, so without these two the workflow fails at startup. The called workflow's `attest-scorecard` job is JOB-SCOPED on these permissions (closes WP-SCP-023 023B R1 MAJ-SAFE-001), so opt-out runs never request an OIDC token even if you grant them at the wrapper level.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1152:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1153:   > **Repo visibility / ownership prerequisite (TF-023E-001).** GitHub's `actions/attest-build-provenance` rejects user-owned private repos with HTTP error `Feature not available for user-owned private repositories`. Your repo MUST be either (a) public, or (b) owned by an organisation. If neither applies, the attestation step will fail and your runs will not produce a verifiable emit. The aggregator records repos without a verifiable attestation as `verification_failure` (per D-042 trust model); they are NOT silently accepted.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1154:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1155:3. **PR an entry to `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml`** in this repo:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1156:   ```yaml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1157:   - repo: \"<your-owner>/<your-repo>\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1158:     default_branch: \"main\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1159:     expected_scp_workflow_ref: \"jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<the-same-sha>\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1160:     opted_in_at: \"2026-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ\"\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1161:   ```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1162:   The `expected_scp_workflow_ref` is what the aggregator passes to `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow`. **It MUST match the SHA your wrapper pins.** When you bump the SHA pin, update this entry in the same PR (or a sibling PR before the next aggregator run) — a mismatch records as `verification_failure` in the index, NOT silent acceptance.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1163:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1164:**How to read your data:**\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1165:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1166:- **Markdown report:** `docs/scorecards/<YYYY-MM-DD>.md` is rendered weekly. The aggregator opens a PR for operator review on the SCP repo each Monday; the report lands on `main` once @jrnb2024 reviews and merges.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1167:- **Central index:** `output/scorecards/index.json` carries the canonical machine-readable shape; schema at `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1168:- **MCP method:** `scp.consult_scorecard` (per D-043) returns aggregated metrics + verification status. Optional filters: `repo_filter` (single repo) and `since_emitted_at` (ISO-8601). Read-only — no mutation surface.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1169:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1170:**Common failure modes you may see in the index:**\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1171:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1172:| Status | Cause | Remediation |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1173:|---|---|---|\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1174:| `verified` | OIDC verification + schema validation succeeded. | None. |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1175:| `verification_failure` | `gh attestation verify --signer-workflow` failed (SHA pin mismatch in `expected_scp_workflow_ref`) OR emit schema validation failed. | Update your registry entry's `expected_scp_workflow_ref` to match your wrapper's pinned SHA. |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1176:| `unreachable` | The aggregator could not reach your repo (rate limit, deletion, transient API error). | If transient, the next weekly run should recover. The aggregator retains the prior verified row's data alongside the unreachable status when available. |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1177:| `no_emit` | No green policy-check run on default branch within last 7 days OR run had no `scorecard-emit` artifact. | Confirm `scorecard-emit: true` is on your wrapper; confirm your default branch's policy-check is green. |\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1178:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1179:**Verifying a downloaded emit on your side:**\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1180:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1181:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1182:gh run download <run-id> --repo <your-owner>/<your-repo> --name scorecard-emit\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1183:gh attestation verify scorecard-emit/scorecard-emit.json \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1184:  --signer-workflow jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/.github/workflows/policy-check.yml@<sha>\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1185:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1186:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1187:**Opt-out:** delete your row from `docs/scorecards/opt-in-registry.yaml` via PR. The next aggregator run will not include you. You can also turn off `scorecard-emit: true` in your wrapper independently.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1188:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1189:**Reference:** `docs/plans/WP-SCP-023-cross-repo-scorecards.md` (plan-doc); `docs/DECISIONS.md` D-041/D-042/D-043; `schemas/scorecard-emit.schema.json` + `schemas/scorecard-index.schema.json`.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1190:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1191:### 12.8 Break-glass procedure for federation-primitive failure\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1192:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1193:Use this procedure when a cohort adopter needs to temporarily disable and then re-enable the federation primitive after a failure. The operator keeps the same single-operator discipline as the rest of ADOPT-001: each gate is explicit, logged, and reviewable.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1194:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1195:#### Gate 1 - DISABLE\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1196:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1197:Run the rollback helper from the SCP repo:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1198:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1199:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1200:scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1201:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1202:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1203:The `<pre-state.json>` input comes from the prior invocation log entry for the adopter repo and is the canonical pre-mutation state. The helper transforms the captured GET-shape JSON into the PUT-shape payload, strips envelope fields recursively, and restores `required_signatures` through its dedicated sub-resource. The rollback SLO is **less than 30 minutes** from operator decision to restored branch-protection state.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1204:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1205:If the restore target removes admin enforcement or removes required status checks, the helper exits 2 unless the operator passes the matching acknowledgement flag:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1206:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1207:- `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1208:- `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1209:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1210:These flags are confirmations, not defaults.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1211:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1212:#### Gate 2 - FIX\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1213:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1214:Pin the adopter wrapper in `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml` to the last known-good release-tag SHA. Use the exact release-tag object SHA, not an arbitrary commit SHA:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1215:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1216:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1217:gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/ref/tags/<release-tag> --jq .object.sha\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1218:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1219:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1220:That SHA is the integrity anchor for Gate 3. Do not substitute `main` HEAD or any other arbitrary commit.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1221:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1222:#### Gate 3 - RE-ENABLE\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1223:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1224:Re-enable the gate only after the wrapper pin has been updated and the operator supplies:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1225:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1226:```bash\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1227:--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-Gate-2>\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1228:```\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1229:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1230:The helper validates that the SHA resolves to an actual release tag in the SCP repo. If the flag is omitted, re-enable is rejected with exit 2.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1231:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1232:> **WARNING.** `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` is an emergency-only bypass for Gate 2. It re-arms the gate against the current wrapper SHA, so if the wrapper is still pinned to a defective SCP SHA the gate will block adopters again.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1233:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1234:> **CAUTION.** When the bypass flag is used, the helper emits a caution line in the invocation log block so the bypass is visible in the audit trail. Use it only when the operator is intentionally prioritising recovery over wrapper-pin verification.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1235:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1236:Reference: D-047, WP-SCP-024 invariant 7, D-035, D-030, and the break-glass guidance in `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md`.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1237:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1238:## 13. Recommended Adoption Phases\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1239:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1240:### Phase 0 — Prep\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1241:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1242:- choose owners\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1243:- choose pilot subsystem\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1244:- add overlay directory\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1245:- add wrapper scripts\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1246:- update governance docs\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1247:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1248:### Phase 1 — Local advisory use\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1249:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1250:- run `consult` before implementation work\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1251:- run `audit-changed` locally before PRs\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1252:- keep domains to `governance,architecture`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1253:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1254:### Phase 2 — CI advisory mode\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1255:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1256:- add PR CI job for changed-file audit\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1257:- publish CI artifacts\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1258:- do not block merges on warnings yet\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1259:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1260:### Phase 3 — Scheduled findings refresh\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1261:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1262:- add scheduled full or subsystem audit\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1263:- start maintaining waivers and accepted debt explicitly\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1264:- review trend and rollup artifacts regularly\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1265:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1266:### Phase 4 — Optional service and estate surfacing\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1267:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1268:- stand up the optional consult service if it helps multiple teams\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1269:- plug emitted artifacts into Control Tower or a local dashboard\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1270:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1271:## 14. Anti-Patterns to Avoid\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1272:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1273:Do not do these:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1274:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1275:- do not make SCP the user's first hard merge gate\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1276:- do not onboard all five domains at once unless the repo already trusts the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1277:  weaker advisory domains\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1278:- do not put repo-specific assumptions into SCP core when an overlay would do\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1279:- do not keep findings in chat, tickets, or screenshots only\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1280:- do not create floating TODOs instead of findings, waivers, or backlog items\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1281:- do not replace the repo's stronger existing review protocol with a weaker SCP\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1282:  process\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1283:- do not run a central service and assume that removes the need for repo-local\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1284:  CI integration\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1285:- do not ship an HTTP service without declaring an `auth_contract` —\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1286:  SVC-003 fires `missing-auth-contract`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1287:- do not declare `mode.user_oidc` while implementing the deprecated\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1288:  `secrets.compare_digest` bearer path — the code-pattern scan fires\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1289:  `impl-missing-user_oidc` (and `impl-undeclared-bearer_legacy` when\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1290:  the `secrets.compare_digest` marker is present in source)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1291:- do not treat `--auth-token` (`mode.bearer_legacy`) as a long-term\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1292:  default — it is deprecated per D-019 and requires a time-bound\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1293:  migration waiver in every interim services.yml\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1294:- do not let a `mode.bearer_legacy` waiver lapse silently — renew via\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1295:  governance or complete the migration before the close date\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1296:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1297:## 15. Adoption Acceptance Checklist\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1298:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1299:A repo is properly onboarded when all of the following are true:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1300:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1301:- SCP is installed as a pinned dependency\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1302:- a repo-local overlay exists with a named owner\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1303:- wrapper scripts exist for consult and audit\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1304:- agent instructions explicitly require consult before coding\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1305:- CI runs changed-file audit on PRs\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1306:- scheduled audit exists for the repo or pilot subsystem\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1307:- waivers are stored in repo and time-bound\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1308:- findings and reports are inspectable through normal repo workflows\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1309:- the team knows who approves waivers and who owns overlay changes\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1310:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1311:### Additional checks for service-hosting repos\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1312:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1313:If the repo hosts an HTTP service audited by SCP, also confirm:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1314:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1315:- `services.yml` declares an `auth_contract` conforming to SVC-003\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1316:  (§11)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1317:- any `mode.bearer_legacy` entry has a registered waiver with an\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1318:  owner and close date\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1319:- the service's real implementation matches the declared modes (the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1320:  code-pattern scan must not fire `impl-missing-*` or\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1321:  `impl-undeclared-*`)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1322:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1323:If those are not true, the repo is not actually onboarded.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1324:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1325:## 16. Source Practices This Guide Was Derived From\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1326:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1327:This onboarding guide is aligned to:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1328:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1329:- `control-tower/governance/docs/DELIVERY_GOVERNANCE_PROTOCOL.md`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1330:- `control-tower/governance/docs/DOCUMENTATION_STANDARDS.md`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1331:- `control-tower/docs/strategy/platform-conformance-strategy.md`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1332:- `control-tower/docs/handoffs/conformance-prompts.md`\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1333:- [STRAT-SCP-001-phased-adoption.md](../strategy/STRAT-SCP-001-phased-adoption.md)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1334:- [README.md](../../README.md)\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1335:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1336:Those sources collectively define the estate's strongest current practice for:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1337:\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1338:- governance discipline\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1339:- thin conformance integration\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1340:- repo-local ownership with shared standards\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1341:- advisory-first rollout\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1342:- explicit project overlays\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:1:#!/usr/bin/env bash\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:2:set -euo pipefail\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3:\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:4:SCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:5:REPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"${SCRIPT_DIR}/../..\" && pwd)\"\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:6:SCRIPT=\"${REPO_ROOT}/scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh\"\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:7:RESTORE_SCRIPT=\"${REPO_ROOT}/scripts/enable-required-check.sh\"\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:8:\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:9:TMPDIR=\"$(mktemp -d)\"\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:10:cleanup() {\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:11:  rm -rf \"$TMPDIR\"\ntests/che