 forward-looking.\n- **TF-023D-002** (low priority): markdown report retention policy — keep last 90 days; compact older. Defer until ~Q3 2026 (~13 weekly reports accumulated). Filed at 023D DISPATCH-NOTE forward-looking.\n- **TF-023D-003** (medium priority): `_log_tool_invocation` carries `key_id=\"pending_021J\"` for every MCP tool — pre-existing audit-trail gap. consult_scorecard exposes the gap because it's the first MCP method exposing aggregated estate-wide data. Closure path: replace with active key_id from `docs/security/mcp-signing-keys.pub` before slice 023E / Threshold A sign-off. Filed at 023D R1 safety MAJ-SAFE-001.\n- **TF-023D-004** (medium priority): drift section in markdown report — plan-doc §5 + DISPATCH-NOTE AC (i) named it. Deferred at 023D because real adopter data is needed to compute drift (until 023E onboards adopters, no drift to surface). Closure path: at slice 023E or first weekly run with ≥2 verified adopters, implement either prior-markdown-comparison or prior-index-comparison. Filed at 023D R1 completeness CMP-MAJ-001.\n- **TF-023D-005** (low priority): MCP server redeploy — `scp.consult_scorecard` MCP method registration is a code change; the deployed MCP server at acc.brokapps.ai requires a redeploy to make the method callable by agents. Closure path: bundle with next ACC deployment cycle. Filed at 023D R1 completeness CMP-MIN-003.\n- **TF-023E-001** (medium priority): SCP-self scorecard-emit opt-in is **deferred** until `standards-control-plane-` becomes public OR transfers to an org. GitHub blocks `actions/attest-build-provenance` on user-owned private repos with \"Feature not available for user-owned private repositories\" — D-042's trust model requires every emit to carry an OIDC attestation, and a self-exemption would weaken it. Surface impact: TF-023C-001 (1-adopter test corpus via SCP-self) cannot close at slice 023E; first real adopter must be public/org-owned (likely FLA, mapp-doc-agent, or an org-owned ACC/CT subrepo). Closure path: (a) make the SCP repo public, OR (b) transfer to an org, OR (c) accept SCP-self perpetually as `verification_failure` in the index (rejected at 023E fix-round-3 — degrades trust signal). Surfaced at 023E CI fix-round-3 (the first PR to set `scorecard-emit: true` on the wrapper failed at the attestation step with the GitHub error message). Cross-references USER-GATE-D criterion (i) carve-out.\n- **TF-023E-002** (medium priority): SCP-self wrapper SHA pin is **stuck at v1.0.0 (@41a5299)** — bumping to any post-WP-SCP-023 SHA produces `startup_failure` because GitHub Actions validates declared permissions on ALL jobs in a called workflow at startup (BEFORE `if:` evaluation) against the caller's ceiling. The `attest-scorecard` job in `policy-check.yml@5ff2acd` declares `attestations: write` + `id-token: write`, which exceeds the wrapper's `contents:read + statuses:write` ceiling, even when `scorecard-emit: false` would skip the job at runtime. Closure path: (a) restructure `policy-check.yml` so `attest-scorecard` lives in a separate top-level workflow file (called workflows can't have job-scoped perms above caller ceiling regardless of `if:`), OR (b) once TF-023E-001 unblocks (repo public/org-owned), grant `attestations: write` + `id-token: write` universally at the wrapper level. (a) preserves least-privilege for opt-out adopters and is the recommended path. Surfaced at 023E fix-round-3 (the bumped wrapper failed startup_failure even after reverting `scorecard-emit: true` because the SHA bump alone trips the validation). Real adopters that opt in MUST follow the (b) path because they will universally grant the two permissions per ADOPT-001 §12.7.15 step 2.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
