{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rg -n \"D-047|024B-extras|restore|break-glass|no-gate-2-verification|workflow wiring\" docs/DECISIONS.md'","aggregated_output":"3:**Last Updated:** 2026-05-10 (D-047 filed for WP-SCP-024 024B-extras; restore/break-glass/workflow wiring)\n33:> 024B-core; the deferred 024B-extras surface carries the `--restore`\n34:> rollback mode and workflow wiring. D-045 is reserved for slice 024C (estate\n79:| D-031 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020K on the SCP repository in the personal-account / single-operator mode resolved at §14 U-k closure: (a) NO `scp-break-glass` GitHub team is created — GitHub teams are not available on user namespaces and `jrnb2024` is a personal user account; (b) `CODEOWNERS` extends to cover the additional governance-sensitive paths named in §4 020K (canonical-minimum), then broadened/extended via 020K R1+R2+R3 safety reviews to close 7 MAJ + 4 MIN + 6 nit findings — see CODEOWNERS file header + `FIX-ROUND-{1,2,3}.md` for the full audit trail of which paths were broadened (subsuming a narrower canonical rule) vs added net-new; (c) at slice 020D2, branch-protection on `main` is configured with `required_approving_review_count = 1`, `dismiss_stale_reviews: true`, and `require_review_from_non_author = false` (solo operator; self-approval is the only option) — **NOTE (D-033 amendment, 2026-04-30 evening):** the anticipated `required_approving_review_count = 1` was corrected to `count = 0` by D-033 when the first PR through enforced mode revealed that GitHub forbids PR self-review; count=1 + sole CODEOWNER = operator locked out of repo. See D-033 for the live state, the operational test path (USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64), and the second-maintainer escalation path; (d) §8 bus-factor-1 risk row remains LIVE with quarterly escalation review at 2026-07-21 named in `STATUS.md` \"Open scheduled follow-ups\" and in auto-memory `project_scheduled_followups.md`. **Escalation path when a second maintainer onboards:** add them to `CODEOWNERS`, flip `require_review_from_non_author = true`, amend §8 risk row to CLOSED. **020D1 → 020D2 dependency:** 020K completes before 020D2 opens (the branch-protection wiring at 020D2 reads from CODEOWNERS established here). Identified at WP-SCP-020 plan §3 sequence + §4 020K + §14 U-k closure | ACCEPTED | Personal-account path is the only viable shape for v1.0.0 on a personal user namespace. The CODEOWNERS expansion forces every future change to `renovate/**` (Renovate preset that cascades pin-bumps across adopters), `docs/DECISIONS.md` (the decision-record canonical home), and `output/findings/waivers.json` (the safety-valve store) through reviewer attention rather than allowing direct push. Bus-factor-1 is acknowledged as live operational exposure rather than papered over: `require_review_from_non_author = false` reflects reality (a solo operator cannot self-approve under non-author review), and the 2026-07-21 quarterly review is the named re-evaluation moment. Path (b) extension of `CODEOWNERS` is forward-looking on `renovate/**` (the directory does not yet exist in the working tree; it lands in slice 020F); CODEOWNERS rules on non-existent paths are no-ops, so adding the rule pre-emptively is harmless and removes a future drift risk where 020F could land without simultaneously adding the matching CODEOWNERS row. Full rationale in `docs/plans/WP-SCP-020-policy-federation-primitive.md` §4 020K + §8 (bus factor risk row, line 188) + §14 U-k closure |\n92:| D-044 | 2026-05-09 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-core operational contracts for cascade scaffolding. Components: (1) `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` (`SCP-073-scaffolder` per WP-SCP-020 §11 follow-up + WP-SCP-021 follow-up `SCP-075-scaffolder-compose`) generates adopter-side artefacts mechanically - bootstrap-only (refuses `CI=true` / `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true` per D-035 symmetry); validates `--scp-sha` against SCP main HEAD lineage (warns if not main HEAD; refuses if non-existent); emits a TF-023E-002 warning for post-v1.2.0 SHAs while recommending the v1.0.0 pin; `--scp-sha` 40-char hex regex; `--default-branch` enum {main, master, develop}; `--scorecard-emit` enum; `--output-dir` writability + path-normalised system-path denylist (incl `/private/var/*` macOS canonicalisation); emits `MANIFEST.json` with SHA256 audit; arguments per plan-doc §5.3. Canonical adopter slugs are normalization aids only, not collision-resistant IDs, so cohort repo names must remain unique after canonicalization. (2) `templates/adopter-wrapper.yml.tmpl` is the canonical adopter wrapper shape per ADOPT-001 §12 with Renovate inline-comment marker `# renovate: datasource=github-tags depName=jrnb2024/standards-control-plane` enabling auto-bump per plan-doc invariant 8 Threshold A criterion; substitutions `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`, `{{SCP_SHA}}`, `{{SCORECARD_EMIT}}`; least-privilege workflow-level permissions (`contents:read` + `statuses:write` only). (3) `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` CLI tool implements plan-doc invariant 2 cascade-status CI enforcement: 4 enforcement behaviours (fail-closed default for absent/unrecognised; `onboarded` -> log-entry-modified + target-match; `onboarded-operator-bump` -> log entry + `STATUS.md` `TF-024X-renovate-<slug>` row matching invariant 2 regex literally; `blocked-on-adopter-conflict` -> `DISPATCH-NOTE` `TF-024X-conflict-<adopter>` reference + log file NOT modified) + explicit tooling-slice opt-in gate for `cascade-status: not applicable` (`--allow-not-applicable`; default refusal for direct CLI use). Regex via `python3 re.search()` (PCRE-style); exactly-one-match assertions on both `cascade-status` and `**Target:**` extraction close multi-occurrence injection bypasses; adopter-slug canonicalisation per plan-doc spec. CLI tool only - GitHub Actions workflow wiring (`.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml`) defers to slice 024B-extras alongside `enable-required-check.sh -