ng-tree diff of `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md` as part of prior-entry detection; the new CI workflow `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires the CLI gate into PR checks with `paths-ignore: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**`; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure and explicitly names the `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` escape hatch; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the escape hatch is explicitly auditable, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. | \nSTATUS.md:156:| 2 | NEW `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` added with `paths-ignore: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[AB]*/**` so 024A / 024B tooling slices do not self-trigger the gate. |\nSTATUS.md:310:- **TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001** (open): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence (docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md) — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7; merge-blocking AC for 024B-extras per plan-doc §6 + 024A R1 MAJ-SAFE-003; closes when operator runs forward-mode + --restore round-trip on throw-away test repo + commits byte-for-byte match evidence.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1227:--expected-wrapper-sha <release-tag-sha-from-Gate-2>\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1230:When prior restore evidence exists, the helper requires `--expected-wrapper-sha` and validates that the SHA resolves to an actual release tag in the SCP repo. If the flag is omitted in that state, re-enable is rejected with exit 2.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1232:> **WARNING.** `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` is an emergency-only bypass for Gate 2. It re-arms the gate against the current wrapper SHA, so if the wrapper is still pinned to a defective SCP SHA the gate will block adopters again.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
