nal closure of the spec gap; neither weakens the security posture. The 4-layer protection (signed commits + required check + no admin bypass + tag protection) remains intact. The review-count=0 acceptance is the explicit bus-factor-1 cost; review enforcement returns the moment a second maintainer joins. Identified by USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64's failed merge attempt 2026-04-30 |\n| D-034 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020F renovate-tag-protection (parallel ruleset to D-030's `v*` ruleset, targeting `refs/tags/renovate/v*`). Closes 020F R1 safety review CRIT-SAFE-001: `renovate/v*` tag series unprotected — an attacker with push access could silently re-point `renovate/v1.0.0` to a malicious commit and cascade adversarial Renovate config to every estate adopter on their next scheduled run. The 020J ruleset matches `refs/tags/v*` (literal v-prefix at start) only. New ruleset `scp-tag-protection-renovate-v` applies same protections (deletion / non_fast_forward / update blocked, `enforcement: active`, `bypass_actors: []`). Configured via `scripts/configure-020f-renovate-tag-protection.sh` (idempotent, jq-based JSON construction to eliminate heredoc-interpolation injection surface, multi-property post-creation verification). Documented in `docs/security/branch-protection.md` \"Tag protection — renovate/v* pattern\" section. Symmetric with D-030 in posture and rationale; the only material difference is the tag-pattern segment. The `renovate/v*` series carries equal supply-chain weight as `v*` because every adopter that extends the preset cascades changes from the renovate-pattern tag to their own gate config | ACCEPTED | The 020J ruleset's `v*` literal-prefix pattern is by-design narrow; broadening to all release-track tags would require a separate ruleset per pattern. Renovate's preset shorthand `github>jrnb2024/standards-control-plane//renovate/default#renovate/v1.0.0` is the standard Renovate adopter onboarding shape; without ruleset protection, the entire preset